{"parentUuid":"844916cd-fe3b-43f2-bdaa-67009d4d4741","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4Lotk4JQQVpa2ZQCnhh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`main` CI is red, and I caused it by merging several PRs back-to-back without waiting for `main`'s CI between them. #516 now verifies evidence on load. #518's test edits a baseline manifest and expects the identity check to catch it, but integrity rejection now fires first. Each was green alone, so neither PR's own CI showed it. The failing runs are on the #517 and #518 merge commits, and the run on the current head (`dead38b6`, which includes #522) is still in progress.\n\nThe fix is PR #525, test-only. It asserts the integrity rejection for the un-re-recorded edit. Then, after an operator re-record, it asserts the identity mismatch. That test file passes 13/13 locally. I added the lesson to `tasks/lessons.md`: wait for `main`'s CI between merges that touch the same subsystem.\n\nWhere the release stands:\n- **Release run failure:** the failed v1.2.0 release run has nothing to do with this. It stopped at the \"tag must be an ancestor of main\" guard.\n- **#524:** it is based on rc.1 code, not current `main`, so its CI doesn't include the broken test.\n- **Order of work:** merge #525, then #524 (merge commit), re-run the failed release job, and bring #523, #519 and #514 up to date with `main`.\n- **Monitor:** I'm watching #525, #524, #523, #519 and #514.\n\nNothing is published, and I'll ask you before publishing the draft."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":684,"cache_read_input_tokens":255969,"output_tokens":481,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":684,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"