{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"9d5521742ecfd29786665f9300326af485eadac6bb8a12f14d9f9d86cceaaf11","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWSgNwHe46usrfk49KNsdW","type":"tool_result","content":"> **Status:** the latest stable release is [v1.1.4](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases). v1.2.0 is in release qualification (candidate `v1.2.0-rc.1`) and is not yet released. Development plans and this README do not establish release readiness; see [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases) and [`docs/releases/`](docs/releases/).\n> To pin a release or install a prerelease, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to a tag from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases):\n> ```sh\n> curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.1.4 sh\n> ```\n/usr/bin/grep: docs/quickstart.md: No such file or directory\n## [v1.2.0] - Unreleased\n\nRelease notes: [`docs/releases/v1.2.0.md`](docs/releases/v1.2.0.md). Candidate: [`rc.1`](docs/releases/v1.2.0-rc.1.md). Plan: [`docs/v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md`](docs/v1.2.0/SEMANT\n\n### Changed\n2. Updates the README status line (\"the latest stable release is ...\") and the README and `quickstart.md` install pins to that tag, and removes any \"in development\" wording for it.\n3. Replaces `Unreleased` in the CHANGELOG heading of the new version with the tag date.\n\n`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` (run in CI) fails when any of these disagree with `LATEST`, so the follow-up PR is the one that turns it green again. The stable-promotion commit itself passes because `LATEST` still\n\nv1.2.0 needs this follow-up: `LATEST` is `v1.1.4` and the CHANGELOG heading `[v1.2.0]` says `Unreleased` until it is done.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]}}
