{"parentUuid":"3064ee88-0ae7-44ea-b4ae-dfc5289a2607","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4m73GJLURVHiHxJ5E3A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"One fix before I commit: I left a host-specific nvm path in the Node 22/24 line, which is noise for other readers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2595,"cache_read_input_tokens":353592,"output_tokens":1643,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":492},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2595,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1643,"cache_read_input_tokens":353592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2595},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4m731RWKSNAiCjMQqQM","requestRef":"940f196f-3d21-484e-b190-40c68b121fd5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents","attributionPlugin":"mattpocock-skills","type":"assistant","uuid":"bebdd7b1-978c-442f-a7be-e8d51610eefb","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:04:34.009Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"bebdd7b1-978c-442f-a7be-e8d51610eefb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4m73GJLURVHiHxJ5E3A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016X8Au5qXXc9qDu3UC1VXHm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/agents-md && sed -i 's| (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/`)||' AGENTS.md && grep -n \"nvm\" AGENTS.md | head -2; wc -c AGENTS.md; git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(agents): rewrite AGENTS.md around what an agent cannot look up\n\nReal build and test commands (including the one-file test command and the mandatory throwaway HOME), a completion criterion, the CI and merge rules learned in v1.2.0 (required checks, merge-commit merges, stale PR merge refs, stable promotion order), and the evidence-honesty rule. Drops the stale v1.0.0 framing and the commands that do not exist (npm run lint). XERJ section tightened without changing its rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/agents-md-optimize 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --title \"docs(agents): rewrite AGENTS.md around what an agent cannot look up\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\n\\`AGENTS.md\\` listed three alternative commands per step (one, \\`npm run lint\\`, does not exist), carried v1.0.0 framing that no longer matches the work, restated \\`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\\` in a summary, and said nothing about the CI, merge and release rules that cost time in v1.2.0. This rewrite keeps what an agent cannot find by looking and points to the rest:\n\n- Real commands, the one-file test command and the mandatory throwaway \\`HOME\\`, and a checkable completion criterion (replaces \\\"always run tests\\\").\n- CI and merge rules from v1.2.0: required checks, merge-commit merges with \\`--match-head-commit\\`, one merge at a time per subsystem, stale PR merge refs, the stable-promotion order (land on main, then tag) and immutable tags, Node 22 and 24 for test-runner changes.\n- The evidence-honesty rule (\\\"ledger closed, qualification pending\\\").\n- XERJ section kept with the same rules, tightened; prohibitions that had a positive form are stated positively.\n- Removed: no-op conventions (\\\"keep functions modular\\\"), the alternative commands, the v1.0.0 slice framing.\n\n## Validation\n\nDocs only. Every command and path in the file was checked against \\`Makefile\\`, \\`cli/package.json\\`, \\`.github/\\` and the ruleset on main; no test or script reads the repository \\`AGENTS.md\\`. The local checkout's uncommitted \\\"Agent skills\\\" block and untracked \\`docs/agents/\\` are not included (they are not on main).\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1","description":"Commit AGENTS.md rewrite and open PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2595,"cache_read_input_tokens":353592,"output_tokens":1643,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":492},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2595,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1643,"cache_read_input_tokens":353592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2595},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7226,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016X8Au5qXXc9qDu3UC1VXHm":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/agents-md && sed -i 's| (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/`)||' AGENTS.md && grep -n \"nvm\" AGENTS.md | head -2; wc -c AGENTS.md; git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(agents): rewrite AGENTS.md around what an agent cannot look up\n\nReal build and test commands (including the one-file test command and the mandatory throwaway HOME), a completion criterion, the CI and merge rules learned in v1.2.0 (required checks, merge-commit merges, stale PR merge refs, stable promotion order), and the evidence-honesty rule. Drops the stale v1.0.0 framing and the commands that do not exist (npm run lint). XERJ section tightened without changing its rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/agents-md-optimize 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --title \"docs(agents): rewrite AGENTS.md around what an agent cannot look up\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\n\\`AGENTS.md\\` listed three alternative commands per step (one, \\`npm run lint\\`, does not exist), carried v1.0.0 framing that no longer matches the work, restated \\`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\\` in a summary, and said nothing about the CI, merge and release rules that cost time in v1.2.0. This rewrite keeps what an agent cannot find by looking and points to the rest:\n\n- Real commands, the one-file test command and the mandatory throwaway \\`HOME\\`, and a checkable completion criterion (replaces \\\"always run tests\\\").\n- CI and merge rules from v1.2.0: required checks, merge-commit merges with \\`--match-head-commit\\`, one merge at a time per subsystem, stale PR merge refs, the stable-promotion order (land on main, then tag) and immutable tags, Node 22 and 24 for test-runner changes.\n- The evidence-honesty rule (\\\"ledger closed, qualification pending\\\").\n- XERJ section kept with the same rules, tightened; prohibitions that had a positive form are stated positively.\n- Removed: no-op conventions (\\\"keep functions modular\\\"), the alternative commands, the v1.0.0 slice framing.\n\n## Validation\n\nDocs only. Every command and path in the file was checked against \\`Makefile\\`, \\`cli/package.json\\`, \\`.github/\\` and the ruleset on main; no test or script reads the repository \\`AGENTS.md\\`. The local checkout's uncommitted \\\"Agent skills\\\" block and untracked \\`docs/agents/\\` are not included (they are not on main).\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1","description":"Commit AGENTS.md rewrite and open PR"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch4m731RWKSNAiCjMQqQM","requestRef":"940f196f-3d21-484e-b190-40c68b121fd5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents","attributionPlugin":"mattpocock-skills","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fc6316b-faa4-4e1b-a4d0-0af189f4112c","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:04:41.246Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
