{"parentUuid":"be05115a-0c8f-436f-8d4e-f4dc45134496","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01UCoTfWm3uHjK2F7eQnKLkc","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"B=~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15 && mkdir -p $B && cp -p ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md $B/CLAUDE.md && cp -p ~/.claude/RTK.md $B/RTK.md && cp -p /home/mike/CLAUDE.md $B/home-CLAUDE.md && rtk ls -la $B | tail -3; echo; rtk read /home/mike/CLAUDE.md | sed -n 1,200p | awk 'length>0' | cut -c1-160 | head -70\",\"description\":\"Back up the three instruction files and re-read the home project file\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":119},"type":"attachment","uuid":"09f3f8d2-9474-43dd-b782-8f4788551f3f","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:30.858Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"09f3f8d2-9474-43dd-b782-8f4788551f3f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01UCoTfWm3uHjK2F7eQnKLkc","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":456},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6fedbdee-cc93-45dd-93ee-a231819acf0c","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:31.197Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"be05115a-0c8f-436f-8d4e-f4dc45134496","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2bee6e4d-c97d-42ab-9177-36b9ff9547bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCoTfWm3uHjK2F7eQnKLkc","type":"tool_result","content":"664  CLAUDE.md  2.5K\n600  RTK.md  964B\n664  home-CLAUDE.md  4.1K\n\n## Principles\n1. Don't assume. Don't hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.\n2. Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.\n3. Touch only what you must. Clean up only your mess.\n4. Define success criteria. Loop until verified.\n## Agent Workflow\nThis workspace uses specialized AI agents in `~/.claude/agents/`. For any feature, bug fix, or significant change, **delegate to `@orchestrator`** — it manage\n### How it works\n`@orchestrator` runs the pipeline internally:\n1. `@architect` → plans the implementation, identifies affected files\n2. `@coder` → writes code (linter only, no tests)\n3. `@tester` → writes/runs tests (loops with coder if failures)\n4. `@reviewer` → reviews the final diff (security, performance, readability, consistency)\n5. `@design-qa` → screenshots affected pages at mobile/tablet/desktop (UI changes only)\nAll verbose agent output stays inside the orchestrator's context. You get back a structured summary with: changes made, test results, review findings, and any i\n### Direct agent access\n| Agent | Purpose | Invoke |\n|-------|---------|--------|\n| **orchestrator** | Full workflow — plan, code, test, review, QA | `@orchestrator` |\n| **architect** | Plan only — scope, trade-offs, risks | `@architect` |\n| **coder** | Implement only — code + lint | `@coder` |\n| **tester** | Test only — write/run affected tests | `@tester` |\n| **reviewer** | Review only — check diff for issues | `@reviewer` |\n| **design-qa** | Visual QA — screenshot aisyndicate at 3 viewports | `@design-qa` |\n| **security-auditor** | Deep security audit — auth, injection, data exposure | `@security-auditor` |\n| **migration-planner** | Plan DB migrations safely (alembic, sqlite3) | `@migration-planner` |\n| **api-designer** | Review REST/gRPC API design | `@api-designer` |\n| **ci-validator** | Validate GitLab CI pipeline configs | `@ci-validator` |\n### When NOT to delegate\n- Quick questions about the codebase (just answer directly)\n- Reading/explaining code (just read and explain)\n- Git operations, deployments, or config changes (handle directly)\n### Verify script\nRun `./scripts/verify.sh` to run only affected tests across all sub-projects (Go, Playwright, pytest). Used by the tester agent internally.\n## gstack\nUse the `/browse` skill from gstack for all web browsing. **Never use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools.**\nAvailable gstack skills: `/office-hours`, `/plan-ceo-review`, `/plan-eng-review`, `/plan-design-review`, `/design-consultation`, `/design-shotgun`, `/design-htm\n### Sub-projects\n| Project | Language | Location |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| SyndicateCode | Go 1.25, bubbletea TUI, gRPC, sqlite3 | `./SyndicateCode/` |\n| aisyndicate | Next.js 16, React, TypeScript, Radix UI | `./aisyndicate/` |\n| syndicateclaw | Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, alembic | `./syndicateclaw/` |\n| controlplane-enterprise | Go, enterprise control plane | `./controlplane-enterprise/` |\n| syndicategate | Go, backend service | `./syndicategate/` |\n## graphify\nThis project has a knowledge graph at graphify-out/ with god nodes, community structure, and cross-file relationships.\nRules:\n- For codebase questions, first run `graphify query \"<question>\"` when graphify-out/graph.json exists. Use `graphify path \"<A>\" \"<B>\"` for relationships and `gr\n- If graphify-out/wiki/index.md exists, use it for broad navigation instead of raw source browsing.\n- Read graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture review or when query/path/explain do not surface enough context.\n- After modifying code, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost).","is_error":false}]},