alidator** | Validate GitLab CI pipeline configs | `@ci-validator` |\n### When NOT to delegate\n- Quick questions about the codebase (just answer directly)\n- Reading/explaining code (just read and explain)\n- Git operations, deployments, or config changes (handle directly)\n### Verify script\nRun `./scripts/verify.sh` to run only affected tests across all sub-projects (Go, Playwright, pytest). Used by the tester agent internally.\n## gstack\nUse the `/browse` skill from gstack for all web browsing. **Never use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools.**\nAvailable gstack skills: `/office-hours`, `/plan-ceo-review`, `/plan-eng-review`, `/plan-design-review`, `/design-consultation`, `/design-shotgun`, `/design-htm\n### Sub-projects\n| Project | Language | Location |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| SyndicateCode | Go 1.25, bubbletea TUI, gRPC, sqlite3 | `./SyndicateCode/` |\n| aisyndicate | Next.js 16, React, TypeScript, Radix UI | `./aisyndicate/` |\n| syndicateclaw | Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, alembic | `./syndicateclaw/` |\n| controlplane-enterprise | Go, enterprise control plane | `./controlplane-enterprise/` |\n| syndicategate | Go, backend service | `./syndicategate/` |\n## graphify\nThis project has a knowledge graph at graphify-out/ with god nodes, community structure, and cross-file relationships.\nRules:\n- For codebase questions, first run `graphify query \"<question>\"` when graphify-out/graph.json exists. Use `graphify path \"<A>\" \"<B>\"` for relationships and `gr\n- If graphify-out/wiki/index.md exists, use it for broad navigation instead of raw source browsing.\n- Read graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture review or when query/path/explain do not surface enough context.\n- After modifying code, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"be05115a-0c8f-436f-8d4e-f4dc45134496","per