{"parentUuid":"255d9230-d9c0-4d94-9f1e-0da0907a3e16","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4mBernu4tFTfTXCoodQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3841,"cache_read_input_tokens":358009,"output_tokens":1228,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":236},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":358009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1896,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4mBeavTGKt5zpxoSSG8","requestRef":"02162567-df80-4936-8d55-4fa56d8c4e74","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents","attributionPlugin":"mattpocock-skills","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c16043e-d8db-4dcd-ac9d-b1363bc659a4","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:34.662Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"4c16043e-d8db-4dcd-ac9d-b1363bc659a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4mBernu4tFTfTXCoodQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018gLjW96hfbdbAAKKxrViMT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md <<'EOF'\n## Workflow\n\n### Plan\n- Plan any non-trivial task (3+ steps or an architectural decision) before building: write the plan to `tasks/todo.md` as checkable items and check in before implementing. Plan the verification steps too.\n- When something goes sideways, stop and re-plan at once.\n- Tick items off as you go, give a high-level summary of each change, and end with a review section in `tasks/todo.md`.\n\n### Subagents\n- Keep the main context clean: offload research, exploration and parallel analysis to subagents, one tack per subagent. Throw more subagents at a complex problem.\n\n### Lessons\n- After any user correction, add the pattern to `tasks/lessons.md` as a rule that prevents the same mistake, and iterate until the mistake rate drops. Review the file at session start.\n\n### Done means proven\n- A task is complete when evidence shows it works: tests run, logs checked, behaviour diffed against main where relevant. Ask: would a staff engineer approve this?\n\n### Elegance\n- For a non-trivial change, pause and look for a more elegant way; when a fix feels hacky, implement the elegant solution with everything you now know. Keep simple, obvious fixes simple. Challenge your own work before presenting it.\n\n### Bug reports\n- Fix them from the evidence: logs, errors, failing tests, CI failures included. Resolve without being walked through it.\n\n## Principles\n- **Simplicity first**: the smallest change that works, touching only what is necessary.\n- **Root cause**: no temporary fixes; senior-developer standard.\n\n@RTK.md\n\n# graphify\n`/graphify` → invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` (`~/.claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md`) before anything else.\nEOF\ncat > ~/.claude/RTK.md <<'EOF'\n# RTK (Rust Token Killer)\n\nA hook rewrites shell commands through `rtk` (60-90% fewer tokens): write ordinary commands (`git status` runs as `rtk git status`).\n\n- Raw output: `rtk proxy <cmd>`. Use it to debug, and whenever a rewritten `grep`, `awk` or `sed` pipeline returns filtered or odd output; rerun it raw before trusting it.\n- Savings: `rtk gain`, `rtk gain --history`. Missed opportunities: `rtk discover`.\n- If `rtk gain` fails, a different `rtk` is installed (reachingforthejack/rtk, Rust Type Kit); check `which rtk`.\nEOF\nwc -c ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md ~/.claude/RTK.md","description":"Write optimized global CLAUDE.md and RTK.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3841,"cache_read_input_tokens":358009,"output_tokens":1228,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":236},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":358009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":5120,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018gLjW96hfbdbAAKKxrViMT":{"command":"cat > ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md <<'EOF'\n## Workflow\n\n### Plan\n- Plan any non-trivial task (3+ steps or an architectural decision) before building: write the plan to `tasks/todo.md` as checkable items and check in before implementing. Plan the verification steps too.\n- When something goes sideways, stop and re-plan at once.\n- Tick items off as you go, give a high-level summary of each change, and end with a review section in `tasks/todo.md`.\n\n### Subagents\n- Keep the main context clean: offload research, exploration and parallel analysis to subagents, one tack per subagent. Throw more subagents at a complex problem.\n\n### Lessons\n- After any user correction, add the pattern to `tasks/lessons.md` as a rule that prevents the same mistake, and iterate until the mistake rate drops. Review the file at session start.\n\n### Done means proven\n- A task is complete when evidence shows it works: tests run, logs checked, behaviour diffed against main where relevant. Ask: would a staff engineer approve this?\n\n### Elegance\n- For a non-trivial change, pause and look for a more elegant way; when a fix feels hacky, implement the elegant solution with everything you now know. Keep simple, obvious fixes simple. Challenge your own work before presenting it.\n\n### Bug reports\n- Fix them from the evidence: logs, errors, failing tests, CI failures included. Resolve without being walked through it.\n\n## Principles\n- **Simplicity first**: the smallest change that works, touching only what is necessary.\n- **Root cause**: no temporary fixes; senior-developer standard.\n\n@RTK.md\n\n# graphify\n`/graphify` → invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` (`~/.claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md`) before anything else.\nEOF\ncat > ~/.claude/RTK.md <<'EOF'\n# RTK (Rust Token Killer)\n\nA hook rewrites shell commands through `rtk` (60-90% fewer tokens): write ordinary commands (`git status` runs as `rtk git status`).\n\n- Raw output: `rtk proxy <cmd>`. Use it to debug, and whenever a rewritten `grep`, `awk` or `sed` pipeline returns filtered or odd output; rerun it raw before trusting it.\n- Savings: `rtk gain`, `rtk gain --history`. Missed opportunities: `rtk discover`.\n- If `rtk gain` fails, a different `rtk` is installed (reachingforthejack/rtk, Rust Type Kit); check `which rtk`.\nEOF\nwc -c ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md ~/.claude/RTK.md","description":"Write optimized global CLAUDE.md and RTK.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4mBeavTGKt5zpxoSSG8","requestRef":"02162567-df80-4936-8d55-4fa56d8c4e74","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents","attributionPlugin":"mattpocock-skills","type":"assistant","uuid":"478be5b6-9128-44e6-83eb-b3002249fcb7","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:39.814Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
