{"parentUuid":"9829f852-cb31-4703-9335-41c12166d9cb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2bee6e4d-c97d-42ab-9177-36b9ff9547bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YFZqX7ws3UnznMU2r68GJC","type":"tool_result","content":"10: This workspace uses specialized AI agents in `~/.claude/agents/`. For any feature, bug fix, or significant change, **delegate to `@orchestrator`** — it manages the full workflow and returns a concise summary.\n21: All verbose agent output stays inside the orchestrator's context. You get back a structured summary with: changes made, test results, review findings, and any issues.\n52: Available gstack skills: `/office-hours`, `/plan-ceo-review`, `/plan-eng-review`, `/plan-design-review`, `/design-consultation`, `/design-shotgun`, `/design-html`, `/review`, `/ship`, `/land-and-deploy`, `/canary`, `/benchmark`, `/browse`, `/connect-chrome`, `/qa`, `/qa-only`, `/design-review`, `/setup-browser-cookies`, `/setup-deploy`, `/retro`, `/investigate`, `/document-release`, `/codex`, `/cso`, `/autoplan`, `/plan-devex-review`, `/devex-review`, `/careful`, `/freeze`, `/guard`, `/unfreeze`, `/gstack-upgrade`, `/learn`\n69: - For codebase questions, first run `graphify query \"<question>\"` when graphify-out/graph.json exists. Use `graphify path \"<A>\" \"<B>\"` for relationships and `graphify explain \"<concept>\"` for focused concepts. These return a scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md or raw grep output.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"53a8d780-c7d7-4900-8472-571b01fde679","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:44.407Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"10: This workspace uses specialized AI agents in `~/.claude/agents/`. For any feature, bug fix, or significant change, **delegate to `@orchestrator`** — it manages the full workflow and returns a concise summary.\n21: All verbose agent output stays inside the orchestrator's context. You get back a structured summary with: changes made, test results, review findings, and any issues.\n52: Available gstack skills: `/office-hours`, `/plan-ceo-review`, `/plan-eng-review`, `/plan-design-review`, `/design-consultation`, `/design-shotgun`, `/design-html`, `/review`, `/ship`, `/land-and-deploy`, `/canary`, `/benchmark`, `/browse`, `/connect-chrome`, `/qa`, `/qa-only`, `/design-review`, `/setup-browser-cookies`, `/setup-deploy`, `/retro`, `/investigate`, `/document-release`, `/codex`, `/cso`, `/autoplan`, `/plan-devex-review`, `/devex-review`, `/careful`, `/freeze`, `/guard`, `/unfreeze`, `/gstack-upgrade`, `/learn`\n69: - For codebase questions, first run `graphify query \"<question>\"` when graphify-out/graph.json exists. Use `graphify path \"<A>\" \"<B>\"` for relationships and `graphify explain \"<concept>\"` for focused concepts. These return a scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md or raw grep output.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9829f852-cb31-4703-9335-41c12166d9cb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","id":"e4f355df-188d-4111-bc47-591b10640861","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:44.807Z","version":"2.1.323","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"02245c82d4cb86350db44b7c9960d5f359fa3c3746ce766c103fc6f328b1a703","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"70c62003-16dc-407a-89a4-9e2d8476b2dc","keep":674,"tail":["f67a2e0b5a7dd6d26dfcdc201d9159a4169624fac9541619c3b0a12bcce570e2","962e88c918bdeb44c47ef18265740007d7e7591d36612039d150b5f06a705268"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",675,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"2b22fcc058e06f4100ffa7f10240cb0c603ea9b845260ad4c66b3cf1e58ba515"}
{"parentUuid":"53a8d780-c7d7-4900-8472-571b01fde679","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4mCb4dAe76TTkJ8UeAd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rxc94bR21bk5rBsg6WPiWG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /home/mike/CLAUDE.md <<'EOF'\n## Principles\n\n1. Don't assume. Don't hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.\n2. Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.\n3. Touch only what you must. Clean up only your mess.\n4. Define success criteria. Loop until verified.\n\n## Agent workflow\n\nSpecialised agents live in `~/.claude/agents/` (their descriptions are in the agent list). Delegate any feature, bug fix or significant change to **`@orchestrator`**: it runs the pipeline and returns one structured summary (changes, test results, review findings, issues) while the verbose output stays in its context.\n\nPipeline: `@architect` plans and identifies affected files → `@coder` writes code (linter only, no tests) → `@tester` writes and runs tests, looping with coder on failures → `@reviewer` reviews the final diff (security, performance, readability, consistency) → `@design-qa` screenshots affected pages at mobile, tablet and desktop (UI changes only).\n\nCall a single agent directly for one stage: architect, coder, tester, reviewer, design-qa, security-auditor, migration-planner (alembic, sqlite3), api-designer, ci-validator (GitLab CI).\n\nHandle these yourself, without delegating: codebase questions, reading and explaining code, git operations, deployments, config changes.\n\nAffected tests across all sub-projects (Go, Playwright, pytest): `./scripts/verify.sh` (the tester agent uses it).\n\n## Browsing\n\nUse the gstack `/browse` skill for all web browsing, and keep `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools out of use.\n\n## Sub-projects\n\n| Project | Stack | Location |\n|---------|-------|----------|\n| SyndicateCode | Go 1.25, bubbletea TUI, gRPC, sqlite3 | `./SyndicateCode/` |\n| aisyndicate | Next.js 16, React, TypeScript, Radix UI | `./aisyndicate/` |\n| syndicateclaw | Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, alembic | `./syndicateclaw/` |\n| controlplane-enterprise | Go, enterprise control plane | `./controlplane-enterprise/` |\n| syndicategate | Go, backend service | `./syndicategate/` |\n\n## graphify\n\n`graphify-out/` holds a knowledge graph (god nodes, communities, cross-file relationships).\n\n- For a codebase question, start with `graphify query \"<question>\"` when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists; use `graphify path \"<A>\" \"<B>\"` for relationships and `graphify explain \"<concept>\"` for one concept. Each returns a scoped subgraph, usually far smaller than `GRAPH_REPORT.md` or raw grep.\n- Navigate broadly through `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` when it exists.\n- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for broad architecture review, or when query, path and explain fall short.\n- After modifying code, run `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost).\nEOF\nwc -c /home/mike/CLAUDE.md; diff <(sed 's/[[:space:]]*$//' ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/home-CLAUDE.md | wc -c) <(wc -c < /home/mike/CLAUDE.md) >/dev/null; echo originals: $(wc -c < ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/home-CLAUDE.md) $(wc -c < ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/CLAUDE.md) $(wc -c < ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/RTK.md)","description":"Write optimized home project CLAUDE.md and compare sizes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":788,"cache_read_input_tokens":363244,"output_tokens":1352,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":788,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":363244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":788},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":6885,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Rxc94bR21bk5rBsg6WPiWG":{"command":"cat > /home/mike/CLAUDE.md <<'EOF'\n## Principles\n\n1. Don't assume. Don't hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.\n2. Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.\n3. Touch only what you must. Clean up only your mess.\n4. Define success criteria. Loop until verified.\n\n## Agent workflow\n\nSpecialised agents live in `~/.claude/agents/` (their descriptions are in the agent list). Delegate any feature, bug fix or significant change to **`@orchestrator`**: it runs the pipeline and returns one structured summary (changes, test results, review findings, issues) while the verbose output stays in its context.\n\nPipeline: `@architect` plans and identifies affected files → `@coder` writes code (linter only, no tests) → `@tester` writes and runs tests, looping with coder on failures → `@reviewer` reviews the final diff (security, performance, readability, consistency) → `@design-qa` screenshots affected pages at mobile, tablet and desktop (UI changes only).\n\nCall a single agent directly for one stage: architect, coder, tester, reviewer, design-qa, security-auditor, migration-planner (alembic, sqlite3), api-designer, ci-validator (GitLab CI).\n\nHandle these yourself, without delegating: codebase questions, reading and explaining code, git operations, deployments, config changes.\n\nAffected tests across all sub-projects (Go, Playwright, pytest): `./scripts/verify.sh` (the tester agent uses it).\n\n## Browsing\n\nUse the gstack `/browse` skill for all web browsing, and keep `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools out of use.\n\n## Sub-projects\n\n| Project | Stack | Location |\n|---------|-------|----------|\n| SyndicateCode | Go 1.25, bubbletea TUI, gRPC, sqlite3 | `./SyndicateCode/` |\n| aisyndicate | Next.js 16, React, TypeScript, Radix UI | `./aisyndicate/` |\n| syndicateclaw | Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, alembic | `./syndicateclaw/` |\n| controlplane-enterprise | Go, enterprise control plane | `./controlplane-enterprise/` |\n| syndicategate | Go, backend service | `./syndicategate/` |\n\n## graphify\n\n`graphify-out/` holds a knowledge graph (god nodes, communities, cross-file relationships).\n\n- For a codebase question, start with `graphify query \"<question>\"` when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists; use `graphify path \"<A>\" \"<B>\"` for relationships and `graphify explain \"<concept>\"` for one concept. Each returns a scoped subgraph, usually far smaller than `GRAPH_REPORT.md` or raw grep.\n- Navigate broadly through `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` when it exists.\n- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for broad architecture review, or when query, path and explain fall short.\n- After modifying code, run `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost).\nEOF\nwc -c /home/mike/CLAUDE.md; diff <(sed 's/[[:space:]]*$//' ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/home-CLAUDE.md | wc -c) <(wc -c < /home/mike/CLAUDE.md) >/dev/null; echo originals: $(wc -c < ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/home-CLAUDE.md) $(wc -c < ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/CLAUDE.md) $(wc -c < ~/.claude/backups/2026-11-15/RTK.md)","description":"Write optimized home project CLAUDE.md and compare sizes"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4mCafKMkYZStfQWvJ8n","requestRef":"e4f355df-188d-4111-bc47-591b10640861","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents","attributionPlugin":"mattpocock-skills","type":"assistant","uuid":"6bad2245-2c1d-4880-8cdd-02d43aec7a1e","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:05:52.332Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"64