{"parentUuid":"6ad02a3d-6a30-4ea2-9fa6-0b6fc24b1fdf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4mbvixFZL4rJN3nqKgL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011U7gCpNwbZyypvFYWQ2LN4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/agent-rules-books/main/release-it/release-it.mini.md","prompt":"Describe the structure and style of this rule file: headings, how each rule is phrased (imperative? with rationale? with triggers?), length per rule, and show 6-8 representative rules verbatim. Note any conventions for scoping or applicability."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":368226,"output_tokens":667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":94},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":667,"cache_read_input_tokens":368226,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":1155,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011U7gCpNwbZyypvFYWQ2LN4":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/agent-rules-books/main/release-it/release-it.mini.md","prompt":"Describe the structure and style of this rule file: headings, how each rule is phrased (imperative? with rationale? with triggers?), length per rule, and show 6-8 representative rules verbatim. Note any conventions for scoping or applicability."}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Ch4mbvS67snU5MBEBoTpj","requestRef":"67d2aed9-fdbd-4de0-a02a-09dd2e40448f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"5152aad7-4e87-48ec-acc3-003a47393cc2","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:11:06.292Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"ed055f81-246d-4afb-bcad-a92072ebdd37","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a64db6bd-a503-4549-bc43-76dbb357cf44","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L3YZb4Sz2QLjqGHEV5Ud12","type":"tool_result","content":"**Tiers**\n- **`mini`** is the default for most task work and the best starting point for skills. It's \"the recommended version for most real task use.\"\n- **`nano`** is for very tight budgets, a tiny always-on baseline, or portability across tools with small limits.\n- **`full`** is reference material for audits, deep skills, focused one-off sessions, and deriving smaller rules.\n\n**Always-on vs. on-demand**\n- Start with one primary rule set and use the smallest mechanism that changes decisions: \"Use the smallest mechanism that still changes the agent's decisions.\"\n- Always-on is for stable defaults. Use one carefully chosen `mini`, or `nano` if `mini` is too large.\n- Prefer scoped, on-demand, or retrieval-based loading over global loading.\n- Load task-specific books as skills or on-demand rules, invoked only when the task matches.\n- Use retrieval or MCP for large, dynamic, or rarely needed material.\n\n**Skills**\n- Skills suit workflows like refactoring, legacy changes, reliability work, and domain modeling.\n- A `mini` file is usually the right skill body, with an optional `reference.md` backed by `full`.\n- Keep the active skill concise and move long examples and full rule files into reference files or retrieval.\n\n**Combining books**\n- Keep one primary always-on rule set and move the rest to on-demand mechanisms.\n- Use one shared `mini` baseline where possible, and avoid loading several `full` files globally.\n\n**Context budget**\n- Don't put long procedures in always-on files. Turn them into skills.\n- Use `nano` when `mini` would compete with more important project context.\n- Treat memories as helpers, not the canonical source of shared rules.\n\n**Tool-specific setup**\n- **Codex:** Use skills for workflows, a root `AGENTS.md` for the base layer, and nested overrides only where a subtree needs different pressure.\n- **Claude Code:** Keep root `CLAUDE.md` short and import a shared `AGENTS.md` with `@AGENTS.md`. Use `.claude/rules/` or path-scoped skills for subsystem guidance. Set `disable-model-invocation: true` for side-effectful flows like deploys.\n- **Cursor:** Prefer `.cursor/rules` over `AGENTS.md`. Use at most one short `Always` rule, and scope the rest as `Auto Attached`, `Agent Requested`, or `Manual`.\n\n**Pitfalls to avoid**\n- A giant `Always` rule, or a long `full` file pasted into `CLAUDE.md`\n- Long procedures in `AGENTS.md`\n- Relying on auto memory or memories for shared rules"}]},"uuid":"94ff637f-f1cb-474e-9d93-6f31067d064a","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:11:11.903Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":12517,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Tiers**\n- **`mini`** is the default for most task work and the best starting point for skills. It's \"the recommended version for most real task use.\"\n- **`nano`** is for very tight budgets, a tiny always-on baseline, or portability across tools with small limits.\n- **`full`** is reference material for audits, deep skills, focused one-off sessions, and deriving smaller rules.\n\n**Always-on vs. on-demand**\n- Start with one primary rule set and use the smallest mechanism that changes decisions: \"Use the smallest mechanism that still changes the agent's decisions.\"\n- Always-on is for stable defaults. Use one carefully chosen `mini`, or `nano` if `mini` is too large.\n- Prefer scoped, on-demand, or retrieval-based loading over global loading.\n- Load task-specific books as skills or on-demand rules, invoked only when the task matches.\n- Use retrieval or MCP for large, dynamic, or rarely needed material.\n\n**Skills**\n- Skills suit workflows like refactoring, legacy changes, reliability work, and domain modeling.\n- A `mini` file is usually the right skill body, with an optional `reference.md` backed by `full`.\n- Keep the active skill concise and move long examples and full rule files into reference files or retrieval.\n\n**Combining books**\n- Keep one primary always-on rule set and move the rest to on-demand mechanisms.\n- Use one shared `mini` baseline where possible, and avoid loading several `full` files globally.\n\n**Context budget**\n- Don't put long procedures in always-on files. Turn them into skills.\n- Use `nano` when `mini` would compete with more important project context.\n- Treat memories as helpers, not the canonical source of shared rules.\n\n**Tool-specific setup**\n- **Codex:** Use skills for workflows, a root `AGENTS.md` for the base layer, and nested overrides only where a subtree needs different pressure.\n- **Claude Code:** Keep root `CLAUDE.md` short and import a shared `AGENTS.md` with `@AGENTS.md`. Use `.claude/rules/` or path-scoped skills for subsystem guidance. Set `disable-model-invocation: true` for side-effectful flows like deploys.\n- **Cursor:** Prefer `.cursor/rules` over `AGENTS.md`. Use at most one short `Always` rule, and scope the rest as `Auto Attached`, `Agent Requested`, or `Manual`.\n\n**Pitfalls to avoid**\n- A giant `Always` rule, or a long `full` file pasted into `CLAUDE.md`\n- Long procedures in `AGENTS.md`\n- Relying on auto memory or memories for shared rules","durationMs":7697,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/agent-rules-books/main/docs/USAGE.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed055f81-246d-4afb-bcad-a92072ebdd37","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
