{"parentUuid":"4b235ec6-0f23-4ccc-8578-c4a192e32f38","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4mt2WeWgeVmqoGgkYf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Nexus already loads the first of AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md, so adding a CLAUDE.md is safe. I also found that it reads files raw and doesn't follow the `@` import convention, which I'm now fixing.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":379250,"output_tokens":2406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":836},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2406,"cache_read_input_tokens":379250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4mt2EHaDPB6dkaWj7uA","requestRef":"d75d654f-b457-4881-9d76-1ab150f3d1dc","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9aa6cff2-f272-4560-8c9f-5ed304ef2dd8","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:14:47.980Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"9aa6cff2-f272-4560-8c9f-5ed304ef2dd8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4mt2WeWgeVmqoGgkYf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ks3xsgGgMawhhMooRsHHZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/agents-md && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open(\"AGENTS.md\").read()\nstart=s.index(\"## Reference coding with XERJ (required)\")\nend=s.index(\"## Concurrency, claims and release authority\")\nxerj=s[start:end]\n# on-demand doc: everything except the heading, with a header\nbody=xerj.split(\"\\n\",1)[1].strip()\ndoc=\"# Reference coding with XERJ\\n\\nThe detail behind the \\\"Reference coding\\\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\\n\\n\"+body+\"\\n\"\nopen(\"docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md\",\"w\").write(doc)\nnew_section='''## Reference coding with XERJ (required)\n- Before writing non-trivial code that has a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), read what mature projects do: query the local XERJ node, then record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- Node, commands, corpora, licence and privacy rules, the field report, and the fallback when XERJ is unavailable (\"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" plus `git grep`): `docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md`. Read it when you start that first query.\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+new_section+s[end:]\n# Entire CLI line back under build and test\nentire=\"- Entire CLI: export `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` before any `entire` command. The Entire gate no longer counts toward merging.\\n\"\nassert entire in doc\ndoc=doc.replace(entire,\"\")\nopen(\"docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md\",\"w\").write(doc)\ns=s.replace(\"- Preserve existing comments and unrelated changes.\\n\",\"- Preserve existing comments and unrelated changes.\\n\"+entire,1)\n# merging/release as triggers + final checklist\nm0=s.index(\"## Merging and releasing\")\nnew_merge='''## Merging and releasing\nBias to correct: a green PR is not a green `main`, and a pushed tag cannot be taken back.\n- When merging: required checks are `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, `linux-x86_64`; read each check's conclusion (empty or in-progress is not success). Merge with a merge commit, `gh pr merge <n> --merge --match-head-commit <full-sha>`. PRs that touch one subsystem merge one at a time, each followed by the CI run on `main`: two PRs green alone can break `main` together.\n- When a PR's checks look wrong after `main` moved: PR checks run on GitHub's merge commit, so confirm the run checked out the current `merge_commit_sha` (`gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n> --jq .merge_commit_sha`); a stale one tests old content.\n- When cutting a stable release: make a version-only commit directly on the accepted RC (`node scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs <rc-ref> <stable-ref>`), land it on `main` through a merge-commit PR, and only then tag, because `release.yml` requires the tagged commit to be an ancestor of `main`. Version tags are immutable: re-run a failed run, or move to the next RC or patch. Then follow `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`.\n- When reporting a gate or a result: state it as measured (\"ledger closed, qualification pending\"), record failed runs unaltered, and make no frontier-grade claim without external qualification.\n- Before tagging or merging, check: required checks green at the exact head? CI on `main` green after the previous merge? Tagged commit an ancestor of `main`? Claims match the evidence?\n'''\ns=s[:m0]+new_merge\nopen(\"AGENTS.md\",\"w\").write(s)\nopen(\"CLAUDE.md\",\"w\").write(\"@AGENTS.md\\n\")\nEOF\nwc -c AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md; head -3 docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md | cut -c1-150; grep -n \"^## \" AGENTS.md","description":"Split XERJ into an on-demand doc, add CLAUDE.md, restructure merge rules as triggers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":379250,"output_tokens":2406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":836},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2406,"cache_read_input_tokens":379250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7623,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018ks3xsgGgMawhhMooRsHHZ":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/agents-md && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open(\"AGENTS.md\").read()\nstart=s.index(\"## Reference coding with XERJ (required)\")\nend=s.index(\"## Concurrency, claims and release authority\")\nxerj=s[start:end]\n# on-demand doc: everything except the heading, with a header\nbody=xerj.split(\"\\n\",1)[1].strip()\ndoc=\"# Reference coding with XERJ\\n\\nThe detail behind the \\\"Reference coding\\\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\\n\\n\"+body+\"\\n\"\nopen(\"docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md\",\"w\").write(doc)\nnew_section='''## Reference coding with XERJ (required)\n- Before writing non-trivial code that has a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), read what mature projects do: query the local XERJ node, then record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- Node, commands, corpora, licence and privacy rules, the field report, and the fallback when XERJ is unavailable (\"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" plus `git grep`): `docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md`. Read it when you start that first query.\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+new_section+s[end:]\n# Entire CLI line back under build and test\nentire=\"- Entire CLI: export `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` before any `entire` command. The Entire gate no longer counts toward merging.\\n\"\nassert entire in doc\ndoc=doc.replace(entire,\"\")\nopen(\"docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md\",\"w\").write(doc)\ns=s.replace(\"- Preserve existing comments and unrelated changes.\\n\",\"- Preserve existing comments and unrelated changes.\\n\"+entire,1)\n# merging/release as triggers + final checklist\nm0=s.index(\"## Merging and releasing\")\nnew_merge='''## Merging and releasing\nBias to correct: a green PR is not a green `main`, and a pushed tag cannot be taken back.\n- When merging: required checks are `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, `linux-x86_64`; read each check's conclusion (empty or in-progress is not success). Merge with a merge commit, `gh pr merge <n> --merge --match-head-commit <full-sha>`. PRs that touch one subsystem merge one at a time, each followed by the CI run on `main`: two PRs green alone can break `main` together.\n- When a PR's checks look wrong after `main` moved: PR checks run on GitHub's merge commit, so confirm the run checked out the current `merge_commit_sha` (`gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n> --jq .merge_commit_sha`); a stale one tests old content.\n- When cutting a stable release: make a version-only commit directly on the accepted RC (`node scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs <rc-ref> <stable-ref>`), land it on `main` through a merge-commit PR, and only then tag, because `release.yml` requires the tagged commit to be an ancestor of `main`. Version tags are immutable: re-run a failed run, or move to the next RC or patch. Then follow `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`.\n- When reporting a gate or a result: state it as measured (\"ledger closed, qualification pending\"), record failed runs unaltered, and make no frontier-grade claim without external qualification.\n- Before tagging or merging, check: required checks green at the exact head? CI on `main` green after the previous merge? Tagged commit an ancestor of `main`? Claims match the evidence?\n'''\ns=s[:m0]+new_merge\nopen(\"AGENTS.md\",\"w\").write(s)\nopen(\"CLAUDE.md\",\"w\").write(\"@AGENTS.md\\n\")\nEOF\nwc -c AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md; head -3 docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md | cut -c1-150; grep -n \"^## \" AGENTS.md","description":"Split XERJ into an on-demand doc, add CLAUDE.md, restructure merge rules as triggers"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch4mt2EHaDPB6dkaWj7uA","requestRef":"d75d654f-b457-4881-9d76-1ab150f3d1dc","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e028f785-a4ee-4c57-8340-eac14c7ae7c6","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:14:55.615Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
