{"parentUuid":"381be568-82f9-48ff-9f43-4a38f4bb42fc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8dca44bb-c11d-425a-aee9-e31977e857cd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SdywrxQWFaeMAqyLzEsNxs","type":"tool_result","content":"# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query,\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handli\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailabl\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xer\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code:\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are abs\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively l\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\n12:- Entire CLI: export `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` before any `entire` command. The Entire gate no lo\nok 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)\nok\nok\n9511312a\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cf5c7088-b594-4be1-b8f0-a32a0c44617e","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:15:27.117Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query,\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handli\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailabl\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemc