{"parentUuid":"844d7355-8066-4b09-9ac9-a296cec446a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4nQQqAohraWXuumLBA9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2936,"cache_read_input_tokens":394099,"output_tokens":3281,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2200},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2936,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3281,"cache_read_input_tokens":394099,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2936},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":23335,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4nQQX4kfXQkrWGZr7Vq","requestRef":"920a836a-b998-4b1e-80dc-1bd2b1796547","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"83f45e26-84cd-4742-8696-e8e6719bcab5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:21:56.025Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"83f45e26-84cd-4742-8696-e8e6719bcab5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4nQQqAohraWXuumLBA9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I read the main repo and the SDK docs through a page summarizer, not the source, so treat the quoted phrasings as paraphrase. The docs also don't cover event-log or replay internals or the benchmarks, so I can't say anything on those.\n\nOpenHands has split into an agent SDK and server (`software-agent-sdk`), a CLI, and a web \"Agent Canvas\". The Canvas can also drive third-party agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode) over ACP.\n\n**Lessons from their V0 → V1 rewrite, which map to our code**\n- **Sandboxing opt-in.** V0 ran every tool call in Docker, and the agent and sandbox states drifted apart. V1 runs agent and tools in one process by default. We already do that, so this confirms the direction.\n- **One mutable state.** Everything else is immutable, which they say enables reliable persistence and replay. This resembles our known v1.2.0 limitation that a baseline is memory-only after a restart, and that `verified` isn't re-checked on resume.\n- **A hard line between agent core and apps.** In V0, app-specific conditionals and prompts leaked into the agent. They now expose an OpenAPI contract with a generated TypeScript client. That is relevant to the protocol work in the v1.3 plan.\n\n**Mechanisms to compare with ours**\n- **Compaction as a log record.** A condensation is a normal event listing the forgotten event ids, the summary and where it's inserted. It fires at 120 events (summarizing down to about 60) or after a context-window error, and a cheaper model can write the summary. Our open gap `compaction-03`, checking that every gating requirement survives compaction, would be easier to test if compaction left such a record.\n- **Stuck detection.** It is on by default and compares actions by content, not ids. It trips on the same action and result 4 times, the same action erroring 3 times, 3 monologue messages in a row, or an A/B ping-pong for 6 cycles. Our CS-3 detector is deliberately looser: 5/10/20 by call class, so reruns between edits stay legitimate. Alternating patterns and monologues may not be covered the same way, but I haven't checked ours.\n- **Security.** They add a required `security_risk` field to non-read-only tool schemas and let the model rate its own action, with no extra calls. The default is to pause on HIGH or UNKNOWN. The model grades itself, which is weaker than our deterministic authority classification. I'd copy the audit trail of decisions, not the self-rating as a gate.\n- **Trigger-based skills.** Skills activate on triggers and come from a public extensions repo, the same on-demand loading idea as in the `agent-rules-books` repo.\n\n**Positioning**\n- Agent Canvas is a control centre for several agents, driven by ACP. Once our ACP adapter exists (AC-1 in the v1.3 plan), Nexus could be one of the agents such a canvas drives. Our differentiator is evidence and verification, which a control centre could surface.\n- I'd skip the GUI, Electron and Helm work.\n\nIf you want any of this acted on, the cheapest first step is a quick audit of our detector for ping-pong and monologue gaps. I haven't changed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2936,"cache_read_input_tokens":394099,"output_tokens":3281,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2200},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2936,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3281,"cache_read_input_tokens":394099,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2936},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4nQQX4kfXQkrWGZr7Vq","requestRef":"920a836a-b998-4b1e-80dc-1bd2b1796547","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"028f1036-b0f7-412d-af73-1b9b3a463af3","timestamp":"2026-11-15T13:21:58.914Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
