{"parentUuid":"492ea950-7988-439e-8c62-1551ddce1083","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4rc6zg6PsyN1hCBFWxc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The audit is done and read-only, so nothing changed. It covers `cli/src/agent.ts` and `cli/src/core/independent_review.ts` on `main`.\n\n**1. Cheap clearing before summarizing: we already do this, with no LLM involved**\n- Compaction is deterministic. `admitContext` runs a ladder that keeps the 2, then 1, then 0 most recent turns. It pairs that with a shrinking budget for retained raw detail: 6000, 3000, 1200, 400 or 0 characters, with stronger settings from the second attempt on.\n- It keeps raw bodies newest-first, ranks the model's own analysis above raw tool output (it \"cannot be reacquired by rerunning a tool\"), pins the first decision, and never compacts away tool results the model hasn't seen yet. It also keeps reconstructible queries, so cleared output can be re-run.\n- It starts at 80% predictive pressure or when the request wouldn't fit, and stops when a pass doesn't shrink anything. After low-yield compactions it only compacts when it must.\n- We have nothing equivalent to the optional cheap-model summary of the elided middle. I wouldn't add one without a measurement showing the loss matters.\n\n**2. Does clearing break the evidence chain? Not for the reviewer path**\n- The independent reviewer gets a separate package: requirements, authorized scope, baseline and diff, and the verifier receipts. The implementer's narrative is deliberately stripped. Compacting the agent's context can't remove any of it.\n- The TUI also says full output is \"retained in session evidence\".\n- **Not verified:** exactly how the model itself retrieves a cleared output. By design it re-runs the call, and a \"you ran this same call before; findings were recorded\" note is added when it does.\n\n**3. Does the model see its remaining budget? No**\n- I found no notice about context tokens. The model gets a step-limit notice (only under an operator step limit) and a \"your recorded findings have outgrown your memory\" notice, which is an indirect pressure signal.\n- With local models whose context limit is an estimate, a precise number could mislead, so I'd leave it.\n\n**The actionable gap**\n- `compaction-03` is still unowned: after each ladder rung, every gating requirement must still be present. The durable record keeps task requests, but I found no test that walks the rungs and asserts the requirement ledger survives. That would be a small, concrete unit, and I haven't written it or filed it.\n\nOpen items:\n- **`main` CI on `181c3833`:** the monitor is still waiting on it.\n- **#541:** its required checks are still pending. It is the PR for the `AGENTS.md` rewrite."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":424127,"output_tokens":1881,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":999},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1881,"cache_read_input_tokens":424127,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4rc6d6oSJJ1tC1pziDf","requestRef":"e7b44017-1fcf-40f1-9b23-33679fc01f23","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ace8fea0-af3b-4831-b1a2-9d2cb4565b84","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:16:53.208Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-