{"parentUuid":"9399656f-be0d-4afe-a48f-8e8aa95eed6e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4rnHMHxBPbNR78FjLEb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BbtsKZXGDbZYxrUKL3EyuG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5-plan && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nold3=\"| CX-3 | Compaction probe: after summarising, a second bounded call checks that the summary keeps every gating requirement (reference: Gemini CLI `chatCompressionService.ts:770`); reject and fall back otherwise | closes the check `compaction-03` expects, together with CX-5 | M | P1 |\"\nnew3=\"| CX-3 | Compaction probe: after summarising, a second bounded call checks that the summary keeps every gating requirement (reference: Gemini CLI `chatCompressionService.ts:770`); reject and fall back otherwise. Scope: the `compact --llm` path and any future summarising path only; the default ladder (`admitContext`) is deterministic and writes no summary, so CX-5 alone covers it | closes the check `compaction-03` expects on the summarising path, together with CX-5 | M | P1 |\"\nold5=\"| CX-5 | Post-compaction invariant: every gating requirement is present, or the turn blocks (owns CERI `compaction-03`) | scenario active | S | P1 |\"\nnew5=\"| CX-5 | Post-compaction invariant: after every compaction, every gating requirement of the pinned ledger (`seedRequirements`) is present in the request, or the turn blocks with a named reason (owns CERI `compaction-03`). Covers each rung of the `admitContext` ladder (recent turns 2, 1, 0 against detail budgets 6000 down to 0) and `compact --llm`; an over-limit ledger is omitted whole and blocks, never truncated (Codex reference, SI-6) | a test walks every rung and asserts the ledger survives; a forced zero-budget rung with an over-limit ledger blocks; scenario `compaction-03` active | S | P1 |\"\nassert old3 in s and old5 in s\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.repla