{"parentUuid":"400ca166-6ee1-4bf7-8f7a-a33fc21e3f1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4roRXTKp9x6AgUgWT5F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BUGe1UsGwaVeQBnyiWYxqA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5-plan && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(v1.2.1): CX-5 acceptance from the compaction audit; CX-3 scoped to the summarising path\n\ncompaction-03 was already owned by CX-5 (GA-19). The 2026-11-15 audit of admitContext sets its acceptance (walk every ladder rung and compact --llm; over-limit ledger blocks, never truncated) and shows the default compaction writes no summary, so the CX-3 probe applies only to the summarising path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/cx5-plan-refine 2>&1 | tail -1; PR=$(gh pr create --base main --title \"docs(v1.2.1): plan compaction-03 acceptance in CX-5; scope CX-3\" --body \"compaction-03 already has an owner: v1.2.1 CX-5 (gap GA-19). A read-only audit of the compaction code on main (\\`admitContext\\` in cli/src/agent.ts) sets its acceptance and corrects a premise:\n\n- CX-5 now names what the test must cover: the pinned ledger (\\`seedRequirements\\`) present after every rung of the ladder (recent turns 2/1/0 x detail budgets 6000..0) and after \\`compact --llm\\`; an over-limit ledger blocks with a named reason and is never truncated.\n- CX-3 (summary probe) is scoped to the summarising path. The default compaction is deterministic and writes no summary, so CX-5 alone covers it.\n- Not planned, on purpose: telling the model its remaining token budget. No such notice exists today; with local models the limit is an estimate and a precise number could mislead.\n\nThe v1.2.0 notes keep saying \\\"no owning unit\\\"; they are accurate for that release and are not rewritten. Docs only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" 2>&1 | tail -1); e