{"parentUuid":"0fa469ca-4935-4393-866f-7da87f9153a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4rsRQcWdAVwAWnoYnCz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It was already planned, so I refined the existing plan in **PR #542** instead of adding a duplicate unit.\n\n- **Ownership:** `compaction-03` is owned by **CX-5** in the v1.2.1 plan, tracked as gap **GA-19**. I confirmed that in the plan before touching anything. The \"no owning unit\" wording is only in the v1.2.0 notes, which are accurate for that release, and I left them alone.\n- **CX-5 acceptance:** it now says what the test must cover. After every rung of the `admitContext` ladder (recent turns 2, 1, 0 against detail budgets 6000 down to 0) and after `compact --llm`, every requirement in the pinned ledger must still be in the request. An over-limit ledger blocks with a named reason and is never truncated.\n- **CX-3 scope:** that unit (a probe that checks a summary kept every requirement) now applies only to the `compact --llm` path. The default compaction is deterministic and writes no summary, so CX-5 alone covers it. I left CX-3's size and priority unchanged.\n- **Gap register:** the matching rows in the gap analysis now point to CX-5.\n- **Telling the model its remaining token budget:** not planned, deliberately. No such notice exists today, and with local models the limit is only an estimate, so a precise number could mislead. The PR body records that reasoning.\n\nDocs only; I ran the drift check and it passes. The number #542 is read from the PR list this time.\n\nStill waiting: `main` CI on `181c3833` and the required checks on #541. The monitor `bsiupod7h` reports the `main` result."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":433212,"output_tokens":536,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_us