{"parentUuid":"9d2ae65d-dc87-49ff-8f47-2a11be444807","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4sDYu7hrpdCRUXv2gSN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't read the report itself, so this is mostly from summaries. [Anthropic's page](https://resources.anthropic.com/2026-agentic-coding-trends-report) is a gated landing page with no findings on it. The [public PDF](https://resources.anthropic.com/hubfs/2026%20Agentic%20Coding%20Trends%20Report.pdf) came back as binary, and I have no PDF extractor installed. I read two secondary summaries instead: [Tessl](https://tessl.io/blog/8-trends-shaping-software-engineering-in-2026-according-to-anthropics-agentic-coding-report/) and [handsonai](https://handsonai.info/resources/anthropic-coding-trends/). Treat what follows as the summaries' account of the report.\n\n**The eight trends, per Tessl**\n- **Roles shift:** the software lifecycle moves toward supervising agents, system design and review.\n- **Agent teams:** specialised agents work in parallel under an orchestrator.\n- **End-to-end work:** tasks stretch to multiple hours or days.\n- **Asking for help:** agents flag uncertainty and risk, and agents also review AI-written code.\n- **Beyond engineers:** legacy languages and non-engineering roles.\n- **Shorter timelines:** more, faster delivery.\n- **Non-engineers build tools.**\n- **Security cuts both ways:** it helps defenders and attackers scale.\n\n**The one number**\n- handsonai says engineers use AI in roughly 60% of their work but can fully delegate only 0–20% of tasks. Neither summary says how that was measured. Tessl cites no figures at all, and neither summary mentions company case studies.\n\n**Lessons for Nexus**\n- **Verification, not generation, is the bottleneck.** If the 0–20% delegation figure holds, the missing piece is trust in the output. That is where our work already sits: receipts, independent review that needs verifier evidence, and verification files the agent can't silently edit. I'd say that plainly, without a frontier-grade claim.\n- **\"Agents learn to ask for help\" depends on the model flagging its own uncertainty.** Ours is enforced by gates: BLOCKED outcomes, a steering conflict that asks the operator, and requirements marked blocked. I'd check whether headless runs have a clear escalate-and-resume path, but I haven't audited it.\n- **Multi-hour and multi-day tasks are a measurement gap, not a feature gap.** Our known limits (`verified` not re-checked on resume, baselines memory-only after a restart) matter more at that length. The v1.2.1 benchmark and context units are where to test long-horizon runs.\n- **Agent teams need isolation.** Our SI-8 rule (concurrency above 1 requires `git.isolate`) is the coordination safeguard.\n- **Security:** agent-generated code at scale supports our verification-path guard and the language-server containment from v1.2.0.\n\n**Caveats:** it is a vendor report, the methodology is unstated in these summaries, and the two summaries don't even agree on the structure (six takeaways against eight trends). I'd rely on the trends as framing only.\n\n**Status:** `main` CI on `181c3833` and `85ef1f69` is now in progress, no longer queued. #541 and #542 each have three required checks pending."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1877,"cache_read_input_tokens":442190,"output_tokens":1109,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1877,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1109,"cache_read_input_tokens":442190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1877},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4sDYb1rTKxivWdgZRZe","requestRef":"4df393a8-9b4a-47bd-91d0-538d2357f432","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"2135aefb-67ba-4ebd-9a68-03e4d081b4a6","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:24:46.913Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
