{"parentUuid":"63aa9f6b-2946-472f-99bb-eb3eaf12bf4f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01LQssAgdURF9JeqqTewLL6Q","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":667},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d2b37a00-b138-4571-b8d9-d44ecca875d0","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:30:13.268Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"63aa9f6b-2946-472f-99bb-eb3eaf12bf4f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"800b2278-3d1a-4146-9101-4891a64978af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQssAgdURF9JeqqTewLL6Q","type":"tool_result","content":"### MQ: measure and qualify\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MQ-0 | Run the G1.1-4 matrix on the v1.2.0 release-candidate archive under the GATEWAY claim; record `docs/evidence/v1.2.0/…` and add the figure to the rc notes (closes GA-03) | evidence file with archive sha256, per-alias counts, repaired / invalid counts; notes updated by a docs PR | S | P0 |\n| MQ-1 | Benchmark adapter: a Harbor / Terminal-Bench runner for Nexus (template: Goose `evals/harbor/`), plus a SWE-bench-style adapter if the task format allows a hermetic run | `nexus` runs a pinned subset in task containers with no network leaks; results JSON with task ids, model, gateway alias, Nexus version, seed or sampli\n| MQ-2 | False-completion metric: for every run record Nexus's own verdict and the benchmark's ground truth; report pass rate, **claimed-done-but-wrong rate**, and **verified-but-wrong rate** with Wilson 95% intervals (the repo already has the interval code in `eval/score.mjs`); compare against the same model through at least on\n| MQ-3 | Real-project smoke: a nightly job that runs a scripted task on pinned copies of representative repositories (a JS project with `node_modules`, a Makefile project, a Python project, a Rust project, and the owner's own repositories where licensing allows) and fails when `task_completed` errors, hangs or ends UNVERIFIED fo\n| MQ-4 | Scheduled model conformance: a nightly or weekly job that runs the tool-call matrix against the configured gateway aliases and alerts on a drop; claim protocol so it never collides with a human run (template: Goose `model-toolcall-conformance.yml`) | one alert path tested with a forced failure | S | P1 |\n| MQ-5 | CERI baseline identity bound to evidence (audit F02): baseline manifest, model digest, sampling and configuration recorded and verified when a comparison is made; a comparison without bound baselines is labelled non-certifying (decision D7, included) | a comparison against an edited baseline fails; test with a swapped m\n| MQ-6 | CERI evidence loading verifies the integrity record (audit F06): `passed:\"false\"` no longer loads as true, run-id collisions are refused, a tampered record is rejected (D7) | tests for each of the three defects | M | P0 |\n| MQ-7 | Audit Slices B–G, decide each as a unit or a dated deferral, then build in this order: B evidence lifecycle, C verified baselines and paired comparisons (needed for MQ-2 to be called certifying), E request-context manifests, D installed-evaluator adapter, F recovery reference checker, G bounded campaigns (D7). B and C\n\nDependencies: MQ-1 → MQ-2. MQ-3 and MQ-4 are independent. Decision D3 (what is published) and D4 (scope and cost) gate MQ-1 and MQ-2.\n\n### VC: verification completeness (the v1.2.0 deferrals)\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VC-1 | SI-5 operator-declared boundary rules (import allow/deny, protected public files) checked on the candidate diff with deterministic analysis; interface/schema/format changes classified compatible / potentially breaking / unknown; coverage limits always reported | boundary violation = REJECT; undeclared dependency = advis\n| VC-2 | DV-3 operator-authorised regression obligations: a confirmed failing test becomes a protected obligation only on operator authorisation; the original failure record is kept when later minimised | authorised obligation replayed on the next candidate and a weakening edit recorded; unauthorised promotion cannot happen | M \n| VC-3 | DV-4 attempt lineage (parent attempt, diff hash) and behavioural differential against a declared reference only when an authorised requirement names one | baseline-defect correction not blocked when an authoritative requirement contradicts the baseline; finite-case agreement never reported as equivalence | M | P2 |\n| VC-4 | Close the two pending CERI scenarios once VC-1 lands; assign an owner to every scenario in `semantic_integrity` | pending count 0 or each pending carries a unit id | S | P1 |\n| VC-5 | Re-check `verified` on resume (invalidate when the candidate identity differs) and persist the unbound-pass marker so a resumed task does not hit the \"no matching baseline\" refusal | resume test: edited workspace demotes `verified`; resume after an unbound pass completes as REGRESSION_FREE | S | P1 |\n| VC-6 | Type-check gaps: baseline run to catch callers broken in untouched files, count shell-changed files as modified (workspace diff, not edit tools), Go (`go vet`) and Python (pyright/mypy when configured) | a change that breaks an untouched caller blocks VERIFIED; opt-out stays | M | P2 |\n| VC-7 | Convergence on the `run_tests` path and for operator-configured verifiers | a `run_tests`-only loop stops with the history attached | S | P2 |\n| VC-8 | Per-role tool allowlists beyond reviewer and researcher (old backlog REQ:259, accepted 2026-11-15): allowlists for implementer and tester, consistent with SI-2's tester scoping (`roleToolAllowList`, `cli/src/agent.ts:5490`) | each role's disallowed tool is refused with a reason; existing flows unchanged | S | P2 (v1.2.2\n\n### WM: weak-model robustness\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WM-1 | Schema-driven argument repair (stringified JSON, \"20\" to 20, nulls, arrays) only where the schema makes the fix unambiguous (reference: opencode `plugin/tool-input-repair.ts`); every repair recorded | repair counted in the matrix as repaired, never as native valid | M | P1 |\n| WM-2 | Edit-failure feedback: when an edit does not apply, return the closest actual lines (reference: Aider `editblock_coder.py:100-312`) | test with whitespace and elision mismatches | S | P1 |\n| WM-3 | Extend the G1.1-4 matrix to every alias the gateway serves, with pacing and cache-bypass checks unchanged | per-alias table in evidence | S | P1 |\n\n### CX: context\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CX-1 | Label every injected summary block (including `compact --llm`) as untrusted data with its source (G-SI-6) | request-shape snapshot (TI-1) updated; test with an injected instruction in a summary | S | P1 |\n| CX-2 | Compaction state stored separately from the canonical transcript and validated by a hash of the covered prefix on resume (reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript | M | P1 |\n| CX-3 | Compaction probe: after summarising, a second bounded call checks that the summary keeps every gating requirement (reference: Gemini CLI `chatCompressionService.ts:770`); reject and fall back otherwise. Scope: the `compact --llm` path and any future summarising path only; the default ladder (`admitContext`) is determini\n| CX-4 | Tool-output masking above a token threshold, with the full output retrievable by id (references: Gemini CLI `toolOutputMaskingService.ts:25`, Cline cached tool results) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves | S | P2 |\n| CX-5 | Post-compaction invariant: after every compaction, every gating requirement of the pinned ledger (`seedRequirements`) is present in the request, or the turn blocks with a named reason (owns CERI `compaction-03`). Covers each rung of the `admitContext` ladder (recent turns 2, 1, 0 against detail budgets 6000 down to 0) a\n| CX-6 | Prompt caching: request cache hints for providers that support them; measure cached-token share | share reported in the matrix | S | P2 |\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"26573b59-9453-4340-bbeb-9d4689d6cf26","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:30:13.709Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"### MQ: measure and qualify\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MQ-0 | Run the G1.1-4 matrix on the v1.2.0 release-candidate archive under the GATEWAY claim; record `docs/evidence/v1.2.0/…` and add the figure to the rc notes (closes GA-03) | evidence file with archive sha256, per-alias counts, repaired / invalid counts; notes updated by a docs PR | S | P0 |\n| MQ-1 | Benchmark adapter: a Harbor / Terminal-Bench runner for Nexus (template: Goose `evals/harbor/`), plus a SWE-bench-style adapter if the task format allows a hermetic run | `nexus` runs a pinned subset in task containers with no network leaks; results JSON with task ids, model, gateway alias, Nexus version, seed or sampli\n| MQ-2 | False-completion metric: for every run record Nexus's own verdict and the benchmark's ground truth; report pass rate, **claimed-done-but-wrong rate**, and **verified-but-wrong rate** with Wilson 95% intervals (the repo already has the interval code in `eval/score.mjs`); compare against the same model through at least on\n| MQ-3 | Real-project smoke: a nightly job that runs a scripted task on pinned copies of representative repositories (a JS project with `node_modules`, a Makefile project, a Python project, a Rust project, and the owner's own repositories where licensing allows) and fails when `task_completed` errors, hangs or ends UNVERIFIED fo\n| MQ-4 | Scheduled model conformance: a nightly or weekly job that runs the tool-call matrix against the configured gateway aliases and alerts on a drop; claim protocol so it never collides with a human run (template: Goose `model-toolcall-conformance.yml`) | one alert path tested with a forced failure | S | P1 |\n| MQ-5 | CERI baseline identity bound to evidence (audit F02): baseline manifest, model digest, sampling and configuration recorded and verified when a comparison is made; a comparison without bound baselines is labelled non-certifying (decision D7, included) | a comparison against an edited baseline fails; test with a swapped m\n| MQ-6 | CERI evidence loading verifies the integrity record (audit F06): `passed:\"false\"` no longer loads as true, run-id collisions are refused, a tampered record is rejected (D7) | tests for each of the three defects | M | P0 |\n| MQ-7 | Audit Slices B–G, decide each as a unit or a dated deferral, then build in this order: B evidence lifecycle, C verified baselines and paired comparisons (needed for MQ-2 to be called certifying), E request-context manifests, D installed-evaluator adapter, F recovery reference checker, G bounded campaigns (D7). B and C\n\nDependencies: MQ-1 → MQ-2. MQ-3 and MQ-4 are independent. Decision D3 (what is published) and D4 (scope and cost) gate MQ-1 and MQ-2.\n\n### VC: verification completeness (the v1.2.0 deferrals)\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VC-1 | SI-5 operator-declared boundary rules (import allow/deny, protected public files) checked on the candidate diff with deterministic analysis; interface/schema/format changes classified compatible / potentially breaking / unknown; coverage limits always reported | boundary violation = REJECT; undeclared dependency = advis\n| VC-2 | DV-3 operator-authorised regression obligations: a confirmed failing test becomes a protected obligation only on operator authorisation; the original failure record is kept when later minimised | authorised obligation replayed on the next candidate and a weakening edit recorded; unauthorised promotion cannot happen | M \n| VC-3 | DV-4 attempt lineage (parent attempt, diff hash) and behavioural differential against a declared reference only when an authorised requirement names one | baseline-defect correction not blocked when an authoritative requirement contradicts the baseline; finite-case agreement never reported as equivalence | M | P2 |\n| VC-4 | Close the two pending CERI scenarios once VC-1 lands; assign an owner to every scenario in `semantic_integrity` | pending count 0 or each pending carries a unit id | S | P1 |\n| VC-5 | Re-check `verified` on resume (invalidate when the candidate identity differs) and persist the unbound-pass marker so a resumed task does not hit the \"no matching baseline\" refusal | resume test: edited workspace demotes `verified`; resume after an unbound pass completes as REGRESSION_FREE | S | P1 |\n| VC-6 | Type-check gaps: baseline run to catch callers broken in untouched files, count shell-changed files as modified (workspace diff, not edit tools), Go (`go vet`) and Python (pyright/mypy when configured) | a change that breaks an untouched caller blocks VERIFIED; opt-out stays | M | P2 |\n| VC-7 | Convergence on the `run_tests` path and for operator-configured verifiers | a `run_tests`-only loop stops with the history attached | S | P2 |\n| VC-8 | Per-role tool allowlists beyond reviewer and researcher (old backlog REQ:259, accepted 2026-11-15): allowlists for implementer and tester, consistent with SI-2's tester scoping (`roleToolAllowList`, `cli/src/agent.ts:5490`) | each role's disallowed tool is refused with a reason; existing flows unchanged | S | P2 (v1.2.2\n\n### WM: weak-model robustness\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WM-1 | Schema-driven argument repair (stringified JSON, \"20\" to 20, nulls, arrays) only where the schema makes the fix unambiguous (reference: opencode `plugin/tool-input-repair.ts`); every repair recorded | repair counted in the matrix as repaired, never as native valid | M | P1 |\n| WM-2 | Edit-failure feedback: when an edit does not apply, return the closest actual lines (reference: Aider `editblock_coder.py:100-312`) | test with whitespace and elision mismatches | S | P1 |\n| WM-3 | Extend the G1.1-4 matrix to every alias the gateway serves, with pacing and cache-bypass checks unchanged | per-alias table in evidence | S | P1 |\n\n### CX: context\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CX-1 | Label every injected summary block (including `compact --llm`) as untrusted data with its source (G-SI-6) | request-shape snapshot (TI-1) updated; test with an injected instruction in a summary | S | P1 |\n| CX-2 | Compaction state stored separately from the canonical transcript and validated by a hash of the covered prefix on resume (reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript | M | P1 |\n| CX-3 | Compaction probe: after summarising, a second bounded call checks that the summary keeps every gating requirement (reference: Gemini CLI `chatCompressionService.ts:770`); reject and fall back otherwise. Scope: the `compact --llm` path and any future summarising path only; the default ladder (`admitContext`) is determini\n| CX-4 | Tool-output masking above a token threshold, with the full output retrievable by id (references: Gemini CLI `toolOutputMaskingService.ts:25`, Cline cached tool results) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves | S | P2 |\n| CX-5 | Post-compaction invariant: after every compaction, every gating requirement of the pinned ledger (`seedRequirements`) is present in the request, or the turn blocks with a named reason (owns CERI `compaction-03`). Covers each rung of the `admitContext` ladder (recent turns 2, 1, 0 against detail budgets 6000 down to 0) a\n| CX-6 | Prompt caching: request cache hints for providers that support them; measure cached-token share | share reported in the matrix | S | P2 |","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"63aa9f6b-2946-472f-99bb-eb3eaf12bf4f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
