{"parentUuid":"a37c43bf-4994-4ad5-a7b9-79f66cd6fd05","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01WDjaUt6JH6kZHPLbroEPZ5","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":795},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c882a313-524b-4a49-a55b-7a5050026d1f","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:30:39.461Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"a37c43bf-4994-4ad5-a7b9-79f66cd6fd05","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"800b2278-3d1a-4146-9101-4891a64978af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WDjaUt6JH6kZHPLbroEPZ5","type":"tool_result","content":"1: # Nexus Code v1.3 plan: the platform track\n5: ## 1. Purpose and theme\n16: ## 2. Evidence and its limits\n23: ## 3. Principles\n34: ## 4. Workstreams and units\n38: ### PF: protocol and embedding foundation\n47: ### AC: ACP and IDE access\n56: ### VR: Nexus as the verification layer\n63: ### BG: background and scheduled runs\n71: ### GV: governance\n81: ### HK: hooks and plugins\n89: ### PA: parallel agents and goals\n97: ## 5. Sequencing\n106: ## 6. Release gates\n118: ## 7. Decisions needed\n132: ## 8. Risks\n PF-1 | Publish the client protocol: JSON Schema generated from `cli/src/protocol.ts`, a checked-in copy, a TS/Rust parity test replacing hand-sync\n PF-2 | `nexus run --json` result schema with a `schema_version`, documented exit codes in the manual, `--input-json` or stdin for the task \n PF-3 | Transport beyond a parent's stdio: a unix domain socket (default) with a token and origin check for any localhost HTTP/WebSocket listener (\n PF-4 | Library entry point: a `lib` entry that does not run commander on import, `exports` and `types` in `cli/package.json`, a package name decis\n AC-1 | ACP adapter over the sidecar protocol (stdio), hand-rolled JSON-RPC with no dependency: `initialize` with a capability list, `session/new`,\n AC-2 | ACP conformance: fixture suite plus runs against two real ACP clients (decision D14), recorded as fixtures; no live model \n VR-1 | `nexus verify` (no agent run): given a worktree or a base and head, run the discovered or configured verifier, the type-check evidence (CG-\n VR-2 | Expose verification as an MCP tool and an ACP extension so another harness can call Nexus to check its own work (`serve-mcp` today exposes \n BG-1 | Detached runner: a user-level job runner that owns durable operations so a run survives its CLI process (decision D15: a documented `system\n BG-2 | Schedules: a spec (trigger `cron`, `every` or `once`; objective ledger id; `max_rounds`; timeout; policy `read-only` or `worktree-write`; o\n BG-3 | Event triggers (file change, webhook) \n GV-1 | Managed policy with fixed precedence **system > user > project**: `/etc/nexus/policy.toml` (path per decision D16), `~/.config/nexus/policy\n GV-2 | Audit export: `nexus audit export <task\\\n GV-3 | Hash-chain the flight recorder and the verification-attempt log (today append-only by convention only) and verify the chain on `nexus fligh\n GV-4 | Telemetry transparency (this also settles v1.2.1 unit PC-5): document what the local traces contain, add a setting to disable them and a re\n GV-5 | Admin controls from the system policy: a strict mode that disables auto and full-access, an MCP and plugin allowlist \n HK-1 | Declarative command hooks: events `pre-tool`, `post-tool`, `pre-verify`, `post-verify`, `permission-request`, `session-start`, `session-end\n HK-2 | Plugin manifest `nexus-plugin.json` (name, version, declared contributions: hooks, skills, verifiers, MCP servers; required permissions); i\n HK-3 | Per-plugin trust instead of per-directory, and run workspace-defined plugin hooks as subprocesses rather than in-process (a trusted workspa\n PA-1 | Parallel run visibility: `nexus operation watch` (CLI view first) showing units, worktrees and owners; a worktree owner id recorded in the \n PA-2 | Verified merge arbitration: when parallel units integrate, apply each diff, run verification on the merged tree, reject on failure. No peer\n PA-3 | Goal semantics: a ledger entry active from an earlier process resumes **paused** (opencode `goal.ts` boot id), stall counting by failure fi\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bfcf4270-3da1-4c83-ae68-480b84b9e006","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:30:40.058Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1: # Nexus Code