 change, webhook) \n GV-1 | Managed policy with fixed precedence **system > user > project**: `/etc/nexus/policy.toml` (path per decision D16), `~/.config/nexus/policy\n GV-2 | Audit export: `nexus audit export <task\\\n GV-3 | Hash-chain the flight recorder and the verification-attempt log (today append-only by convention only) and verify the chain on `nexus fligh\n GV-4 | Telemetry transparency (this also settles v1.2.1 unit PC-5): document what the local traces contain, add a setting to disable them and a re\n GV-5 | Admin controls from the system policy: a strict mode that disables auto and full-access, an MCP and plugin allowlist \n HK-1 | Declarative command hooks: events `pre-tool`, `post-tool`, `pre-verify`, `post-verify`, `permission-request`, `session-start`, `session-end\n HK-2 | Plugin manifest `nexus-plugin.json` (name, version, declared contributions: hooks, skills, verifiers, MCP servers; required permissions); i\n HK-3 | Per-plugin trust instead of per-directory, and run workspace-defined plugin hooks as subprocesses rather than in-process (a trusted workspa\n PA-1 | Parallel run visibility: `nexus operation watch` (CLI view first) showing units, worktrees and owners; a worktree owner id recorded in the \n PA-2 | Verified merge arbitration: when parallel units integrate, apply each diff, run verification on the merged tree, reject on failure. No peer\n PA-3 | Goal semantics: a ledger entry active from an earlier process resumes **paused** (opencode `goal.ts` boot id), stall counting by failure fi","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a37c43bf-4994-4ad5-a7b9-79f66cd6fd05","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","ve