{"parentUuid":"1d9eb9d5-903e-432f-9dfd-e1c28c520341","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"800b2278-3d1a-4146-9101-4891a64978af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5PcEsvfyxG75AsnKNV9DL","type":"tool_result","content":"== PLAN §5 + §9\n## 5. Sequencing and release split\n\nCapacity warning. After the 2026-11-15 decisions the unit list is about three times what v1.2.0 carried, and v1.2.0 took a week of agent work with a 70-minute CI cycle. All of it cannot be one release without cutting corners that this project does not cut. Decision D12 (accepted 2026-11-15): **v1.2.1 = Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2; v1.2.2 = Phase 3 and the native provider protocols.** Anything not merged with green ga\n\nPhase 0 (immediately after v1.2.0 ships): MQ-0, DH-1, DH-2, DH-5, PC-2, PC-1. These cut the cycle time, remove the hang class and finish the evidence.\n\nPhase 1 (independent, parallelisable): MQ-3, MQ-5, MQ-6, MQ-1, then MQ-2 (needs MQ-5/MQ-6 to be called certifying); PR-1, PR-2, PR-3, PR-9, PR-11; CS-3, CS-4, WM-1, WM-2, CX-1, CX-5, VC-5.\n\nPhase 2: PR-4, PR-5, PR-12; CS-7, CS-8 (D5); MQ-7 slices B and C; CS-1 and CS-2 (defaults per D1 and D2: CS-1 stays opt-in unless the default is changed by a later decision); CX-2, CX-3, VC-1, RD-3, RD-4, MT-3, WM-3, MQ-4, PC-3, DH-3, DH-4, DH-6.\n\nPhase 3 (v1.2.2): native protocols PR-6 (Gemini), PR-7 (Bedrock), PR-8 (Vertex), PR-10; CS-9, CS-10, VC-8, RD-7 (added 2026-11-15 from the old-backlog review); MQ-7 slices D, E, F, G; RD-1 (macOS arm64; D6 default is Linux x86_64 only, so this waits for a decision), MT-1, MT-2, VC-2, VC-3, VC-6, VC-7, CX-4, CX-6, RD-2, RD-5, RD-6, CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6.\n\nD9 note: \"every cloud provider configurable\" is delivered in v1.2.1 for every OpenAI-compatible provider and for Azure OpenAI, Gemini's compatible endpoint and Bedrock's OpenAI-compatible endpoint (PR-2, PR-3, PR-5), which is most of the 334 providers in models.dev. The three native protocols (Gemini, Bedrock Converse with SigV4, Vertex with ADC) are the largest pieces and ship in v1.2.2 unless you move them up.\n\n## 9. Evidence still missing\n\nThe qualification evidence from 2026-10-12 and the v1.0.0 readiness document were not read for this plan (DH-5). Peer behaviour is as read in source on the clone dates in `GAP_ANALYSIS.md`; OpenHands was not assessed and Claude Code was not read.\n== GAP register tail\n| GA-35 | Not extracted: `qualification_2026-10-12` evidence and `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` | §1 | P0 (finish the ledger) | DH-5 |\n37:| IDE / protocol | Goose, Cline, opencode, Gemini CLI: ACP; Cline and Gemini CLI: VS Code | none |\n52:| ID | Item | D/U |\n104:| ID | Gap | Evidence | Disp. | Unit |\n| GA-33 | No crash reporting; OTLP opt-in status unverified | §4 ops | P2 | PC-5 |\n| GA-34 | `commander` one major behind (inf, registry not checked); 2 Dependabot PRs | §4 deps | P2 | PC-6 |\n| GA-36 | Forced `tool_choice: required` is sent without checking whether the model accepts it (models.dev lists `capabilities.tools.choice` per model; an Azure-hosted Cl\n| GA-35 | Not extracted: `qualification_2026-10-12` evidence and `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` | §1 | P0 (finish the ledger) | DH-5 |\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"374a9ef3-8a6e-45af-bd41-9334253bd6b0","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:30:53.254Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== PLAN §5 + §9\n## 5. Sequencing and release split\n\nCapacity warning. After the 2026-11-15 decisions the unit list is about three times what v1.2.0 carried, and v1.2.0 took a week of agent work with a 70-minute CI cycle. All of it cannot be one release without cutting corners that this project does not cut. Decision D12 (accepted 2026-11-15): **v1.2.1 = Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2; v1.2.2 = Phase 3 and the native provider protocols.** Anything not merged with green ga\n\nPhase 0 (immediately after v1.2.0 ships): MQ-0, DH-1, DH-2, DH-5, PC-2, PC-1. These cut the cycle time, remove the hang class and finish the evidence.\n\nPhase 1 (independent, parallelisable): MQ-3, MQ-5, MQ-6, MQ-1, then MQ-2 (needs MQ-5/MQ-6 to be called certifying); PR-1, PR-2, PR-3, PR-9, PR-11; CS-3, CS-4, WM-1, WM-2, CX-1, CX-5, VC-5.\n\nPhase 2: PR-4, PR-5, PR-12; CS-7, CS-8 (D5); MQ-7 slices B and C; CS-1 and CS-2 (defaults per D1 and D2: CS-1 stays opt-in unless the default is changed by a later decision); CX-2, CX-3, VC-1, RD-3, RD-4, MT-3, WM-3, MQ-4, PC-3, DH-3, DH-4, DH-6.\n\nPhase 3 (v1.2.2): native protocols PR-6 (Gemini), PR-7 (Bedrock), PR-8 (Vertex), PR-10; CS-9, CS-10, VC-8, RD-7 (added 2026-11-15 from the old-backlog review); MQ-7 slices D, E, F, G; RD-1 (macOS arm64; D6 default is Linux x86_64 only, so this waits for a decision), MT-1, MT-2, VC-2, VC-3, VC-6, VC-7, CX-4, CX-6, RD-2, RD-5, RD-6, CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6.\n\nD9 note: \"every cloud provider configurable\" is delivered in v1.2.1 for every OpenAI-compatible provider and for Azure OpenAI, Gemini's compatible endpoint and Bedrock's OpenAI-compatible endpoint (PR-2, PR-3, PR-5), which is most of the 334 providers in models.dev. The three native protocols (Gemini, Bedrock Converse with SigV4, Vertex with ADC) are the largest pieces and ship in v1.2.2 unless you move them up.\n\n## 9. Evidence still missing\n\nThe qualification evidence from 2026-10-12 and the v1.0.0 readiness document were not read for this plan (DH-5). Peer behaviour is as read in source on the clone dates in `GAP_ANALYSIS.md`; OpenHands was not assessed and Claude Code was not read.\n== GAP register tail\n| GA-35 | Not extracted: `qualification_2026-10-12` evidence and `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` | §1 | P0 (finish the ledger) | DH-5 |\n37:| IDE / protocol | Goose, Cline, opencode, Gemini CLI: ACP; Cline and Gemini CLI: VS Code | none |\n52:| ID | Item | D/U |\n104:| ID | Gap | Evidence | Disp. | Unit |\n| GA-33 | No crash reporting; OTLP opt-in status unverified | §4 ops | P2 | PC-5 |\n| GA-34 | `commander` one major behind (inf, registry not checked); 2 Dependabot PRs | §4 deps | P2 | PC-6 |\n| GA-36 | Forced `tool_choice: required` is sent without checking whether the model accepts it (models.dev lists `capabilities.tools.choice` per model; an Azure-hosted Cl\n| GA-35 | Not extracted: `qualification_2026-10-12` evidence and `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` | §1 | P0 (finish the ledger) | DH-5 |","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d9eb9d5-903e-432f-9dfd-e1c28c520341","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
