; find line numbers in v1.2.1 plan"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4shDTMn68FME8BjqnfY","requestRef":"d121cb73-835c-46c4-bf6d-8f6ac19121ed","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4fd4c8e4-586c-407d-9823-96ab69b94e96","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:31:02.943Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"4fd4c8e4-586c-407d-9823-96ab69b94e96","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_013BUzuf1w4V3TMF5f5UyUMD","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":472},"type":"attachment","uuid":"705d9969-9d16-4714-9f36-41446781e6e6","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:31:03.455Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"4fd4c8e4-586c-407d-9823-96ab69b94e96","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"800b2278-3d1a-4146-9101-4891a64978af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BUzuf1w4V3TMF5f5UyUMD","type":"tool_result","content":"## 2. Evidence and its limits\n\n- **Nexus today** (read-only inventory, 2026-11-15; \"present\" means present in source or docs, nothing was run): sidecar/TUI protocol is NDJSON over the sidecar's stdio with `PROTOCOL_VERSION = 1`, an event `v`, a one-way `hello`, typed unions in `cli/src/protocol.ts:53-204` hand-mirrored in `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/protocol.rs`, **no schema file, no socket**; `nexus run --json` returns `TaskExecutionResult` (`cli/src/core/app.ts:44`) with no schema or version, exit codes defined only in code (0 \n- **Peers, read from source** (shallow clones of 2026-11-13/14; Codex at commit 336b19a; untrusted code, nothing run): ACP servers in goose (`crates/goose/src/acp`), Cline (`apps/cli/src/acp/acpAgent.ts`), Gemini CLI (`packages/cli/src/acp`) and opencode (`packages/cli/src/acp/agent.ts`), the Codex `app-server` (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, websocket or UDS; schema generated from Rust types and checked in); schedulers in goose (`scheduler/full.rs`), Cline (`*.cron.md` and event specs) and opencode (\n- **XERJ reference queries** (2026-11-15, local node, read-only; the `opencode` index is flagged \"not verified complete\", so a miss there is not proof of absence): `xerj code opencode` for ACP, scheduling and plugin manifests; `xerj search --prefix goose` for ACP, scheduler and extension manifests; `xerj search --prefix xc-opencode` for managed policy. **Took:** opencode's wire-level ACP fixture pattern (`packages/cli/test/acp/wire-fixture.ts`) for protocol conformance tests; opencode's schedule\n- **Not covered:** Claude Code and agy were not read (web sources only); parts of Cline's daemon, Codex's hook handler types and plugin manifest, and goose's managed policy were sampled, not read in full; peer behaviour under load was not measured.\n\n51: | AC-1 | ACP adapter over the sidecar protocol (stdio), hand-rolled JSON-RPC with no dependency: `initialize` with a capability list, `session/new`, `session/load`, `session/prompt`, `session/cancel`; streaming `tool_call` and `tool_call_update` with diff content; a `verification` update carrying receipt ids and verifier results; client-bound `session/request_permission` with allow-once and reject only (no \"allow always\" at first); one extension, `_nexus/receipt/get`. Reference: goose, Cline, opencode, Gemini CLI ACP servers and the Codex app-server (all four ACP servers use the same three-option permission request; opencode attaches the diff to the request so the user decides with the change in view) | a scripted ACP client completes a task; an `allow` reply to an action the gates deny has no effect (gate test G-3); the receipt is retrievable | L | P1 |\n60: | VR-1 | `nexus verify` (no agent run): given a worktree or a base and head, run the discovered or configured verifier, the type-check evidence (CG-4), the verification-file guard and the independent reviewer, and print a verdict VERIFIED / REGRESSION_FREE / UNVERIFIED / BLOCKED with the receipt; exit code per the documented contract; usable as a CI gate (pairs with the v1.2.1 GitHub Action, RD-4) | a known-bad diff (weakened test) is not VERIFIED; the same diff produced by another harness gives the same verdict | M | P1 |\n86: | HK-2 | Plugin manifest `nexus-plugin.json` (name, version, declared contributions: hooks, skills, verifiers, MCP servers; required permissions); install from a local path or a git URL **pinned to a commit hash**; capabilities shown at install, resolved commit recorded in an install receipt; `nexus plugins install\\|list\\|remove\\|verify`; no marketplace and no auto-update (reference: Gemini CLI `gemini-extension.json`, goose `.goose-plugin-install.json`). Also fix the documented example in `docs/SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS.md` that does not match the code (`onTurnStart` positional arguments versus a context object) and stop swallowing plugin load errors silently | installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install | M | P1 |\n93: | PA-1 | Parallel run visibility: `nexus operation watch` (CLI view first) showing units, worktrees and owners; a worktree owner id recorded in the receipt (reference: Codex `worktree` crate `owner` and `bind_thread`); a concurrency cap tied to a CPU and memory budget instead of a count only | two parallel units show their owners and states; the cap refuses a third when the budget is exhausted | M | P1 |\n== PLAN CS-10, VC-8, MQ-7 tail, VC-3 line nums\n55 65 70 85 100 102 104\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e838189c-eb51-462a-a640-10a2bbf91ded","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:31:03.723Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 2. Evidence and its limits\n\n- **Nexus today** (read-only inventory, 2026-11-15; \"present\" means present in source or docs, nothing was run): sidecar/TUI protocol is NDJSON over the sidecar's stdio with `PROTOCOL_VERSION = 1`, an event `v`, a one-way `hello`, typed unions in `cli/src/protocol.ts:53-204` hand-mirrored in `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/protocol.rs`, **no schema file, no socket**; `nexus run --json` returns `TaskExecutionResult` (`cli/src/core/app.ts:44`) with no schema or version, exit codes defined only in code (0 \n- **Peers, read from source** (shallow clones of 2026-11-13/14; Codex at commit 336b19a; untrusted code, nothing run): ACP servers in goose (`crates/goose/src/acp`), Cline (`apps/cli/src/acp/acpAgent.ts`), Gemini CLI (`packages/cli/src/acp`) and opencode (`packages/cli/src/acp/agent.ts`), the Codex `app-server` (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, websocket or UDS; schema generated from Rust types and checked in); schedulers in goose (`scheduler/full.rs`), Cline (`*.cron.md` and event specs) and opencode (\n- **XERJ reference queries** (2026-11-15, local node, read-only; the `opencode` index is flagged \"not verified complete\", so a miss there is not proof of absence): `xerj code opencode` for ACP, scheduling and plugin manifests; `xerj search --prefix goose` for ACP, scheduler and extension manifests; `xerj search --prefix xc-opencode` for managed policy. **Took:** opencode's wire-level ACP fixture pattern (`packages/cli/test/acp/wire-fixture.ts`) for protocol conformance tests; opencode's schedule\n- **Not covered:** Claude Code and agy were not read (web sources only); parts of Cline's daemon, Codex's hook handler types and plugin manifest, and goose's managed policy were sampled, not read in full; peer behaviour under load was not measured.\n\n51: | AC-1 | ACP adapter over the sidecar protocol (stdio), hand-rolled JSON-RPC with no dependency: `initialize` with a capability list, `session/new`, `session/load`, `session/prompt`, `session/cancel`; streaming `tool_call` and `tool_call_update` with diff content; a `verification` update carrying receipt ids and verifier results; client-bound `session/request_permission` with allow-once and reject only (no \"allow always\" at first); one extension, `_nexus/receipt/get`. Reference: goose, Cline, opencode, Gemini CLI ACP servers and the Codex app-server (all four ACP servers use the same three-option permission request; opencode attaches the diff to the request so the user decides with the change in view) | a scripted ACP client completes a task; an `allow` reply to an action the gates deny has no effect (gate test G-3); the receipt is retrievable | L | P1 |\n60: | VR-1 | `nexus verify` (no agent run): given a worktree or a base and head, run the discovered or configured verifier, the type-check evidence (CG-4), the verification-file guard and the independent reviewer, and print a verdict VERIFIED / REGRESSION_FREE / UNVERIFIED / BLOCKED with the receipt; exit code per the documented contract; usable as a CI gate (pairs with the v1.2.1 GitHub Action, RD-4) | a known-bad diff (weakened test) is not VERIFIED; the same diff produced by another harness gives the same verdict | M | P1 |\n86: | HK-2 | Plugin manifest `nexus-plugin.json` (name, version, declared contributions: hooks, skills, verifiers, MCP servers; required permissions); install from a local path or a git URL **pinned to a commit hash**; capabilities shown at install, resolved commit recorded in an install receipt; `nexus plugins install\\|list\\|remove\\|verify`; no marketplace and no auto-update (reference: Gemini CLI `gemini-extension.json`, goose `.goose-plugin-install.json`). Also fix the documented example in `docs/SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS.md` that does not match the code (`onTurnStart` positional arguments versus a context object) and stop swallowing plugin load errors silently | installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install | M | P1 |\n93: | PA-1 | Parallel run visibility: `nexus operation watch` (CLI view first) showing units, worktrees and owners; a worktree owner id recorded in the receipt (reference: Codex `worktree` crate `owner` and `bind_thread`); a concurrency cap tied to a CPU and memory budget instead of a count only | two parallel units show their owners and states; the cap refuses a third when the budget is exhausted | M | P1 |\n== PLAN CS-10, VC-8, MQ-7 tail, VC-3 line nums\n55 65 70 85 100 102 104","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4fd4c8e4-586c-407d-9823-96ab69b94e96","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
