{"parentUuid":"346e1ea4-c0e9-4e91-8646-df2848565e7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4shxv2rzTCMksq1ScnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Plan edits are mapped onto existing units: four rows get sharper, four small P2 units are added, sequencing and v1.3 notes get updated, and I'm applying them with exact-match assertions.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3085,"cache_read_input_tokens":484951,"output_tokens":7765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3746},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3085,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7765,"cache_read_input_tokens":484951,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3085},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4shxYT2hMf2DtDP1yVz","requestRef":"d988a550-a45c-478c-9693-92f4d7fd4aeb","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4d98ce1c-cb60-4efc-ad3f-9dd00f44c970","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:31:31.477Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"4d98ce1c-cb60-4efc-ad3f-9dd00f44c970","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4shxv2rzTCMksq1ScnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X3fwSkQKNGF9DV44kCUTUA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5-plan && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ndef sub(s, old, new, label):\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, f\"{label}: expected 1 match, found {s.count(old)}\"\n    return s.replace(old, new)\n\np = \"docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\n\n# CX-2: auditable compaction record\ns = sub(s, \"(reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript | M | P1 |\",\n \"(reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`); the record names the covered event ids, the summary and where it is inserted, so a compaction can be audited and undone (reference: OpenHands `Condensation` event, docs 2026-11-15) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript; the record lists the covered ids | M | P1 |\", \"CX-2\")\n# CX-4: masking cannot remove evidence\ns = sub(s, \"Cline cached tool results) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves | S | P2 |\",\n \"Cline cached tool results). A masked output stays in the evidence store, and the independent reviewer's package (requirements, scope, diff, verifier receipts) does not depend on conversation context, so masking cannot remove evidence (read in `independent_review.ts`, 2026-11-15) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves; the reviewer package is identical before and after masking | S | P2 |\", \"CX-4\")\n# CX-7 + not-planned note after CX-6\ncx6 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| CX-6 |\")]\nassert len(cx6) == 1\ncx7 = (\"| CX-7 | Project instruction files: expand `@path` imports in `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md` and `.nexusrules` (today `getProjectRules` in `cli/src/git.ts` loads the first file raw, so a `CLAUDE.md` holding only `@AGENTS.md` puts that literal text in the prompt); bounded depth, cycle-safe, confined to the workspace, expanded only in a trusted workspace, and report which files were loaded (references: the Claude Code `@AGENTS.md` import convention, the usage guide of `agent-rules-books`) | `CLAUDE.md` containing `@AGENTS.md` loads the AGENTS content once; an import outside the workspace, or in an untrusted workspace, is not read; a cycle stops at the depth bound; the loaded-file list is shown | S | P2 |\")\nnote = (\"\\n\\nNot planned in the CX group: telling the model its remaining token budget (Anthropic context-management post, \\\"context awareness\\\"). No such notice exists today; with local models the context limit is an estimate, so a precise number could mislead. Revisit only with a measurement from MQ-8.\")\ns = sub(s, cx6[0], cx6[0] + \"\\n\" + cx7 + note, \"CX-6/CX-7\")\n# CS-11 after CS-10\ncs10 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| CS-10 |\")]\nassert len(cs10) == 1\ncs11 = (\"| CS-11 | Loop-pattern audit against OpenHands' stuck detector (docs, 2026-11-15: the same action and result 4 times, the same action erroring 3 times, 3 consecutive messages without progress, an A/B ping-pong for 6 cycles): replay each as a scripted transcript against CS-3, the non-progress recovery and DV-2; add detection only where a transcript runs unchecked (CS-3 thresholds stay deliberately higher, by call class) | one scripted transcript per pattern, each ending BLOCKED or recovered, or a recorded reason the existing guard already stops it | S | P2 |\")\ns = sub(s, cs10[0], cs10[0] + \"\\n\" + cs11, \"CS-10/CS-11\")\n# VC-9 after VC-8\nvc8 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| VC-8 |\")]\nassert len(vc8) == 1\nvc9 = (\"| VC-9 | Headless needs-input audit (Anthropic 2026 trends report, trend 4: agents that learn when to ask for help): list every path where a headless run needs an operator decision (steering that negates a requirement, a requirement marked blocked, a denied approval, a verification-file edit) and give each the same resumable outcome, a stable `needs_input` reason carrying the question and resumable with the answer; build only the missing glue | each path ends BLOCKED with a machine-readable question and resumes with an answer; no path guesses | S | P2 |\")\ns = sub(s, vc8[0], vc8[0] + \"\\n\" + vc9, \"VC-8/VC-9\")\n# VC-3: reference enables long runs (note, no priority change)\ns = sub(s, \"only when an authorised requirement names one |\",\n \"only when an authorised requirement names one (the Anthropic 2026 trends report's flagship long run, Rakuten's seven-hour single run at 99.9% numerical accuracy against a reference method, succeeded because a reference existed: the reference is what lets a long run stay autonomous. Raising this to P1 if MQ-1 shows reference-checkable tasks are common is an owner decision, not made here) |\", \"VC-3\")\n# MQ-8 after MQ-7\nmq7 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| MQ-7 |\")]\nassert len(mq7) == 1\nmq8 = (\"| MQ-8 | Long-horizon and A/B measurement (the Anthropic trends report, trend 3; `agent-rules-books` and the context-management post both report gains without a methodology): one multi-hour scripted task on a pinned repository with a resume part-way, and paired runs of the same scenarios with an instruction file, or tool-output clearing, on and off; report completion, claimed-done-but-wrong rate, tokens and wall time with Wilson 95% intervals | results JSON with the paired runs, model, gateway alias, Nexus version and seeds; no effect claimed unless the interval excludes zero (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2) | M | P2 (v1.2.2) |\")\ns = sub(s, mq7[0], mq7[0] + \"\\n\" + mq8, \"MQ-7/MQ-8\")\ns = sub(s, \"Dependencies: MQ-1 → MQ-2. MQ-3\", \"Dependencies: MQ-1 → MQ-2 → MQ-8. MQ-3\", \"MQ deps\")\n# sequencing\ns = sub(s, \"PC-3, DH-3, DH-4, DH-6.\", \"PC-3, DH-3, DH-4, DH-6, CX-7, CS-11, VC-9.\", \"phase 2\")\ns = sub(s, \"CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6.\", \"CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6, MQ-8 (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2).\", \"phase 3\")\n# section 9\ns = sub(s, \"OpenHands was not assessed and Claude Code was not read.\",\n \"OpenHands was read at documentation level on 2026-11-15 (architecture, security, condenser and stuck-detection pages; not its source), the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report was read in full (a vendor document with no methodology and customer-reported figures), and Claude Code was not read. Still missing: any measurement that instruction files or tool-output clearing change outcomes, and any record of a multi-hour run with a resume (MQ-8).\", \"section 9\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\n\ng = \"docs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md\"\nt = open(g).read()\nga35 = [l for l in t.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| GA-35 |\")]\nassert len(ga35) == 1\nrows = \"\\n\".join([\n \"| GA-37 | Project instruction files: `@path` imports are not expanded (`getProjectRules` loads the first file raw) | research 2026-11-15 (agent-rules-books) | P2 | CX-7 |\",\n \"| GA-38 | Loop patterns not audited against peers: A/B ping-pong and consecutive no-progress messages (OpenHands thresholds 4/3/3/6) | research 2026-11-15 (OpenHands docs) | P2 | CS-11 |\",\n \"| GA-39 | Headless \\\"needs an operator decision\\\" paths are not confirmed to share one resumable outcome | research 2026-11-15 (Anthropic trends report, trend 4) | P2 | VC-9 |\",\n \"| GA-40 | No measurement that instruction files or context clearing change outcomes; no multi-hour run with a resume | research 2026-11-15 (trends report, context-management post, agent-rules-books) | P2 | MQ-8 |\",\n])\nt = t.replace(ga35[0], ga35[0] + \"\\n\" + rows)\nopen(g, \"w\").write(t)\n\nv = \"docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md\"\nu = open(v).read()\nu = sub(u, \"(all four ACP servers use the same three-option permission request; opencode attaches the diff to the request so the user decides with the change in view)\",\n \"(all four ACP servers use the same three-option permission request; opencode attaches the diff to the request so the user decides with the change in view). The host side exists too: OpenHands' Agent Canvas drives Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI and OpenCode over ACP (docs, 2026-11-15), so an ACP server is what makes Nexus drivable by such hosts\", \"AC-1\")\nu = sub(u, \"no marketplace and no auto-update (reference: Gemini CLI `gemini-extension.json`, goose `.goose-plugin-install.json`).\",\n \"no marketplace and no auto-update (reference: Gemini CLI `gemini-extension.json`, goose `.goose-plugin-install.json`). Skills load on a declared trigger and are not always-on (references: OpenHands trigger-based skills, the on-demand-loading guidance of `agent-rules-books`).\", \"HK-2\")\nu = sub(u, \"| installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install | M | P1 |\",\n \"| installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install; a skill whose trigger did not fire adds nothing to the request (request-shape snapshot) | M | P1 |\", \"HK-2 accept\")\nu = sub(u, \"- **Not covered:**\",\n \"- **Research notes** (2026-11-15): the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report (read in full; a vendor document with no methodology, customer-reported figures) and OpenHands (documentation, not source) support three priorities here: VR-1 and VR-2 (the report's own evidence is that people delegate what is cheaply checkable, so verifiability is the delegation boundary), PA-1 (it names a view of concurrent agent sessions) and AC-1 (above). They are framing, not evidence about Nexus.\\n- **Not covered:**\", \"v1.3 evidence\")\nopen(v, \"w\").write(u)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | tail -5; node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Apply the lessons to the v1.2.1 plan, gap analysis and v1.3 plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3085,"cache_read_input_tokens":484951,"output_tokens":7765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3746},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3085,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7765,"cache_read_input_tokens":484951,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3085},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":18705,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01X3fwSkQKNGF9DV44kCUTUA":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5-plan && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ndef sub(s, old, new, label):\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, f\"{label}: expected 1 match, found {s.count(old)}\"\n    return s.replace(old, new)\n\np = \"docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\n\n# CX-2: auditable compaction record\ns = sub(s, \"(reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript | M | P1 |\",\n \"(reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`); the record names the covered event ids, the summary and where it is inserted, so a compaction can be audited and undone (reference: OpenHands `Condensation` event, docs 2026-11-15) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript; the record lists the covered ids | M | P1 |\", \"CX-2\")\n# CX-4: masking cannot remove evidence\ns = sub(s, \"Cline cached tool results) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves | S | P2 |\",\n \"Cline cached tool results). A masked output stays in the evidence store, and the independent reviewer's package (requirements, scope, diff, verifier receipts) does not depend on conversation context, so masking cannot remove evidence (read in `independent_review.ts`, 2026-11-15) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves; the reviewer package is identical before and after masking | S | P2 |\", \"CX-4\")\n# CX-7 + not-planned note after CX-6\ncx6 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| CX-6 |\")]\nassert len(cx6) == 1\ncx7 = (\"| CX-7 | Project instruction files: expand `@path` imports in `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md` and `.nexusrules` (today `getProjectRules` in `cli/src/git.ts` loads the first file raw, so a `CLAUDE.md` holding only `@AGENTS.md` puts that literal text in the prompt); bounded depth, cycle-safe, confined to the workspace, expanded only in a trusted workspace, and report which files were loaded (references: the Claude Code `@AGENTS.md` import convention, the usage guide of `agent-rules-books`) | `CLAUDE.md` containing `@AGENTS.md` loads the AGENTS content once; an import outside the workspace, or in an untrusted workspace, is not read; a cycle stops at the depth bound; the loaded-file list is shown | S | P2 |\")\nnote = (\"\\n\\nNot planned in the CX group: telling the model its remaining token budget (Anthropic context-management post, \\\"context awareness\\\"). No such notice exists today; with local models the context limit is an estimate, so a precise number could mislead. Revisit only with a measurement from MQ-8.\")\ns = sub(s, cx6[0], cx6[0] + \"\\n\" + cx7 + note, \"CX-6/CX-7\")\n# CS-11 after CS-10\ncs10 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| CS-10 |\")]\nassert len(cs10) == 1\ncs11 = (\"| CS-11 | Loop-pattern audit against OpenHands' stuck detector (docs, 2026-11-15: the same action and result 4 times, the same action erroring 3 times, 3 consecutive messages without progress, an A/B ping-pong for 6 cycles): replay each as a scripted transcript against CS-3, the non-progress recovery and DV-2; add detection only where a transcript runs unchecked (CS-3 thresholds stay deliberately higher, by call class) | one scripted transcript per pattern, each ending BLOCKED or recovered, or a recorded reason the existing guard already stops it | S | P2 |\")\ns = sub(s, cs10[0], cs10[0] + \"\\n\" + cs11, \"CS-10/CS-11\")\n# VC-9 after VC-8\nvc8 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| VC-8 |\")]\nassert len(vc8) == 1\nvc9 = (\"| VC-9 | Headless needs-input audit (Anthropic 2026 trends report, trend 4: agents that learn when to ask for help): list every path where a headless run needs an operator decision (steering that negates a requirement, a requirement marked blocked, a denied approval, a verification-file edit) and give each the same resumable outcome, a stable `needs_input` reason carrying the question and resumable with the answer; build only the missing glue | each path ends BLOCKED with a machine-readable question and resumes with an answer; no path guesses | S | P2 |\")\ns = sub(s, vc8[0], vc8[0] + \"\\n\" + vc9, \"VC-8/VC-9\")\n# VC-3: reference enables long runs (note, no priority change)\ns = sub(s, \"only when an authorised requirement names one |\",\n \"only when an authorised requirement names one (the Anthropic 2026 trends report's flagship long run, Rakuten's seven-hour single run at 99.9% numerical accuracy against a reference method, succeeded because a reference existed: the reference is what lets a long run stay autonomous. Raising this to P1 if MQ-1 shows reference-checkable tasks are common is an owner decision, not made here) |\", \"VC-3\")\n# MQ-8 after MQ-7\nmq7 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| MQ-7 |\")]\nassert len(mq7) == 1\nmq8 = (\"| MQ-8 | Long-horizon and A/B measurement (the Anthropic trends report, trend 3; `agent-rules-books` and the context-management post both report gains without a methodology): one multi-hour scripted task on a pinned repository with a resume part-way, and paired runs of the same scenarios with an instruction file, or tool-output clearing, on and off; report completion, claimed-done-but-wrong rate, tokens and wall time with Wilson 95% intervals | results JSON with the paired runs, model, gateway alias, Nexus version and seeds; no effect claimed unless the interval excludes zero (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2) | M | P2 (v1.2.2) |\")\ns = sub(s, mq7[0], mq7[0] + \"\\n\" + mq8, \"MQ-7/MQ-8\")\ns = sub(s, \"Dependencies: MQ-1 → MQ-2. MQ-3\", \"Dependencies: MQ-1 → MQ-2 → MQ-8. MQ-3\", \"MQ deps\")\n# sequencing\ns = sub(s, \"PC-3, DH-3, DH-4, DH-6.\", \"PC-3, DH-3, DH-4, DH-6, CX-7, CS-11, VC-9.\", \"phase 2\")\ns = sub(s, \"CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6.\", \"CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6, MQ-8 (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2).\", \"phase 3\")\n# section 9\ns = sub(s, \"OpenHands was not assessed and Claude Code was not read.\",\n \"OpenHands was read at documentation level on 2026-11-15 (architecture, security, condenser and stuck-detection pages; not its source), the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report was read in full (a vendor document with no methodology and customer-reported figures), and Claude Code was not read. Still missing: any measurement that instruction files or tool-output clearing change outcomes, and any record of a multi-hour run with a resume (MQ-8).\", \"section 9\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\n\ng = \"docs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md\"\nt = open(g).read()\nga35 = [l for l in t.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| GA-35 |\")]\nassert len(ga35) == 1\nrows = \"\\n\".join([\n \"| GA-37 | Project instruction files: `@path` imports are not expanded (`getProjectRules` loads the first file raw) | research 2026-11-15 (agent-rules-books) | P2 | CX-7 |\",\n \"| GA-38 | Loop patterns not audited against peers: A/B ping-pong and consecutive no-progress messages (OpenHands thresholds 4/3/3/6) | research 2026-11-15 (OpenHands docs) | P2 | CS-11 |\",\n \"| GA-39 | Headless \\\"needs an operator decision\\\" paths are not confirmed to share one resumable outcome | research 2026-11-15 (Anthropic trends report, trend 4) | P2 | VC-9 |\",\n \"| GA-40 | No measurement that instruction files or context clearing change outcomes; no multi-hour run with a resume | research 2026-11-15 (trends report, context-management post, agent-rules-books) | P2 | MQ-8 |\",\n])\nt = t.replace(ga35[0], ga35[0] + \"\\n\" + rows)\nopen(g, \"w\").write(t)\n\nv = \"docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md\"\nu = open(v).read()\nu = sub(u, \"(all four ACP servers use the same three-option permission request; opencode attaches the diff to the request so the user decides with the change in view)\",\n \"(all four ACP servers use the same three-option permission request; opencode attaches the diff to the request so the user decides with the change in view). The host side exists too: OpenHands' Agent Canvas drives Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI and OpenCode over ACP (docs, 2026-11-15), so an ACP server is what makes Nexus drivable by such hosts\", \"AC-1\")\nu = sub(u, \"no marketplace and no auto-update (reference: Gemini CLI `gemini-extension.json`, goose `.goose-plugin-install.json`).\",\n \"no marketplace and no auto-update (reference: Gemini CLI `gemini-extension.json`, goose `.goose-plugin-install.json`). Skills load on a declared trigger and are not always-on (references: OpenHands trigger-based skills, the on-demand-loading guidance of `agent-rules-books`).\", \"HK-2\")\nu = sub(u, \"| installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install | M | P1 |\",\n \"| installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install; a skill whose trigger did not fire adds nothing to the request (request-shape snapshot) | M | P1 |\", \"HK-2 accept\")\nu = sub(u, \"- **Not covered:**\",\n \"- **Research notes** (2026-11-15): the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report (read in full; a vendor document with no methodology, customer-reported figures) and OpenHands (documentation, not source) support three priorities here: VR-1 and VR-2 (the report's own evidence is that people delegate what is cheaply checkable, so verifiability is the delegation boundary), PA-1 (it names a view of concurrent agent sessions) and AC-1 (above). They are framing, not evidence about Nexus.\\n- **Not covered:**\", \"v1.3 evidence\")\nopen(v, \"w\").write(u)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | tail -5; node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Apply the lessons to the v1.2.1 plan, gap analysis and v1.3 plan"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch4shxYT2hMf2DtDP1yVz","requestRef":"d988a550-a45c-478c-9693-92f4d7fd4aeb","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"381168a6-baab-4e1a-a23a-03289059062e","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:31:50.200Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
