{"parentUuid":"82ca98f4-bc21-4a1c-9e46-8bf4900f24fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4sn7WL2TiCwPNanvVVY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Nothing in the plan has stale unit counts, and the CX table and its new note render fine. I'm committing this to #542's branch, which already includes the CX-5 work, and updating the PR title and description to match.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2055,"cache_read_input_tokens":496081,"output_tokens":1543,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1543,"cache_read_input_tokens":496081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2055},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4sn6rPFJ9mCwAHriksK","requestRef":"2db030aa-096b-45ad-9197-e86f155b7831","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1947395b-b8c7-4018-9300-4c01de609899","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:32:03.659Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"1947395b-b8c7-4018-9300-4c01de609899","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4sn7WL2TiCwPNanvVVY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013yuaUdxm8XaNhKKj7G2LMz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5-plan && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(plans): fold the 2026-11-15 research lessons into v1.2.1 and v1.3\n\nv1.2.1: CX-2 and CX-4 sharpened; new CX-7 (project instruction @import), CS-11 (loop-pattern audit), VC-9 (headless needs-input audit), MQ-8 (long-horizon and A/B measurement); VC-3 note on reference-enabled autonomy; sequencing, evidence-missing section and gaps GA-37..40 updated. v1.3: AC-1, HK-2 and evidence notes. The remaining-budget notice is recorded as not planned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q origin v1/cx5-plan-refine 2>&1 | tail -1; git rev-parse --short HEAD; cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr edit 542 --title \"docs(plans): CX-5 acceptance and the 2026-11-15 research lessons\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nTwo changes to the plan docs, docs only.\n\n**1. compaction-03 acceptance.** It already had an owner (v1.2.1 CX-5, GA-19). A read-only audit of \\`admitContext\\` sets its acceptance (walk every ladder rung and \\`compact --llm\\`; an over-limit ledger blocks, never truncated) and shows the default compaction writes no summary, so CX-3 is scoped to the summarising path.\n\n**2. Lessons from the research done 2026-11-15** (agent-rules-books, OpenHands docs, Anthropic's context-management post, Anthropic's 2026 Agentic Coding Trends Report, read in full):\n- v1.2.1 sharpened: CX-2 (compaction record names covered ids), CX-4 (masking cannot remove evidence; the reviewer package is independent of conversation context), VC-3 (a reference is what lets a long run stay autonomous; raising its priority is an owner decision, not made here).\n- v1.2.1 new, all P2: CX-7 (project instruction \\`@path\\` imports; today \\`getProjectRules\\` loads the first file raw), CS-11 (loop-pattern audit: ping-pong and no-progress messages), VC-9 (headless needs-input audit), MQ-8 (long-horizon and A/B measurement, v1.2.2, needs MQ-1 and MQ-2). Gaps GA-37 to GA-40. Sequencing and section 9 (evidence still missing) updated.\n- v1.3: AC-1 (hosts such as OpenHands' Agent Canvas drive agents over ACP), HK-2 (skills load on a declared trigger), and an evidence note tying VR-1, VR-2 and PA-1 to the report.\n- Recorded as **not planned**: telling the model its remaining token budget.\n\nAll sources are vendor or documentation-level; none is evidence about Nexus, and the plan says so.\n\n## Validation\n\nDocs only. Every edit was applied with an exact-match assertion; \\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` passes. Capacity: four new units land in Phase 2 and Phase 3 of a plan that already warns it cannot all be one release; anything not merged green slips under D12.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr view 542 --json title,state,headRefOid -q '\"#542 \"+.state+\" \"+.headRefOid[0:8]+\" | \"+.title'","description":"Commit, push, and update PR 542 title and body"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2055,"cache_read_input_tokens":496081,"output_tokens":1543,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1543,"cache_read_