{"parentUuid":"fab34669-9508-4a49-9b53-a6f54ef3aae0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4ufqt38bvsQQJvP7SfS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VDt9U6TiiGkNwSF8jY7VY5","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail","prompt":"What is this repository? Summarize its purpose, structure (directories/files), languages, key design ideas, any methodology or principles, notable features, license, maturity (stars, activity), and anything relevant to AI coding agents or agent harnesses. List top-level file/folder names."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26,"cache_read_input_tokens":509166,"output_tokens":175,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":175,"cache_read_input_tokens":509166,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":946,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VDt9U6TiiGkNwSF8jY7VY5":{"url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail","prompt":"What is this repository? Summarize its purpose, structure (directories/files), languages, key design ideas, any methodology or principles, notable features, license, maturity (stars, activity), and anything relevant to AI coding agents or agent harnesses. List top-level file/folder names."}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4ufqXxXDyoeP4vrxcVz","requestRef":"393faf51-4bde-4d5d-b6fe-26400624eb27","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4c5b76e-cba2-46e1-b485-9a2ba45b1213","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:56:50.706Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"e4c5b76e-cba2-46e1-b485-9a2ba45b1213","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"55e5c103-f7a2-454f-8998-dfa743d591d3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VDt9U6TiiGkNwSF8jY7VY5","type":"tool_result","content":"**Ponytail** (DietrichGebert/ponytail) is a prompt-based skill that tries to make AI coding agents write less code. Its tagline is \"Makes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev in the room.\" The core rule is to write only what the task needs, without cutting validation, error handling, security, or accessibility.\n\n**Purpose and key ideas**\n- Before writing code, the agent climbs a \"ladder\" of questions: does this need to exist, is it already in the codebase, does the standard library or a native platform feature cover it, is there an installed dependency, can it be one line? Only then does it write the minimum that works.\n- The ladder runs after the agent reads the code the change touches, so it is lazy about the solution, not about understanding the problem.\n- Logic with branches, loops, parsers, money, or security gets one small test. Replies end by noting what was skipped or unchecked.\n- Deferred work is marked with `shortcut:` comments, which `/ponytail-debt` collects into a ledger.\n\n**Structure**\n- Core: `skills/` (the main prompt, `SKILL.md`), `AGENTS.md` (a compact version for agents that read rules files), `INSTALL.md`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`.\n- Agent adapters: `.claude-plugin`, `.codex-plugin`, `.cursor/rules`, `.windsurf/rules`, `.clinerules`, `.kiro/steering`, `.opencode`, `.qoder-plugin`, `.qoder/rules`, `.devin-plugin`, `.grok-plugin`, `.kimi-plugin`, `.openclaw/skills`, `.agents`, `.github`.\n- Support: `assets`, `benchmarks`, `commands`, `docs`, `examples`, `hooks`, `i18n`, `pi-extension`, `scripts`, `tests`.\n- Config and metadata: `gemini-extension.json`, `opencode.json`, `package.json`, `plugin.json`, `plugin.yaml`, `__init__.py`, `after-install.md`, `.gitignore`.\n\nThe page doesn't render the language breakdown, so I can't confirm the languages. The config files suggest a mix of JSON, Markdown, and some Python and JavaScript.\n\n**Notable features**\n- Commands: `/ponytail` (set intensity or turn off), `/ponytail-review`, `/ponytail-audit`, `/ponytail-debt`, `/ponytail-gain`, `/ponytail-help`.\n- A Claude Code \"band\" above the prompt showing cost, tokens, agent time, code reuse, and test status, plus a local \"board\" page for history.\n- Installs as a plugin for Claude Code and Codex, or by copying `AGENTS.md` or `SKILL.md` into other agents.\n\n**Claimed results (self-reported, not independently verified on the page)**\n- Ponytail 5 is claimed to cut code by 53%, time by 41%, cost by 26%, and tokens by 45%, across 39 tasks run 5 times each.\n- It claims 98% of risky logic ships with a test, versus 68% without the skill.\n- The benchmark method is linked from the repo, and the page notes limits.\n\n**License:** MIT.\n\n**Maturity:** About 191k stars, 10.7k forks, 369 commits, 101 open issues, and 137 pull requests. It appears on Trendshift rankings.\n\n**Relevance to AI coding agents:** It is a portable instruction set rather than a library. It targets many agent harnesses (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Copilot, Kiro, Gemini, OpenCode, and others) and uses their native rules and hook mechanisms. The page warns users to install only from the official GitHub or npm sources."}]},"uuid":"f72a3144-e869-4295-a732-c12f863427f1","timestamp":"2026-11-15T14:57:03.652Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":367058,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Ponytail** (DietrichGebert/ponytail) is a prompt-based skill that tries to make AI coding agents write less code. Its tagline is \"Makes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev in the room.\" The core rule is to write only what the task needs, without cutting validation, error handling, security, or accessibility.\n\n**Purpose and key ideas**\n- Before writing code, the agent climbs a \"ladder\" of questions: does this need to exist, is it already in the codebase, does the standard library or a native platform feature cover it, is there an installed dependency, can it be one line? Only then does it write the minimum that works.\n- The ladder runs after the agent reads the code the change touches, so it is lazy about the solution, not about understanding the problem.\n- Logic with branches, loops, parsers, money, or security gets one small test. Replies end by noting what was skipped or unchecked.\n- Deferred work is marked with `shortcut:` comments, which `/ponytail-debt` collects into a ledger.\n\n**Structure**\n- Core: `skills/` (the main prompt, `SKILL.md`), `AGENTS.md` (a compact version for agents that read rules files), `INSTALL.md`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`.\n- Agent adapters: `.claude-plugin`, `.codex-plugin`, `.cursor/rules`, `.windsurf/rules`, `.clinerules`, `.kiro/steering`, `.opencode`, `.qoder-plugin`, `.qoder/rules`, `.devin-plugin`, `.grok-plugin`, `.kimi-plugin`, `.openclaw/skills`, `.agents`, `.github`.\n- Support: `assets`, `benchmarks`, `commands`, `docs`, `examples`, `hooks`, `i18n`, `pi-extension`, `scripts`, `tests`.\n- Config and metadata: `gemini-extension.json`, `opencode.json`, `package.json`, `plugin.json`, `plugin.yaml`, `__init__.py`, `after-install.md`, `.gitignore`.\n\nThe page doesn't render the language breakdown, so I can't confirm the languages. The config files suggest a mix of JSON, Markdown, and some Python and JavaScript.\n\n**Notable features**\n- Commands: `/ponytail` (set intensity or turn off), `/ponytail-review`, `/ponytail-audit`, `/ponytail-debt`, `/ponytail-gain`, `/ponytail-help`.\n- A Claude Code \"band\" above the prompt showing cost, tokens, agent time, code reuse, and test status, plus a local \"board\" page for history.\n- Installs as a plugin for Claude Code and Codex, or by copying `AGENTS.md` or `SKILL.md` into other agents.\n\n**Claimed results (self-reported, not independently verified on the page)**\n- Ponytail 5 is claimed to cut code by 53%, time by 41%, cost by 26%, and tokens by 45%, across 39 tasks run 5 times each.\n- It claims 98% of risky logic ships with a test, versus 68% without the skill.\n- The benchmark method is linked from the repo, and the page notes limits.\n\n**License:** MIT.\n\n**Maturity:** About 191k stars, 10.7k forks, 369 commits, 101 open issues, and 137 pull requests. It appears on Trendshift rankings.\n\n**Relevance to AI coding agents:** It is a portable instruction set rather than a library. It targets many agent harnesses (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Copilot, Kiro, Gemini, OpenCode, and others) and uses their native rules and hook mechanisms. The page warns users to install only from the official GitHub or npm sources.","durationMs":12763,"url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e4c5b76e-cba2-46e1-b485-9a2ba45b1213","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
