{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","prNumber":542,"prUrl":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/542","prRepository":"mikeholownych/nexus-code","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:06:59.390Z"}
{"parentUuid":"db990322-55c5-42e0-b8ae-e377306c3d95","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87039fef-1dca-42ea-9005-9e32f5e2f42c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01184sNxx4v4gXeaCewhtP4q","type":"tool_result","content":"All four primitives are typed questions sent in a `questions` dictionary. Each question has an ID, a `type`, and `instructions`. Answers come back under that ID, for example `response.answers[\"id\"].noul`.\n\n**Choice** (`type: choice`)\n- **Request:** `instructions` plus `criteria`, a map of option names to descriptions.\n- **Response:** `choice` (the selected option), `probabilities` (a distribution across every option), and `confidence`.\n- **Constraints:** Answers are limited to the options you supply. The page recommends listing the full set, since a Choice \"always picks one, even when nothing fits.\" For inputs that might fall outside the list, pair it with a Noul asking whether any option fits. No maximum option count is stated.\n\n**Score** (`type: score`)\n- **Request:** `instructions` plus `criteria`, an ordered list of levels.\n- **Response:** `score` (a position along the levels, which can fall between two), `legend` (the levels repeated by number), `probabilities` (a distribution across levels), and `confidence`.\n- **Constraints:** You define the levels, and each should have a clear meaning. No maximum level count is stated.\n\n**Noul** (`type: noul`)\n- **Request:** `instructions` plus an optional `criteria` that clarifies what yes and no mean.\n- **Response:** `noul`, the probability of yes, from 0 to 1. Near 1 is a strong yes, near 0 a strong no, and near 0.5 uncertain. It has no `confidence` field.\n- **Constraints:** It is for clean yes/no judgments. The page warns that a value of 0.5 means equal yes and no probability, not a medium level of something.\n\n**Box** (`type: box`)\n- **Request:** `id`, `type`, and `instructions`. The page does not describe any Box-specific request fields, so none are listed here.\n- **Response:** `box` with `top`, `bottom`, `left`, and `right`, each a fraction from 0 to 1 of the image's height or width, plus `confidence`.\n- **Constraints:** A Box always returns a location, even when the target is absent. Pair it with a Noul asking whether the target is in the image.\n\n**Across all types**\n- Every answer is constrained to your options or levels. The model returns a distribution over them, not free text.\n- Questions in one request are evaluated independently and in parallel.\n- There is no limit on the number of questions per request. The real limit is context size, covered in the models documentation."}]},"uuid":"9d5b066d-79e3-45e7-9aeb-32ef9ab32489","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:07:00.615Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":16368,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"All four primitives are typed questions sent in a `questions` dictionary. Each question has an ID, a `type`, and `instructions`. Answers come back under that ID, for example `response.answers[\"id\"].noul`.\n\n**Choice** (`type: choice`)\n- **Request:** `instructions` plus `criteria`, a map of option names to descriptions.\n- **Response:** `choice` (the selected option), `probabilities` (a distribution across every option), and `confidence`.\n- **Constraints:** Answers are limited to the options you supply. The page recommends listing the full set, since a Choice \"always picks one, even when nothing fits.\" For inputs that might fall outside the list, pair it with a Noul asking whether any option fits. No maximum option count is stated.\n\n**Score** (`type: score`)\n- **Request:** `instructions` plus `criteria`, an ordered list of levels.\n- **Response:** `score` (a position along the levels, which can fall between two), `legend` (the levels repeated by number), `probabilities` (a distribution across levels), and `confidence`.\n- **Constraints:** You define the levels, and each should have a clear meaning. No maximum level count is stated.\n\n**Noul** (`type: noul`)\n- **Request:** `instructions` plus an optional `criteria` that clarifies what yes and no mean.\n- **Response:** `noul`, the probability of yes, from 0 to 1. Near 1 is a strong yes, near 0 a strong no, and near 0.5 uncertain. It has no `confidence` field.\n- **Constraints:** It is for clean yes/no judgments. The page warns that a value of 0.5 means equal yes and no probability, not a medium level of something.\n\n**Box** (`type: box`)\n- **Request:** `id`, `type`, and `instructions`. The page does not describe any Box-specific request fields, so none are listed here.\n- **Response:** `box` with `top`, `bottom`, `left`, and `right`, each a fraction from 0 to 1 of the image's height or width, plus `confidence`.\n- **Constraints:** A Box always returns a location, even when the target is absent. Pair it with a Noul asking whether the target is in the image.\n\n**Across all types**\n- Every answer is constrained to your options or levels. The model returns a distribution over them, not free text.\n- Questions in one request are evaluated independently and in parallel.\n- There is no limit on the number of questions per request. The real limit is context size, covered in the models documentation.","durationMs":8213,"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/go/primitives.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db990322-55c5-42e0-b8ae-e377306c3d95","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
