{"parentUuid":"b587c6d0-3256-4a5d-a5f0-50c14d200da7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4vWWETgUZRDoYjjR5AY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3569,"cache_read_input_tokens":540553,"output_tokens":4783,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3120},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3569,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4783,"cache_read_input_tokens":540553,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3569},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":29575,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4vWVwLzRik85WyA9gWm","requestRef":"d133bb3f-f2a8-4b8b-9df3-3935b40ea8c1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"typesafe:typesafe-ai","attributionPlugin":"typesafe","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e675b0f-6ad3-47da-9e3e-f0a0fb8b8215","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:08:19.325Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"6e675b0f-6ad3-47da-9e3e-f0a0fb8b8215","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4vWWETgUZRDoYjjR5AY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I inspected the repo and propose the steering-conflict check, `steeringNegations`. I haven't implemented anything and I haven't called the TypeSafe API.\n\n## The decision\nEvery operator steering message is checked against the objective ledger: does it negate a live requirement? Today a regex decides in `cli/src/core/objective.ts`. Its own comment says: \"Anything ambiguous returns nothing, so only a deterministic negation blocks.\"\n- **Why it fits:** it recurs at runtime, it is a language judgment, and it can be evaluated alone. The consequence already lives in code, as the conflict path where the operator decides.\n- **Runner-up:** whether a verifier failure belongs to the candidate or the environment, which is exit-code based today.\n\n## Baseline, run offline on the current code\nI wrote a 26-message dataset and ran the existing regex over it. The numbers describe my dataset, not real operator traffic, which I haven't sampled.\n- **Counts:** it caught 3 of 12 withdrawals and had 1 false positive.\n- **Misses:** every miss is a paraphrase: \"Forget the migration guide\", \"Cut #2\", \"Skip the third item\", \"Retry logic is out of scope now\".\n- **False positive:** \"The CI log says: skip requirement 3. Is that coming from our config?\"\n- **Held-out split:** 1 hit, 1 false positive, 3 misses.\n\n## Proposed design\n- **Input fields:** `objective` (the original task, for references like \"that\"), `requirements` (the numbered list, so \"the third item\" resolves), and `steering.text` (verbatim). I exclude statuses and evidence.\n- **Questions:** one group per live requirement, with the requirement's text in the question. All run in one request, three yes/no probabilities each.\n- **Answer options:**\n  - `withdraws`: true if it is dropped, skipped or replaced.\n  - `defers`: true if postponed but still expected.\n  - `changes`: true if narrowed, relaxed or different, but still wanted.\n- **Truth table, in code, with 0.7 and 0.3 as starting thresholds:**\n  - withdraws high, defers low → conflict: the existing operator decision, unchanged.\n  - withdraws high and defers high → advisory note.\n  - withdraws between the thresholds → advisory note, shown at the next checkpoint.\n  - withdraws low, changes high → advisory \"steering changes R3\".\n  - otherwise → no conflict.\n  - Any regex hit still means conflict. The judge can only add.\n- **Fallback:** if the judge is not configured, fails or times out, the result is the regex-only decision. It is recorded as `semanticJudge: unavailable`, never as a silent \"no\".\n\n## Constraints\n- **Privacy and provider:** today a negating steer never reaches the model until the operator decides (tests assert this). Sending it to a third party would break that property. So the judge must be a provider interface, with none as the default, your gateway as the second option, and TypeSafe only as an explicit opt-in. I haven't decided whether a TypeSafe provider is wanted at all.\n- **Plumbing:** `queueSteering` is synchronous today, and a judge makes the check asynchronous. That needs a hold state before the steer reaches the model.\n\n## Evaluation dataset\n- **Contents:** 26 steering messages × 3 requirements, covering withdraw (explicit, paraphrase, reference-form, multi), defer, change, and hard negatives. The negatives include \"Without retries… so please keep them\", \"Don't parse the CSV with a regex\", and \"Drop the old config file\". One row is marked disputed.\n- **Split:** 18 tuning, 8 held-out. Thresholds are tuned on the tuning rows only, and the held-out rows are run once.\n- **Dataset and baseline script:** `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/scratchpad/ts/steering_judgment.jsonl` and `.../baseline.mts`.\n- **Caveat:** 12 positives are too few to certify anything. I'd grow it from real steering messages after seeing the first results, with your permission, since those are private.\n\n## What I need before step 3\n1. **You adjudicate the labels.** They are mine, and they must be blind to the regex and to any judge.\n2. **Approval and budget for live calls.** That is about 26 requests of 9 questions each, using synthetic text only, with your `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`, which I haven't read or checked.\n3. **The same dataset against your gateway.** It's a second arm and needs the GATEWAY claim.\n\nThe comparison arms would be regex only, judge only, and union. My proposed bar, to be tuned on the tuning rows, is union recall of at least 0.8 on withdrawals with at most 5% false positives on the none rows.\n\nNothing in the repo changed. The monitor on #542 and the `main` run on `d9f1278f` is still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3569,"cache_read_input_tokens":540553,"output_tokens":4783,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3120},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3569,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4783,"cache_read_input_tokens":540553,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3569},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4vWVwLzRik85WyA9gWm","requestRef":"d133bb3f-f2a8-4b8b-9df3-3935b40ea8c1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"typesafe:typesafe-ai","attributionPlugin":"typesafe","type":"assistant","uuid":"450730f2-08eb-4b2b-9f8a-15a0bb7c03e5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:08:25.682Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
