{"parentUuid":"937e7260-2c44-4728-a6c3-ea2ddc3091d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4vyDJjDi8bBzMqiRHup","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The TypeSafe arm is scored, and the gateway arm is still running (about 4 of 26 done). I'll report the full comparison when it finishes. I'm acting on your message: the key was in `~/.zshrc`, and I read that one variable and used it only for that process.\n\n**TypeSafe arm** (`jev-1.14.0`, 26 requests, all HTTP 200, 34,675 input tokens, roughly $0.0015). The key was never printed or written to a file. Synthetic text only.\n\n| Arm | Withdrawals caught (12) | False positives (66 non-withdrawals) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Current regex | 3 | 1 |\n| TypeSafe `withdraws` question | 12 | 0 |\n| Regex or TypeSafe | 12 | 1 (the regex's) |\n\n- **Intervals:** recall is 1.00 (95% interval 0.76–1.00) and the false-positive rate is 0 of 66 (upper bound 0.06). On the held-out rows alone, with only 4 positives, the recall interval is 0.51–1.00, which certifies nothing.\n- **A real regex false positive is fixed:** TypeSafe correctly rejected \"The CI log says: skip requirement 3…\", which the regex wrongly flags. The union keeps that false positive, because any regex hit still counts as a conflict.\n- **The disputed row (#26)** came back as a withdrawal, matching my label.\n- **The weak question is `changes`.** It scores 0.89–0.94 on \"Also make the retry logic log each attempt\", \"Make sure the migration guide mentions the new flag\" and \"Don't parse the CSV with a regex\". Part of that is my own ambiguous definition of \"change\", not model error. It should stay informational only, and I'd rewrite it before relying on it.\n\n**Caveats:** I wrote both the dataset and the questions in the same session. The wording was not tuned (one run, no iteration), but its criteria echo categories I knew were in the set, such as \"restricts how it is done\". This is a pilot and not a qualification, and the dataset needs to grow from real steering messages if you approve that.\n\n**Gateway arm:** under the claim since 15:10:55Z; it is slower than I estimated. I'll check the claim log for release when it completes.\n\n**#542:** its one failure was `eval_integrity` (\"more than 128 disjoint system roots\"). The scanner's enumeration was killed by SIGTERM on a loaded runner, so this is environmental, and a docs-only PR can't cause it. I re-ran only that job and a watch is on it. The test's flakiness under load is worth a note in the plan.\n\nNothing is implemented, and nothing in the repo changed. If you want it kept, I can add the dataset, shared questions and scorer under `eval/` in a PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2609,"cache_read_input_tokens":579202,"output_tokens":927,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2609,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":579202,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2609},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4vyCzt7gq4Fo4f8nr8w","requestRef":"91dcf931-c1c6-4f38-adc2-a63785bba8f9","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"78c60902-4c2f-4cc9-8cf2-c73a84bf594a","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:13:58.562Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473