{"parentUuid":"fb959754-a9b1-47e7-8eb0-a469a40b7bc2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4wetE8VUMsmxHoGadpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3785,"cache_read_input_tokens":587748,"output_tokens":1651,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":629},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3785,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1651,"cache_read_input_tokens":587748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3785},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10777,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch4wesvGnZTUqhGpUELZy","requestRef":"3b084be8-c0e8-4285-9c1c-f5efa1fb0ac1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9d59e36-0358-4b35-b350-0cb4cb0d0cdf","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:23:01.094Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"b9d59e36-0358-4b35-b350-0cb4cb0d0cdf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4wetE8VUMsmxHoGadpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The evaluation is complete for what could run. Both judges beat the regex on this dataset, and the one gap is the gateway arm's row #26, which the gateway being down made impossible to run.\n\n| Arm | Withdrawals caught | False positives | 95% interval on recall |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Current regex | 3 of 12 | 1 of 66 | 0.09–0.53 |\n| TypeSafe (`jev-1.14.0`) | 12 of 12 | 0 of 66 | 0.76–1.00 |\n| Gateway (`engineering/deep`, yes/no) | 11 of 11 | 0 of 64 | 0.74–1.00 |\n| Regex or either judge | all | 1 (the regex's) | same as the judge |\n\n- **The two judges agree.** They gave the same answer on every row where both ran. They fix all 8 paraphrase and reference-form misses (\"Forget the migration guide\", \"Cut #2\", \"Skip the third item\"), and both reject the regex's false positive about the CI log.\n- **Gateway arm:** 25 of 26 rows ran. #26, the disputed row, failed with `ECONNREFUSED`. The gateway at `10.0.8.5:8443` stopped accepting connections right after request 25, and my three re-runs hit the same refusal. I'm not retrying in a loop. The failed record is kept, and the claim was released each time. The claim log labels these runs \"pass\" because it records the wrapper's exit code and not whether the requests succeeded.\n- **Latency and calibration:** the gateway median was about 17 seconds per message (maximum 115), which is too slow for a synchronous steering path, and it gives only yes/no with no probability to threshold. TypeSafe gives probabilities and was much faster, though I didn't record exact timings.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Small dataset:** with 12 positives, only 3–4 of them held out, these are pilot numbers. They show the regex's blind spot and that judges close it, but they don't certify a rate.\n- **Labels and wording:** I wrote the dataset and the wording in the same session, and you approved the labels as written.\n- **`changes` question:** it is weak (precision 0.50 on both judges), partly because \"change\" is ambiguously defined. It stays informational.\n- **Truth table repaired:** conflict if the regex hits or `withdraws` ≥ 0.7, whatever `defers` says, because my first table had a hole that would have downgraded a real withdrawal.\n\n**Privacy:** the gateway judge reaches the same quality without adding a third-party data boundary, so I'd make it the default judge candidate and keep TypeSafe as an explicit opt-in. That is tentative, on 12 positives.\n\n**Your decision:** I haven't implemented anything. I recommend two steps, in order:\n1. Commit the dataset, shared questions and scorer under `eval/` in a PR.\n2. Then implement the judge interface, with the gateway as default and TypeSafe opt-in.\n\nDo you want step 1 now? Other state: #542's re-run is still being watched."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3785,"cache_read_input_tokens":587748,"output_tokens":1651,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":629},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3785,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1651,"cache_read_input_tokens":587748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3785},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4wesvGnZTUqhGpUELZy","requestRef":"3b084be8-c0e8-4285-9c1c-f5efa1fb0ac1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"84c69f7b-7acc-4b69-9469-3437d6a3608d","time