{"parentUuid":"08a62a2e-bfa7-4bd5-81e3-369d67822951","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54RCasGqa53Uy4EBjMH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012r1kBAWNtEk5M9qKBRz455","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"v1.2.1 CX-5 compaction invariant","prompt":"You are implementing unit CX-5 of the Nexus Code v1.2.1 plan, test-first, in its own git worktree. Repo: /home/mike/nexus-code (checkout is stale; work ONLY in your own worktree). Read AGENTS.md and docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md (row CX-5, and CX-3 for scope) on origin/main first.\n\nGOAL (CX-5): after every compaction, every gating requirement of the pinned objective ledger (`seedRequirements` in cli/src/core/objective.ts, `gatingRequirements`) is present in the request sent to the model, or the turn blocks with a named reason. This owns CERI scenario `compaction-03` (post-compaction check that every gating requirement is present); the scenario is currently pending in the CERI `semantic_integrity` domain (cli/src/ceri/, cli/test/ceri_semantic_integrity.test.ts): make it active.\nCoverage the acceptance requires: (1) a test that walks EVERY rung of the compaction ladder in `admitContext` (cli/src/agent.ts, ~line 4113: recentTurns lists [2,1,0] / [1,0] against detail budgets [6000,3000,1200,400,0] / [3000,1200,400,0]) and asserts the ledger survives each rung; (2) the `compact --llm` path (find it: grep compact in cli/src/slash/session_commands.ts and cli/src/session.ts); (3) an over-limit ledger (bigger than the context budget) is omitted whole and the turn BLOCKS with a named reason (use the existing outcome/reason vocabulary in cli/src/core/turn.ts), never truncated; (4) CERI scenario compaction-03 active and passing. First verify by reading code whether the ledger is actually carried inside `messages` or injected separately per request (the v1.2.0 audit found no requirement loss, so this may be a guard plus a blocking path; do not invent a bug).\n\nPROCESS (mandatory):\n- `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git fetch origin && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5 -b v1/cx5-compaction-invariant origin/main`, then `ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cli/node_modules /home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5/cli/node_modules` (pc2 has an installed node_modules).\n- Write failing tests first, then the minimal code. Run tests with a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<file>.test.ts`. Any test that builds an AutonomousAgent, RustCoreBridge or gateway must `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"` and shut them down. Run the affected files on Node 22 AND 24 (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin` and `.../v24.21.0/bin` first on PATH). `npm --prefix cli run build` (tsc) must be clean. Some tests fail on this host for host reasons (unbuilt cli/dist, stray /tmp/.git); compare against origin/main for any file you doubt before calling it a defect, and CI is the arbiter.\n- XERJ reference coding: the local XERJ node (`systemctl --user is-active xerj`, docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md) — query for how peers verify state after compaction (e.g. Gemini CLI chatCompressionService, Codex retain_across_windows, Cline) and record queries and what you took/rejected in the PR body \"Reference coding\" section.\n- Rules: chain shell commands with &&; never `git stash`; never touch ~/.config/nexus/config.env or any credential file; never use the gateway or any inference (not needed); do not merge, tag, publish, or force-push. Commit with the trailer line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Push your branch and open a PR to main with `gh pr create` using the template sections of .github/pull_request_template.md; END the PR body with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. CAPTURE the PR number from the `gh pr create` output (or `gh pr list --head <branch>`); do not guess it.\n- Keep the change minimal and touch only what you must. Preserve existing comments.\n\nREPORT BACK (concise): PR number and head SHA, files changed, what you found about where the ledger lives, test results with pass/fail TOTALS read from the output, Node 22 and 24 results, anything you could not verify."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":608095,"output_tokens":6899,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2208},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":6899,"cache_read_input_tokens":608095,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10738,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012r1kBAWNtEk5M9qKBRz455":{"description":"v1.2.1 CX-5 compaction invariant","prompt":"You are implementing unit CX-5 of the Nexus Code v1.2.1 plan, test-first, in its own git worktree. Repo: /home/mike/nexus-code (checkout is stale; work ONLY in your own worktree). Read AGENTS.md and docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md (row CX-5, and CX-3 for scope) on origin/main first.\n\nGOAL (CX-5): after every compaction, every gating requirement of the pinned objective ledger (`seedRequirements` in cli/src/core/objective.ts, `gatingRequirements`) is present in the request sent to the model, or the turn blocks with a named reason. This owns CERI scenario `compaction-03` (post-compaction check that every gating requirement is present); the scenario is currently