{"parentUuid":"0cb0cfd1-72d7-45d9-b23a-6a213ea7b22a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54RCasGqa53Uy4EBjMH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018QLsN9Pw8c6D7u7gxMgXVL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"v1.2.1 VC-5 verified re-check on resume","prompt":"You are implementing unit VC-5 of the Nexus Code v1.2.1 plan, test-first, in its own git worktree. Repo: /home/mike/nexus-code (checkout is stale; work ONLY in your own worktree). Read AGENTS.md and docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md (row VC-5) and docs/releases/v1.2.0.md \"Known limitations\" on origin/main first.\n\nGOAL (VC-5): (a) re-check `verified` on resume: a requirement marked verified must be demoted when the candidate identity differs on resume (workspace edited since verification); (b) persist the \"unbound-pass\" marker so a resumed task does not hit the \"no matching pre-change baseline\" refusal and completes as REGRESSION_FREE (v1.2.0 limitation: after a restart following an unbound-verifier pass the baseline is memory-only, so the resumed task is refused and only a fresh task recovers). Find the relevant code: grep in cli/src for `verified`, `requirementDone`, `REGRESSION_FREE`, `unbound`, `baseline`, `candidate identity` (cli/src/core/objective.ts, cli/src/core/verification*.ts, cli/src/agent.ts, cli/src/core/turn.ts, cli/src/core/receipts*). Acceptance: resume test: an edited workspace demotes `verified`; resume after an unbound pass completes as REGRESSION_FREE.\n\nPROCESS (mandatory):\n- `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git fetch origin && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/vc5 -b v1/vc5-resume-verified origin/main`, then `ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cli/node_modules /home/mike/nexus-wt/vc5/cli/node_modules`.\n- Write failing tests first, then the minimal code. Run tests with a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<file>.test.ts`. Any test that builds an AutonomousAgent, RustCoreBridge or gateway must `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"` and shut them down. Run affected files on Node 22 AND 24 (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin` and `.../v24.21.0/bin` first on PATH). `npm --prefix cli run build` (tsc) must be clean. Some tests fail on this host for host reasons (unbuilt cli/dist, stray /tmp/.git); compare against origin/main for any file you doubt, CI is the arbiter.\n- Candidate identity must use the existing mechanism (find how the candidate identity / worktree digest is computed for receipts; do not invent a second one). Persisted markers need integrity consideration consistent with the existing durable-file helpers (cli/src/core/durable_file.ts).\n- XERJ reference coding: query the local XERJ node (`systemctl --user is-active xerj`, docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md) for how peers invalidate stale state on resume (e.g. opencode, Cline, Codex rollout/resume) and record queries and what you took/rejected in the PR body \"Reference coding\" section.\n- Rules: chain shell commands with &&; never `git stash`; never touch ~/.config/nexus/config.env or credential files; no inference/gateway use; do not merge, tag, publish or force-push. Commit trailer: `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Push your branch, open a PR to main with `gh pr create` using .github/pull_request_template.md sections, END the body with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. CAPTURE the PR number from the `gh pr create` output (or `gh pr list --head <branch>`); do not guess it.\n- Minimal change; preserve existing comments.\n\nREPORT BACK (concise): PR number and head SHA, files changed, design (what identity, where persisted), test results with pass/fail TOTALS read from output, Node 22 and 24 results, anything not verified."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":60