{"parentUuid":"c2fd3d9f-7594-4419-89c0-f216720ea6cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54aBxew1VAfvF4QMzep","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The in-repo scorer reproduces the scratchpad numbers exactly. Now the README (with the results and their caveats, stated plainly) and the validation test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5031,"cache_read_input_tokens":620635,"output_tokens":4201,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":283},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4201,"cache_read_input_tokens":620635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5031},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch54aBSu4mCa5kVTZdUGp","requestRef":"0d1ed9de-35ba-4a6d-9b58-b8268124f139","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"5911c919-a2a2-486b-ab97-ad9b7e6b487f","timestamp":"2026-11-15T16:53:36.861Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"5911c919-a2a2-486b-ab97-ad9b7e6b487f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54aBxew1VAfvF4QMzep","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015osWw7WSMG1usuxGJry1R7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval/docs/research/steering-judgment && cd $D && cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Steering judgment: an independent evaluation (research record, 2026-11-15)\n\n**Status: research only. No product behaviour changed.** The steering-conflict check (`steeringNegations` in `cli/src/core/objective.ts`) is still the regex described in v1.2.0 SI-3. This directory records an evaluation of replacing part of it with a language judgment, so the decision to build it can rest on evidence.\n\n## The decision under test\n\nEvery operator steering message is checked against the objective ledger: does it negate a live requirement? Today a regex decides, and its own comment says \"Anything ambiguous returns nothing, so only a deterministic negation blocks.\" That trades recall for precision: paraphrases such as \"Forget the migration guide\" or \"Cut #2\" pass unseen.\n\n## Design (judgments from a model, the decision in code)\n\n- **State** (named fields): `objective`, `requirements` (the numbered list, so \"the third item\" resolves) and `steering.text` (verbatim). Statuses and evidence are left out.\n- **Questions**, one group per live requirement, all in one request, each a yes/no probability (`questions.mjs`, the single source of the wording): `withdraws` (dropped, skipped or replaced), `defers` (postponed, still expected), `changes` (narrowed, relaxed or different, still wanted).\n- **Decision, in code:** conflict (the existing operator decision, unchanged) if the regex hits **or** `withdraws` >= 0.7, whatever `defers` says. `withdraws` between 0.3 and 0.7: advisory note, no block. `defers` and `changes` only add a note to what the operator sees. The first draft of this table let a high `defers` downgrade a real withdrawal and left a cell undefined; the data exposed that, and this is the repaired rule. Silently dropping a requirement is the failure, an extra prompt is cheap.\n- **Fallback:** a judge that is not configured, errors or times out leaves the regex-only decision and records `semanticJudge: unavailable`; it is never recorded as \"no negation\".\n- **Data boundary:** the steer of a negating message is held from the model until the operator decides (SI-3 tests assert this), so a judge must not send it to a third party by default. Judges are providers: none (default), the configured gateway, or an explicit opt-in.\n\n## Dataset\n\n`dataset.jsonl`: 26 synthetic steering messages against three requirements (`1. Parse the CSV input`, `2. Add retry logic to the uploader`, `3. Write the migration guide`), so 78 (message, requirement) judgments. Strata: explicit and paraphrased withdrawals, reference forms (\"Cut #2\", \"the third item\"), multi-requirement, deferral, change, and hard negatives (supports, extends, question, a negator word, a restricted method, reported speech, another object). 18 rows are `tune`, 8 are `heldout`; thresholds are set on `tune` only and `heldout` is run once. One row is `disputed`. The labels were written by the agent from the steering text alone, before any judge output existed, and approved by the owner on 2026-11-15. **All text is synthetic: no operator or repository data was sent anywhere.**\n\n## Results (2026-11-15; raw responses in `results/2026-11-15/`, scorer output in `score.txt`)\n\nWithdrawal label (12 true withdrawals among 78 judgments), 95% Wilson intervals:\n\n| Arm | Caught | False positives | Recall interval |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Current regex | 3 of 12 | 1 of 66 | 0.09-0.53 |\n| TypeSafe `jev-1.14.0` | 12 of 12 | 0 of 66 | 0.76-1.00 |\n| Gateway `engineering/deep` (yes/no) | 11 of 11 | 0 of 64 | 0.74-1.00 |\n| Regex or a judge | all | 1 (the regex's) | as the judge |\n\n- Both judges agreed on every row where both ran. The only false positive left in the union is the regex's own, on \"The CI log says: skip requirement 3. Is that coming from our config?\" (reported speech).\n- On `withdraws` the lowest score on a true withdrawal was 0.88 and the highest on anything else 0.25 (TypeSafe), so the 0.7 and 0.3 thresholds sat inside a wide gap.\n- The `changes` question is weak (precision 0.50 on both judges): it fires on \"Also make the retry logic log each attempt\" and \"Make sure the migration guide mentions the new flag\". Part of that is an ambiguous definition of \"change\", not model error. It stays informational.\n- **Gateway row #26 is missing**, not a \"no\": the gateway refused connections (`ECONNREFUSED`) as request 25 finished and again on re-runs; both failed records are kept. It counts toward `MISSING` in the scorer.\n- The gateway took a median of about 17 s per message (maximum 115 s), too slow for a synchronous steering path.\n\n## Limits\n\n- 12 positives are too few to certify a rate; on the held-out rows alone the recall interval is 0.51-1.00 (TypeSafe) and 0.44-1.00 (gateway).\n- The agent wrote both the dataset and the question wording in one session. The wording was not tuned (one run, no iteration), but its criteria echo categories that were known to be in the set.\n- The regex's low recall is partly by design (precision first), and this dataset is deliberately rich in paraphrases. It is not a sample of real steering traffic, which has not been measured.\n- Next, if built: grow the set from real steering messages (with the owner's consent, since they are private), re-label blind, and re-run once on a fresh held-out split.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n- Offline, no network: `cd cli && node --import tsx ../docs/research/steering-judgment/score.mts <results-dir>` scores the regex baseline and whichever judge arms the results directory holds. Without results it prints only the regex arm.\n- TypeSafe arm (opt-in; sends synthetic text to a third party): `TYPESAFE_API_KEY=... node run_typesafe.mjs <out-dir>`; add `--dry-run` to write the exact payloads and send nothing. The model is pinned to `jev-1.14.0`.\n- Gateway arm (holds the GATEWAY claim, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`): `NEXUS_GATEWAY_KEY=... NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=... node run_gateway.mjs <out-dir> [--only <id>]`. Keys come from the environment and are never written.\nEOF\ncd /home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval/cli && node --import tsx ../docs/research/steering-judgment/score.mts ../docs/research/steering-judgment/results/2026-11-15 > ../docs/research/steering-judgment/results/2026-11-15/score.txt 2>&1; wc -l ../docs/research/steering-judgment/results/2026-11-15/score.txt; cat > test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts <<'EOF'\n/**\n * The steering-judgment research dataset (docs/research/steering-judgment) is well formed: unique ids, known splits and\n * labels, a label for each of the three requirements, and a held-out split that is not empty. No network, no model.\n */\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst dir = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"../../docs/research/steering-judgment\");\nconst rows = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, \"dataset.jsonl\"), \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\nconst LABELS = new Set([\"withdraws\", \"defers\", \"changes\", \"none\"]);\n\ntest(\"the steering-judgment dataset is well formed\", () => {\n  assert.ok(rows.length >= 20);\n  assert.equal(new Set(rows.map((r) => r.id)).size, rows.length, \"ids are unique\");\n  for (const row of rows) {\n    assert.ok(row.split === \"tune\" || row.split === \"heldout\", `row ${row.id} has a known split`);\n    assert.ok(typeof row.steering === \"string\" && row.steering.trim().length > 0, `row ${row.id} has a steering message`);\n    assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(row.expected).sort(), [\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\"], `row ${row.id} labels all three requirements`);\n    for (const label of Object.values(row.expected)) assert.ok(LABELS.has(label as string), `row ${row.id} uses a known label`);\n  }\n  assert.ok(rows.some((r) => r.split === \"heldout\"), \"a held-out split exists\");\n  assert.ok(rows.some((r) => Object.values(r.expected).includes(\"withdraws\")), \"withdrawals are present\");\n  assert.ok(rows.some((r) => Object.values(r.expected).every((l) => l === \"none\")), \"hard negatives are present\");\n});\n\ntest(\"the shared question module yields one withdraws, defers and changes question per requirement\", async () => {\n  const { questionsFor, REQUIREMENTS } = await import(path.join(dir, \"questions.mjs\"));\n  const questions = questionsFor();\n  assert.equal(Object.keys(questions).length, REQUIREMENTS.length * 3);\n  for (const requirement of REQUIREMENTS) for (const kind of [\"withdraws\", \"defers\", \"changes\"]) {\n    const question = questions[`r${requirement.number}.${kind}`];\n    assert.equal(question.type, \"noul\");\n    assert.ok(question.instructions.includes(\"`steering.text`\"), \"the question names the state path it reads\");\n    assert.ok(question.instructions.includes(requirement.text), \"the question names its requirement\");\n  }\n});\nEOF\nH=$(mktemp -d); HOME=$H node --import tsx --test test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts 2>&1 | sed 's/\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]//g' | awk '/^ℹ (tests|pass|fail) /{printf \"%s \", $0} END{print \"\"}'; (cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval && ~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin/node --version >/dev/null && cd cli && HOME=$H PATH=~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin:$PATH node --import tsx --test test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts 2>&1 | sed 's/\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]//g' | awk '/^# (tests|pass|fail) |^ℹ (tests|pass|fail) /{printf \"%s \", $0} END{print \" (node22)\"}')","description":"Write README and the dataset validation test; regenerate scorer output; run on Node 24 and 22","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5031,"cache_read_input_tokens":620635,"output_tokens":4201,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":283},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4201,"cache_read_input_tokens":620635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5031},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":23169,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015osWw7WSMG1usuxGJry1R7":{"command":"D=/home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval/docs/research/steering-judgment && cd $D && cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Steering judgment: an independent evaluation (research record, 2026-11-15)\n\n**Status: research only. No product behaviour changed.** The steering-conflict check (`steeringNegations` in `cli/src/core/objective.ts`) is still the regex described in v1.2.0 SI-3. This directory records an evaluation of replacing part of it with a language judgment, so the decision to build it can rest on evidence.\n\n## The decision under test\n\nEvery operator steering message is checked against the objective ledger: does it negate a live requirement? Today a regex decides, and its own comment says \"Anything ambiguous returns nothing, so only a deterministic negation blocks.\" That trades recall for precision: paraphrases such as \"Forget the migration guide\" or \"Cut #2\" pass unseen.\n\n## Design (judgments from a model, the decision in code)\n\n- **State** (named fields): `objective`, `requirements` (the numbered list, so \"the third item\" resolves) and `steering.text` (verbatim). Statuses and evidence are left out.\n- **Questions**, one group per live requirement, all in one request, each a yes/no probability (`questions.mjs`, the single source of the wording): `withdraws` (dropped, skipped or replaced), `defers` (postponed, still expected), `changes` (narrowed, relaxed or different, still wanted).\n- **Decision, in code:** conflict (the existing operator decision, unchanged) if the regex hits **or** `withdraws` >= 0.7, whatever `defers` says. `withdraws` between 0.3 and 0.7: advisory note, no block. `defers` and `changes` only add a note to what the operator sees. The first draft of this table let a high `defers` downgrade a real withdrawal and left a cell undefined; the data exposed that, and this is the repaired rule. Silently dropping a requirement is the failure, an extra prompt is cheap.\n- **Fallback:** a judge that is not configured, errors or times out leaves the regex-only decision and records `semanticJudge: unavailable`; it is never recorded as \"no negation\".\n- **Data boundary:** the steer of a negating message is held from the model until the operator decides (SI-3 tests assert this), so a judge must not send it to a third party by default. Judges are providers: none (default), the configured gateway, or an explicit opt-in.\n\n## Dataset\n\n`dataset.jsonl`: 26 synthetic steering messages against three requirements (`1. Parse the CSV input`, `2. Add retry logic to the uploader`, `3. Write the migration guide`), so 78 (message, requirement) judgments. Strata: explicit and paraphrased withdrawals, reference forms (\"Cut #2\", \"the third item\"), multi-requirement, deferral, change, and hard negatives (supports, extends, question, a negator word, a restricted method, reported speech, another object). 18 rows are `tune`, 8 are `heldout`; thresholds are set on `tune` only and `heldout` is run once. One row is `disputed`. The labels were written by the agent from the steering text alone, before any judge output existed, and approved by the owner on 2026-11-15. **All text is synthetic: no operator or repository data was sent anywhere.**\n\n## Results (2026-11-15; raw responses in `results/2026-11-15/`, scorer output in `score.txt`)\n\nWithdrawal label (12 true withdrawals among 78 judgments), 95% Wilson intervals:\n\n| Arm | Caught | False positives | Recall interval |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Current regex | 3 of 12 | 1 of 66 | 0.09-0.53 |\n| TypeSafe `jev-1.14.0` | 12 of 12 | 0 of 66 | 0.76-1.00 |\n| Gateway `engineering/deep` (yes/no) | 11 of 11 | 0 of 64 | 0.74-1.00 |\n| Regex or a judge | all | 1 (the regex's) | as the judge |\n\n- Both judges agreed on every row where both ran. The only false positive left in the union is the regex's own, on \"The CI log says: skip requirement 3. Is that coming from our config?\" (reported speech).\n- On `withdraws` the lowest score on a true withdrawal was 0.88 and the highest on anything else 0.25 (TypeSafe), so the 0.7 and 0.3 thresholds sat inside a wide gap.\n- The `changes` question is weak (precision 0.50 on both judges): it fires on \"Also make the retry logic log each attempt\" and \"Make sure the migration guide mentions the new flag\". Part of that is an ambiguous definition of \"change\", not model error. It stays informational.\n- **Gateway row #26 is missing**, not a \"no\": the gateway refused connections (`ECONNREFUSED`) as request 25 finished and again on re-runs; both failed records are kept. It counts toward `MISSING` in the scorer.\n- The gateway took a median of about 17 s per message (maximum 115 s), too slow for a synchronous steering path.\n\n## Limits\n\n- 12 positives are too few to certify a rate; on the held-out rows alone the recall interval is 0.51-1.00 (TypeSafe) and 0.44-1.00 (gateway).\n- The agent wrote both the dataset and the question wording in one session. The wording was not tuned (one run, no iteration), but its criteria echo categories that were known to be in the set.\n- The regex's low recall is partly by design (precision first), and this dataset is deliberately rich in paraphrases. It is not a sample of real steering traffic, which has not been measured.\n- Next, if built: grow the set from real steering messages (with the owner's consent, since they are private), re-label blind, and re-run once on a fresh held-out split.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n- Offline, no network: `cd cli && node --import tsx ../docs/research/steering-judgment/score.mts <results-dir>` scores the regex baseline and whichever judge arms the results directory holds. Without results it prints only the regex arm.\n- TypeSafe arm (opt-in; sends synthetic text to a third party): `TYPESAFE_API_KEY=... node run_typesafe.mjs <out-dir>`; add `--dry-run` to write the exact payloads and send nothing. The model is pinned to `jev-1.14.0`.\n- Gateway arm (holds the GATEWAY claim, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`): `NEXUS_GATEWAY_KEY=... NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=... node run_gateway.mjs <out-dir> [--only <id>]`. Keys come from the environment and are never written.\nEOF\ncd /home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval/cli && node --import tsx ../docs/research/steering-judgment/score.mts ../docs/research/steering-judgment/results/2026-11-15 > ../docs/research/steering-judgment/results/2026-11-15/score.txt 2>&1; wc -l ../docs/research/steering-judgment/results/2026-11-15/score.txt; cat > test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts <<'EOF'\n/**\n * The steering-judgment research dataset (docs/research/steering-judgment) is well formed: unique ids, known splits and\n * labels, a label for each of the three requirements, and a held-out split that is not empty. No network, no model.\n */\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst dir = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"../../docs/research/steering-judgment\");\nconst rows = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, \"dataset.jsonl\"), \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\nconst LABELS = new Set([\"withdraws\", \"defers\", \"changes\", \"none\"]);\n\ntest(\"the steering-judgment dataset is well formed\", () => {\n  assert.ok(rows.length >= 20);\n  assert.equal(new Set(rows.map((r) => r.id)).size, rows.length, \"ids are unique\");\n  for (const row of rows) {\n    assert.ok(row.split === \"tune\" || row.split === \"heldout\", `row ${row.id} has a known split`);\n    assert.ok(typeof row.steering === \"string\" && row.steering.trim().length > 0, `row ${row.id} has a steering message`);\n    assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(row.expected).sort(), [\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\"], `row ${row.id} labels all three requirements`);\n    for (const label of Object.values(row.expected)) assert.ok(LABELS.has(label as string), `row ${row.id} uses a known label`);\n  }\n  assert.ok(rows.some((r) => r.split === \"heldout\"), \"a held-out split exists\");\n  assert.ok(rows.some((r) => Object.values(r.expected).includes(\"withdraws\")), \"withdrawals are present\");\n  assert.ok(rows.some((r) => Object.values(r.expected).every((l) => l === \"none\")), \"hard negatives are present\");\n});\n\ntest(\"the shared question module yields one withdraws, defers and changes question per requirement\", async () => {\n  const { questionsFor, REQUIREMENTS } = await import(path.join(dir, \"questions.mjs\"));\n  const questions = questionsFor();\n  assert.equal(Object.keys(questions).length, REQUIREMENTS.length * 3);\n  for (const requirement of REQUIREMENTS) for (const kind of [\"withdraws\", \"defers\", \"changes\"]) {\n    const question = questions[`r${requirement.number}.${kind}`];\n    assert.equal(question.type, \"noul\");\n    assert.ok(question.instructions.includes(\"`steering.text`\"), \"the question names the state path it reads\");\n    assert.ok(question.instructions.includes(requirement.text), \"the question names its requirement\");\n  }\n});\nEOF\nH=$(mktemp -d); HOME=$H node --import tsx --test test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts 2>&1 | sed 's/\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]//g' | awk '/^ℹ (tests|pass|fail) /{printf \"%s \", $0} END{print \"\"}'; (cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval && ~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin/node --version >/dev/null && cd cli && HOME=$H PATH=~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin:$PATH node --import tsx --test test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts 2>&1 | sed 's/\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]//g' | awk '/^# (tests|pass|fail) |^ℹ (tests|pass|fail) /{printf \"%s \", $0} END{print \" (node22)\"}')","description":"Write README and the dataset validation test; regenerate scorer output; run on Node 24 and 22","timeout":180000}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch54aBSu4mCa5kVTZdUGp","requestRef":"0d1ed9de-35ba-4a6d-9b58-b8268124f139","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"44543fc1-abaa-41a5-82bf-4b4ab45af818","timestamp":"2026-11-15T16:54:00.053Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
