{"parentUuid":"fd7abd16-43fd-404d-9b49-365687128a7c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54eDqPUZK2ue5QJoLJ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've decided the open questions as you asked: the steering evidence gets committed as a research record now, the steering judge is deferred to a gated plan unit, and G1.1-4 gets one unaltered measurement on the published v1.2.0 archive. I'm committing the evidence first, then continuing the v1.2.1 plan.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_read_input_tokens":629983,"output_tokens":2398,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1366},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2398,"cache_read_input_tokens":629983,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":25,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch54eDZWeCSAzwLBQ67qE","requestRef":"f603a878-1a8a-492c-a1ab-d2565a7e7fa2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"22b84b17-eb49-43a7-bce6-dbd3ae8e4aa3","timestamp":"2026-11-15T16:54:41.547Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"22b84b17-eb49-43a7-bce6-dbd3ae8e4aa3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54eDqPUZK2ue5QJoLJ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NGu5MDezfZbXhkkjX1gyeM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(research): steering-judgment evaluation record (dataset, shared questions, runners, scorer, raw results)\n\n26 synthetic steering messages against three requirements; regex baseline vs a TypeSafe judge and a gateway judge. Research only: no product behaviour changes. Includes a dataset validation test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/steering-judgment-eval 2>&1 | tail -1; PRURL=$(gh pr create --base main --head v1/steering-judgment-eval --title \"docs(research): steering-judgment evaluation record\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nRecords an independent evaluation of the steering-conflict check (\\`steeringNegations\\`, SI-3), which is a regex that returns nothing on anything ambiguous. **Research only: no product behaviour changes.**\n\nOn 26 synthetic steering messages (78 judgments, 12 true withdrawals) the regex caught 3 of 12 with 1 false positive; a TypeSafe judge (\\`jev-1.14.0\\`) caught 12 of 12 with 0 of 66 false positives, and a gateway judge (\\`engineering/deep\\`, yes/no) caught 11 of 11 with 0 of 64 (row 26 missing: the gateway refused connections). Both judges agree row by row; the one false positive left in the union is the regex's (reported speech). Intervals are wide (12 positives); the README states the limits, including that the dataset and question wording were written in one session.\n\nAdds \\`docs/research/steering-judgment/\\` (dataset, single-source question wording, runners, scorer, raw results) and \\`cli/test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts\\`, a no-network validity check of the dataset.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test: 2 of 2 on Node 22 and 24. The scorer reproduces the recorded numbers. All text sent to either service was synthetic; keys came from the environment and are in no file (scanned). \\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` passes.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs and a dataset test).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nThird-party judging is opt-in and out of the default path; the README records the data-boundary reasoning (a negating steer is held from the model until the operator decides).\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo \"$PRURL\"; gh pr list --head v1/steering-judgment-eval --json number,state -q '.[]|\"#\\(.number) \\(.state)\"'","description":"Commit, push and open the steering evidence PR, reading its real number"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_read_input_tokens":629983,"output_tokens":2398,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1366},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2398,"cache_read_input_tokens":629983,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":4310,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NGu5MDezfZbXhkkjX1gyeM":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/steering-eval && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(research): steering-judgment evaluation record (dataset, shared questions, runners, scorer, raw results)\n\n26 synthetic steering messages against three requirements; regex baseline vs a TypeSafe judge and a gateway judge. Research only: no product behaviour changes. Includes a dataset validation test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/steering-judgment-eval 2>&1 | tail -1; PRURL=$(gh pr create --base main --head v1/steering-judgment-eval --title \"docs(research): steering-judgment evaluation record\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nRecords an independent evaluation of the steering-conflict check (\\`steeringNegations\\`, SI-3), which is a regex that returns nothing on anything ambiguous. **Research only: no product behaviour changes.**\n\nOn 26 synthetic steering messages (78 judgments, 12 true withdrawals) the regex caught 3 of 12 with 1 false positive; a TypeSafe judge (\\`jev-1.14.0\\`) caught 12 of 12 with 0 of 66 false positives, and a gateway judge (\\`engineering/deep\\`, yes/no) caught 11 of 11 with 0 of 64 (row 26 missing: the gateway refused connections). Both judges agree row by row; the one false positive left in the union is the regex's (reported speech). Intervals are wide (12 positives); the README states the limits, including that the dataset and question wording were written in one session.\n\nAdds \\`docs/research/steering-judgment/\\` (dataset, single-source question wording, runners, scorer, raw results) and \\`cli/test/steering_judgment_dataset.test.ts\\`, a no-network validity check of the dataset.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test: 2 of 2 on Node 22 and 24. The scorer reproduces the recorded numbers. All text sent to either service was synthetic; keys came from the environment and are in no file (scanned). \\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` passes.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs and a dataset test).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nThird-party judging is opt-in and out of the default path; the README records the data-boundary reasoning (a negating steer is held from the model until the operator decides).\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo \"$PRURL\"; gh pr list --head v1/steering-judgment-eval --json number,state -q '.[]|\"#\\(.number) \\(.state)\"'","description":"Commit, push and open the steering evidence PR, reading its real number"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch54eDZWeCSAzwLBQ67qE","requestRef":"f603a878-1a8a-492c-a1ab-d2565a7e7fa2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf0efeb9-a9b2-4353-8367-52856384f7a9","timestamp":"2026-11-15T16:54:45.963Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
