{"parentUuid":"bb3a79be-9d0f-4a7b-bbe5-cc9c7652e1a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54pfyGoVANos5B8qbHq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SeV2a99rusdqyddZy54wVR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan-vc10 && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(s, old, new, label):\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, f\"{label}: {s.count(old)} matches\"\n    return s.replace(old, new)\np = \"docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\nvc9 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| VC-9 |\")]; assert len(vc9) == 1\nvc10 = (\"| VC-10 | Steering semantic judge (optional; evidence in `docs/research/steering-judgment/`): a judge provider interface (none by default, the configured gateway, or an explicit opt-in third party) asked, for each live requirement, whether the steering message withdraws, defers or changes it; conflict (the existing operator decision) if the regex hits or `withdraws` >= 0.7 whatever `defers` says, advisory note between 0.3 and 0.7, `defers` and `changes` informational only; an unavailable judge records `semanticJudge: unavailable` and keeps the regex decision; the steer stays held from the model until the operator decides and no text goes to a third party unless opted in | **gated**: build only after a larger evaluation (at least 100 judgments from real steering messages, with the owner's consent, labelled blind, on a fresh held-out split) shows union recall of at least 0.8 with at most 5% false positives on the non-withdrawals, and after the synchronous path can hold a steer while a judge answers (the pilot gateway judge took a median of about 17 s per message) | M | P2 (v1.2.2, gated) |\")\ns = sub(s, vc9[0], vc9[0] + \"\\n\" + vc10, \"VC-9/VC-10\")\npc6 = [l for l in s.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| PC-6 |\")]; assert len(pc6) == 1\npc7 = (\"| PC-7 | Flaky `eval_integrity` scanner test: `Python black-box oracle uses only pinned offline Go and Rust toolchains, or fails preflight` (the \\\"more than 128 disjoint system roots\\\" case) failed once on a loaded runner with `inventory enumeration_exit_batch_1_signal_sigterm` and passed on re-run; find what ends the enumeration (a time bound, a runner limit) and make the test independent of load, or give it a justified bound | passes 10 consecutive runs under artificial CPU load; any bound is documented in the test | S | P2 |\")\ns = sub(s, pc6[0], pc6[0] + \"\\n\" + pc7, \"PC-6/PC-7\")\ns = sub(s, \"CX-7, CS-11, VC-9.\", \"CX-7, CS-11, VC-9, PC-7.\", \"phase 2\")\ns = sub(s, \"MQ-8 (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2).\", \"MQ-8 (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2), VC-10 (gated on a larger evaluation).\", \"phase 3\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\ng = \"docs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md\"\nt = open(g).read()\nga40 = [l for l in t.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| GA-40 |\")]; assert len(ga40) == 1\nrows = \"\\n\".join([\n \"| GA-41 | The steering-conflict check is a regex that returns nothing on paraphrases (3 of 12 withdrawals caught in the 2026-11-15 pilot); a judge closes it in the pilot but the evidence is 12 positives and the gateway judge is too slow for the synchronous path | pilot `docs/research/steering-judgment/` | P2 (gated) | VC-10 |\",\n \"| GA-42 | `eval_integrity` scanner test failed once under runner load (SIGTERM during enumeration) | CI, 2026-11-15 (#542 first run) | P2 | PC-7 |\",\n])\nt = t.replace(ga40[0], ga40[0] + \"\\n\" + rows)\nopen(g, \"w\").write(t)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\nnode scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(v1.2.1): plan VC-10 (gated steering judge) and PC-7 (flaky scanner test)\n\nVC-10 carries the steering-judgment pilot into the plan with explicit build gates (larger real-data evaluation, synchronous hold state); PC-7 records the one flaky eval_integrity failure seen under runner load. Gaps GA-41 and GA-42; sequencing updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/plan-vc10-pc7 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --head v1/plan-vc10-pc7 --title \"docs(v1.2.1): plan VC-10 (gated steering judge) and PC-7 (flaky scanner test)\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nDocs only. Two plan additions from this session's work:\n\n- **VC-10 (P2, v1.2.2, gated):** the optional steering semantic judge. The pilot in docs/research/steering-judgment (PR #543) shows a judge closes the regex's paraphrase blind spot (3 of 12 caught by the regex, 12 of 12 and 11 of 11 by the judges) but on only 12 positives, and the gateway judge took a median of about 17 s per message, too slow for the synchronous steering path. So it is planned with explicit gates, not built: a larger real-data evaluation with owner consent and blind labels, and a hold state while a judge answers. The truth table is the repaired one (conflict if the regex hits or withdraws >= 0.7 regardless of defers).\n- **PC-7 (P2, Phase 2):** the one flaky \\`eval_integrity\\` scanner test (SIGTERM during enumeration under runner load; passed on re-run).\n\nGaps GA-41 and GA-42; sequencing updated. No product behaviour changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` passes; every edit was applied with an exact-match assertion.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr list --head v1/plan-vc10-pc7 --json number,state -q '.[]|\"#\\(.number) \\(.state)\"'","description":"Apply VC-10 and PC-7 to the plan, commit, open the PR, read its real number"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1760,"cache_read_input_tokens":640075,"output_tokens":3176,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking