{"parentUuid":"7419b313-812f-4d68-96cd-96273a9c8833","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch54v1YuFGZsz4k1fpZpG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm now working on four fronts at once, with your authorization to decide and continue.\n\n**Decisions I made, and why**\n- **Steering judge:** planned, not built, as gated unit VC-10 in PR **#544**. The evidence is a 12-positive pilot, the gateway judge's median of about 17 s is too slow for the synchronous path, and the privacy design isn't settled. The gates are a larger real-data evaluation and a hold state while a judge answers.\n- **Flaky scanner test:** also in #544, as PC-7.\n- **Steering evidence:** committed as a research-only PR, **#543**. The dataset, shared questions, runners, scorer and raw results are in `docs/research/steering-judgment/`, plus a no-network test that passes on Node 22 and 24.\n- **G1.1-4:** one measurement on the published v1.2.0 archive, recorded unaltered. It started at 16:56Z under the GATEWAY claim (its sha256 `e5dbb315…`, commit `f1ad33b9`, clean checkout and fresh output directory), and it needs about an hour. Not a rerun-until-pass: it is the first measurement of the artifact that actually shipped.\n\n**In flight**\n- **Three agents** are implementing v1.2.1 units in their own worktrees: CX-5 (compaction invariant), VC-5 (verified re-check on resume) and WM-2 (edit-failure feedback). I'll review each and merge at its exact head, one at a time.\n- **#543 and #544:** CI is running, with a watch on both.\n\nI also saved your authorization to memory, with the hard limits written beside it. The limits are no frontier-grade claim, no tag moves, and failed runs recorded unaltered."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":645188,"output_tokens":572,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0}