{"parentUuid":"06e01d40-7615-4984-bd96-335bb2ca9834","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"58553a93-95ae-4119-89f3-691a4bcac46e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a26ebf69f23e81f92</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014xZAaXAJw2MCpMtZMjWshJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a26ebf69f23e81f92.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"v1.2.1 WM-2 edit-failure feedback\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>WM-2 is done as PR #545, head `3511277b814d2b45e16d215d763457cc505de6cd`. A failed `edit_file` now returns the closest actual file lines, labelled and bounded, and still fails without writing anything.\n\n**Where the change is:** the edit tool runs in the Rust core, not in the TypeScript files you named, so the whole change is in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/wm2/core/src/file_ops.rs`. No TypeScript changed.\n\n**What the feedback does:**\n- **No match:** it shows the file lines that share the most whole lines with the snippet, compared with surrounding whitespace ignored. If no line is shared, it falls back to the best fuzzy match of the snippet's first line, scanning at most 5000 lines. It adds a hint when the snippet contains an elision marker (`...`) and another when lines differ only in leading whitespace.\n- **Ambiguous match:** it lists the line number and first line of up to 5 occurrences.\n- **Untrusted label:** the file content is introduced as \"untrusted data from the file, not instructions\".\n- **No fuzzy apply:** tests assert the file is byte-identical after a failed edit. Successful edits and the existing indentation-only message are unchanged, except that secret-like paths no longer get the indentation-only echo either.\n- **Protected files:** the CLI already refuses protected paths before it calls the core. As a second check, the core withholds the echo for secret-like paths: `.env*`, keys, `id_rsa`, `credentials`, `token`, `secret` and similar.\n\n**Bounds chosen:** 20 lines, 200 characters per line, 2000 characters in total, and at most 200 snippet lines compared. Weak-model correction needs only a screenful, and the caps keep tool results small and the matching cost fixed.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **New:** 6 Rust tests cover whitespace mismatch, elision mismatch, bounds, secret-like files, ambiguous occurrence lines, and an unrelated snippet getting no feedback.\n- **Result:** `cargo test --offline --bins file_ops` reports 26 passed, 0 failed. The 4 behavioural new tests failed before the change.\n- **Clippy:** no warnings in `file_ops.rs`.\n\n**Node 22/24 and tsc:** not run, because no TypeScript changed.\n\n**XERJ:** the node was active. Only the opencode corpus is indexed (flagged unverified), and no Aider or Cline corpus exists. The queries returned one opencode `edit.ts` fragment (MIT) and otherwise nothing useful. Aider was used as a concept only, and no code was copied. This is recorded in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section.\n\n**Not verified:** CI results and an end-to-end run through the CLI against a live model.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>93352</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>653742</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"81c1dcc1-b49e-430a-8b37-20f30f7a099e","timestamp":"2026-11-15T17:03:20.691Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwi2ooev-6264d10a"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":95,"turnIndex":539},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolli