{"parentUuid":"45072a17-9130-4f56-97c1-77d4e4ceb243","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch55U9az7jZxEh41UC2bJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TKNXH17SCAQ3w8fyvocWSi","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a26ebf69f23e81f92","summary":"WM-2 review fix: cap vote map cost","message":"Review of PR #545 (WM-2): no correctness or security defect found; I reproduced `cargo test --offline --bins file_ops` = 26 passed with an isolated CARGO_TARGET_DIR. ONE required fix before merge: robustness of the failure path on large files. In `closest_lines_feedback` the `votes` map is bounded in snippet length (200 lines) but NOT in how often a line repeats in the file: a file with many identical lines of >= 4 chars (e.g. 100k lines of `pass`/`return;`/`continue;`) makes each snippet line vote for every occurrence, up to snippet_lines x file_lines map operations (tens of millions) on a FAILED edit, which is the very path weak models hit repeatedly. Fix: skip common lines. E.g. build `by_text` only for texts that occur at most FEEDBACK_MAX_OCCURRENCES (suggest 50) times in the file (count first, then index), since a line that common cannot identify a location anyway; keep behaviour identical otherwise. Add a test: a generated file of >= 50_000 identical lines plus one distinctive block, a failed edit whose snippet contains both, asserting (a) feedback still points at the distinctive block, and (b) it completes under a generous wall-clock bound (e.g. < 2s in a debug build) — pin the cost, not exact output. Re-run `cd core && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<isolated dir> cargo test --offline --bins file_ops` and clippy, push to the same branch (same PR #545), and report the new head SHA and pass/fail totals. Same rules as before (no merge/tag/publish, chain with &&, never git stash).","type":"message","recipient":"a26ebf69f23e81f92","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Review of PR #545 (WM-2): no correctness or secur…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":653489,"output_tokens":849,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":109},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":653489,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":4585,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TKNXH17SCAQ3w8fyvocWSi":{"to":"a26ebf69f23e81f92","summary":"WM-2 review fix: cap vote map cost","message":"Review of PR #545 (WM-2): no correctness or security defect found; I reproduced `cargo test --offline --bins file_ops` = 26 passed with an isolated CARGO_TARGET_DIR. ONE required fix before merge: robustness of the failure path on large files. In `closest_lines_feedback` the `votes` map is bounded in snippet length (200 lines) but NOT in how often a line repeats in the file: a file with many identical lines of >= 4 chars (e.g. 100k lines of `pass`/`return;`/`continue;`) makes each snippet line vote for every occurrence, up to snippet_lines x file_lines map operations (tens of millions) on a FAILED edit, which is the very path weak models hit repeatedly. Fix: skip common lines. E.g. build `by_text` only for texts that occur at most FEEDBACK_MAX_OCCURRENCES (suggest 50) times in the file (count first, then index), since a line that common cannot identify a location anyway; keep behaviour identical otherwise. Add a test: a generated file of >= 50_000 identical lines plus one distinctive block, a failed edit whose snippet contains both, asserting (a) feedback still points at the distinctive block, and (b) it completes under a generous wall-clock bound (e.g. < 2s in a debug build) — pin the cost, not exact output. Re-run `cd core && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<isolated dir> cargo test --offline --bins file_ops` and clippy, push to the same branch (same PR #545), and report the new head SHA and pass/fail totals. Same rules as before (no merge/tag/publish, chain with &&, never git stash)."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch55U9G8uLuNjQyAwRrAY","requestRef":"84a8159d-7f87-4b62-8c9c-50949b382f23","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b996e29d-a95e-47c2-b3a8-d4d1ad69918f","timestamp":"2026-11-15T17:05:25.404Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
