{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-15T17:08:36.555Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a26ebf69f23e81f92</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01TKNXH17SCAQ3w8fyvocWSi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a26ebf69f23e81f92.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"v1.2.1 WM-2 edit-failure feedback\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The large-file cost problem is fixed and pushed to PR #545; the new head is `acef4acb2b8a6d191fcfd6f0281c910790bc6bdc`.\n\n**Results:** `cargo test --offline --bins file_ops` gives 27 passed, 0 failed, with an isolated `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`. Clippy reports no warnings in `file_ops.rs`. I have not checked CI.\n\n**Fixes, all in `core/src/file_ops.rs`:**\n- **Repeated lines:** `closest_lines_feedback` now counts line occurrences first and indexes only lines that occur 50 times or fewer (`FEEDBACK_MAX_OCCURRENCES`), as you suggested.\n- **Real hot spot:** that change alone did not meet the 2s bound. The test still took about 4.5s, and profiling showed about 5s of it was in the existing `indentation_only_match`, not the vote map. That function scanned every window position and compared up to a snippet's length of lines at each. I changed it to take candidate window starts only from the occurrences of the snippet line that is rarest in the file.\n- **Display bug the new test exposed:** on a long snippet, the 20-line cap showed only the repeated lines and hid the actual mismatch. The feedback now starts one line before the first line that differs from the snippet.\n\n**New test:** `test_failed_edit_feedback_cost_is_bounded_on_repetitive_files` uses a file of 60,000 identical lines plus a distinctive block, and a snippet with 150 repeated lines plus that block with one line changed. It asserts three things:\n- the failed edit finishes in under 2s in a debug build;\n- the feedback shows `distinctive_one` and `let marker = 1;`;\n- the file is unchanged afterwards.\n\nNothing was merged, tagged or published.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>99597</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>190560</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
