ion_only_match`, not the vote map. That function scanned every window position and compared up to a snippet's length of lines at each. I changed it to take candidate window starts only from the occurrences of the snippet line that is rarest in the file.\n- **Display bug the new test exposed:** on a long snippet, the 20-line cap showed only the repeated lines and hid the actual mismatch. The feedback now starts one line before the first line that differs from the snippet.\n\n**New test:** `test_failed_edit_feedback_cost_is_bounded_on_repetitive_files` uses a file of 60,000 identical lines plus a distinctive block, and a snippet with 150 repeated lines plus that block with one line changed. It asserts three things:\n- the failed edit finishes in under 2s in a debug build;\n- the feedback shows `distinctive_one` and `let marker = 1;`;\n- the file is unchanged afterwards.\n\nNothing was merged, tagged or published.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>99597</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>190560</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
