ITY_EXCEEDED` and names the missing requirements. `CapacityRecord.missingRequirements` and a new heading in `cli/src/core/turn.ts` carry that. `compactNow` returns `ok:false` and leaves the conversation unchanged.\n- **CERI:** `compaction-03` is active. I updated the frozen scenario JSON and its sha manifest, changed `ACTIVE_FROZEN` to 24, and added a driver.\n\nFiles are all under `/home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5/cli`: `src/agent.ts`, `src/core/objective.ts`, `src/core/turn.ts`, `test/ceri_semantic_integrity.test.ts`, the two `test/fixtures/ceri/semantic_integrity.scenarios.*` files, and the new `test/compaction_ledger_invariant.test.ts`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **New file:** 6 of 6 pass on both Node 22.22.2 and 24.21.0. It forces each of the 15 `admitContext` rungs as the one admitted. It also covers the second-pass rungs, `compact --llm` (including a refusal to commit when a requirement would be lost), the guard blocking with zero gateway requests, an over-limit ledger blocking, and the zero-budget rung blocking.\n- **Four-file run on Node 22 and 24:** new file plus `ceri_semantic_integrity`, `context_capacity` and `context_auto_compaction` gave 43 tests, 39 pass, 3 fail. `compaction-03` passes.\n- **The 3 failures:** `self-validating-01/02/03`. They fail identically on origin/main on this host (the Rust core handshake fails).\n- **Not like-for-like:** `compaction_continuity` and `sidecar_compact_queue` fail on host Rust-core errors. The base run aborts at the file level, so whole-file totals don't compare. The five-test subset I ran on both trees gave 2 pass, 5 fail each.\n- **Build:** `npm --prefix cli run build` is clean.\n\n**Could not verify:**\n- **Reference coding:** XERJ was active but only has opencode, the prompts corpus and the workflow spec indexed. The Gemini CLI, Codex and Cline code was not reachable, and my broad search timed out with no output. The PR body says so and takes only the plan's design (verify after compaction, refuse rather than send a lossy request).\n- **Second ladder:** the \"attempt 2\" ladder (recent turns [1,0] against budgets [3000..0]) looks unreachable, because an accepted candidate is always admissible and ends the loop. I tested its rungs through candidates only.\n- **CI:** I have not seen a green run.\n\nI left a temporary `/home/mike/nexus-wt/cx5-base` worktree (origin/main with a `cli/dist` build) for the baseline comparison. I did not remove it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>144422</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>41</tool_uses><duration_ms>1003844</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","source_uuid":"b22fb794-8107-439e-ad3d-384e270dad54","delivery_id":"d82d3a9b-b421-4c02-9e1d-66b77ad59462","commandMode":"task-notification","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task"},"runId":"0mwi2oao4-245ef491","timestamp":"2026-11-15T17:08:52.660Z","usage":{"totalTokens":144422,"toolUses":41,"durationMs":1003844}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"95a279c7-65af-42c9-a0fc-aa974f425234","timestamp":"2026-11-15T17:08:52.660Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a091d4740b72a2dc3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_012r1kBAWNtEk5M9qKBRz455</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a091d4740b72a2dc3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"v1.2.1 CX-5 compaction invariant\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children 