{"parentUuid":"d76dadc5-e14f-46e9-a75d-bca2502df432","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch56G25pSWqYurBarzGrx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three agents have reported, and the wave is now five PRs in CI: #543, #544, #545 (WM-2), #546 (CX-5) and #547 (VC-5), plus the G1.1-4 matrix on the published archive. It has been running since 16:56Z, and I'll read its result when it completes.\n\n**VC-5 (#547, head `f9d97e86`)**\n- **What it does:** a `verified` requirement now survives resume only if its recorded inputs equal the current candidate identity, otherwise it is demoted. A resumed task after an unbound-verifier pass now completes as REGRESSION_FREE and never VERIFIED.\n- **Security review:** the persisted marker only weakens. It is honoured only while the verifier definition is still unbindable now, so a forged marker can't excuse a bindable verifier.\n- **Tests:** 52 of 52 pass on Node 22 and 24 across the new file and two neighbouring ones.\n\nI'm holding back the next wave of units: six PRs plus a matrix is enough to saturate CI, and batch-merging into a saturated queue is how `main` broke earlier. I'll merge one PR at a time at its exact head, waiting for the `main` run after each, and start the next units (CX-1, WM-1, DH-5) as those clear."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":675080,"output_tokens":425,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":675080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869},"type":"m