{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"4bd75f43a3fabd79d1ca78e44422ecfb227671eefca4ee25fba076363c2befff","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"While that agent works, I'm recording the stable-archive measurement. It goes into a docs PR with the plan unit for this finding (WM-4), as unaltered evidence with the failure as it actually is."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PL1NDg7kU7nZ9Bs41UspcT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin && git worktree add -q /home/mike/nexus-wt/g114-stable-evidence -b v1/g114-stable-evidence origin/main 2>&1 | tail -1; G=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/scratchpad/g120; D=/home/mike/nexus-wt/g114-stable-evidence/docs/evidence/v1.2.0; cp $G/out-stable/wp-1107-provider-matrix.v1.2.0.json $G/out-stable/wp-1107-provider-matrix.v1.2.0.json.sha256 $D/ && (cd $D && sha256sum -c wp-1107-provider-matrix.v1.2.0.json.sha256) ; RSHA=$(sha256sum $G/out-stable/receipts/dot-nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl | cut -c1-64); echo receipts=$RSHA; cat > $D/probe-lead-reasoning-read_file-2026-11-15.txt <<'EOF'\nProbe, 2026-11-15 17:49Z, under the GATEWAY claim: the plain read_file prompt sent 10 times to engineering/lead-reasoning\nthrough the v1.2.0 client (client.chatCompletion, temperature 0, response cache bypassed). Prompt:\n\"Call the read_file tool exactly once with arguments that satisfy its supplied JSON Schema. Do not add prose.\"\nColumns: alias, tool, attempt, latency, number of native tool calls, toolCallSource, content when there is no call.\n\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 0 ms=11827 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 1 ms=11740 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 2 ms=11781 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 3 ms=11648 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 4 ms=11594 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 5 ms=11659 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 6 ms=11941 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 7 ms=11698 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 8 ms=11672 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nengineering/lead-reasoning read_file 9 ms=11580 calls=0 source=native \"read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\" reasoningLen=2552\nEOF\ncat > $D/G1.1-4-v1.2.0.md <<EOF\n# G1.1-4 on the published v1.2.0 archive (not met)\n\n**Result: not met.** \\`engineering/deep\\` 200/200 native valid; \\`engineering/lead-reasoning\\` **155/200** (77.5%) against the 99.5% bar. Nothing here is independent qualification, and no run was repeated to obtain a better number.\n\n- Candidate: the published \\`v1.2.0\\` release, archive sha256 \\`e5dbb315435a20245964571ddaca3e3e7825e8bc8d04afbf62bacd8543044de3\\` (verified against the release's checksums and attestations), commit \\`f1ad33b9d6c8f3a7acfb6624331eb46484d2977f\\`, tree \\`b3596f269f87f7987aa9e7d38d2a47a1f68bb298\\`, installed with attestation verification. Runner: \\`eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs\\` from the candidate checkout, unmodified; shared gateway only, \\`temperature 0\\`, \\`max_tokens 8192\\`, response cache bypassed, 1200 ms request interval, a fresh output path and a clean checkout.\n- Run: 16:56Z to 17:47Z under the GATEWAY claim. Result \\`wp-1107-provider-matrix.v1.2.0.json\\` (sha256 in the adjacent \\`.sha256\\`, \\`048e1c6b…\\`). Request receipts (not committed, 245 \\`deep\\` and 200 \\`lead-reasoning\\` requests, all \\`completed\\`): sha256 \\`$RSHA\\`.\n\n## What failed, and how this differs from rc.1\n\n| Alias | read_file | write_file | edit_file | run_command |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| \\`engineering/deep\\` | 50/50 | 50/50 | 50/50 | 50/50 (45 feedback retries, as in every earlier run) |\n| \\`engineering/lead-reasoning\\` | **5/50** | 50/50 | 50/50 | 50/50 |\n\nOn rc.1 (\\`G1.1-4-rc.1.md\\`) the failures were five hybrid (\"think before the call\") \\`edit_file\\` prompts that ran to the output cap. This run is a different failure: 45 plain \\`read_file\\` prompts. All 200 \\`lead-reasoning\\` requests completed as requests (no failed receipts), so the 45 invalid answers were completions that were not exactly one correct native call.\n\nA probe straight after the run (\\`probe-lead-reasoning-read_file-2026-11-15.txt\\`) shows what the model returns for the plain \\`read_file\\` prompt: no native tool call, and content that is literally \\`read_file(path=\"README.md\")\\` (python-style function-call text), 10 of 10 times. Earlier the same day the same alias answered this prompt with a native call (rc.1 attempt 3, 06:32Z to 07:05Z: \\`read_file\\` 50/50), so the pool's serving behaviour changed in between. The gateway is outside the product's control.\n\n## What the client does with that, and the follow-up\n\nThe client treats a reply that is \"the call written as text\" as a failed attempt, tells the model and asks again, then forces \\`tool_choice\\`: that path is why \\`deep\\` ends 200/200. It recognises JSON-style and tag-style text calls, not function-call-style text, so for \\`lead-reasoning\\` the safe retry never engages and the reply is plain text. The follow-up is v1.2.1 unit WM-4 (recognise a whole-content call to an offered tool written as \\`name(arg=\"value\")\\`, or inside a \\`[...]\\` list, as a call-as-text so the existing retry applies; recognition only, never execution). It is not claimed to fix anything until a matrix is taken on a build that contains it.\n\n## Standing\n\n- G1.1-4 is **not met** on v1.2.0 by either measurement (195/200 on rc.1, 155/200 on the published archive). The release notes' limitation is updated to say so.\n- Neither number is a regression introduced by a code change: the client code on the request path is identical between v1.1.4, rc.1 and v1.2.0. v1.1.4 passed 200/200 on one rerun. The gate moves with what the gateway's pool returns, which is why the matrix pins the pool's fingerprint and why a passing rerun would supersede a failing one only for the build it was taken on.\n- No rerun was taken to obtain a pass. Qualification of the next release (v1.2.1) is measured on its own release candidate.\nEOF\ncd /home/mike/nexus-wt/g114-stable-evidence && ls docs/evidence/v1.2.0","description":"Create the stable-measurement evidence record in a fresh worktree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
