othing is executed from text (REQ-AGT-112); the G1.1-4 matrix keeps counting native calls only | table of accepted and rejected forms (prose that merely mentions a call, unknown tool, unbalanced, a variable argument); a mock-gateway test where the first reply is function-call text and the retry returns a native call; a matrix taken on the v1.2.1 release candidate before any claim | S | P1 |\")\ns=s.replace(wm3[0], wm3[0]+\"\\n\"+wm4)\nold=\"CS-3, CS-4, WM-1, WM-2, CX-1, CX-5, VC-5.\"\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,\"CS-3, CS-4, WM-1, WM-2, WM-4, CX-1, CX-5, VC-5.\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\n\ng=\"docs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md\"\nt=open(g).read()\nga=[l for l in t.split(\"\\n\") if l.startswith(\"| GA-40 |\")]; assert len(ga)==1\nt=t.replace(ga[0], ga[0]+\"\\n| GA-43 | A reply that is a function-call-style text call (`read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")`) is not recognised as a call written as text, so the safe retry never engages; it made 45 of 50 `lead-reasoning` read_file attempts invalid on the published v1.2.0 matrix | G1.1-4 on v1.2.0, 2026-11-15 (`docs/evidence/v1.2.0/G1.1-4-v1.2.0.md`) | P1 | WM-4 |\")\nopen(g,\"w\").write(t)\n\nn=\"docs/releases/v1.2.0.md\"\nu=open(n).read()\nold=\"The five failures are \\\"think before the call\\\" `edit_file` prompts where the model reasons to the output cap without calling the tool.\"\nassert u.count(old)==1\nu=u.replace(old, old+\" Measured again on the published archive (2026-11-15) it was 155/200: 45 plain `read_file` prompts, where the model answered with the call written as function-call text (`read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")`) that the client does not recognise; see `docs/evidence/v1.2.0/G1.1-4-v1.2.0.md`.\")\nopen(n,\"w\").write(u)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\nnode scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; git add -A && git commit -q -m \"docs(v1.2.0): G1.1-4 on the published archive (not met, 155/200); plan WM-4\n\nUnaltered result, receipts hash, and the probe showing lead-reasoning now writes the read_file call as function-call text, which the client does not recognise. Notes limitation updated; WM-4 (P1) and GA-43 added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/g114-stable-evidence 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --head v1/g114-stable-evidence --title \"docs(v1.2.0): G1.1-4 on the published archive (not met, 155/200); plan WM-4\" --body \"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nDocs only. Records the G1.1-4 measurement taken on the published v1.2.0 archive (sha256 e5dbb315…, commit f1ad33b9): \\`engineering/deep\\` 200/200, \\`engineering/lead-reasoning\\` **155/200**, gate not met. Unaltered result file and hash, request-receipt hash, and a 10-call probe.\n\nThe failure differs from rc.1's: 45 plain \\`read_file\\` prompts, where the model now answers with the call written as function-call text (\\`read_file(path=\\\"README.md\\\")\\`) and no native call; the same prompt returned native calls earlier the same day, so the pool's serving behaviour changed. The client recognises only JSON text as a call written as text, so its safe retry never engages for this form (it does for \\`deep\\`, 45 feedback retries, 200/200).\n\nAdds plan unit WM-4 (P1, recognition only, never execution; qualification only on a v1.2.1 release candidate) and gap GA-43, and updates the v1.2.0 notes limitation. No rerun was taken to obtain a pass. The published release body is updated to match.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` passes. The result file's sha256 is verified against the recorded hash. Claims about the client were checked against \\`cli/src/core/content_tool_call.ts\\`.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (docs only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr list --head v1/g114-stabl