{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-15T18:00:22.492Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a67337be300b451d3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01B7NTtiusnA6mj92P6psKNA</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a67337be300b451d3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"v1.2.1 WM-4 function-call-text recovery\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>WM-4 is done: PR #549, head `e256c832d2dc64a714d672d9daadfaed3939372e`, https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/549. A function-call-style text reply now triggers the existing feedback and forced-retry path. I did not merge, tag or force-push.\n\n**Where it lives:** `isContentCallReply` in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/wm4/cli/src/core/content_tool_call.ts`. When the reply is not JSON, it falls through to a new function-call-text recognizer.\n- The existing client path (`askAgainForNativeCall` in `cli/src/client.ts`) is unchanged.\n- That path only recognizes text calls and never parses arguments for execution, so nothing was reused or added there.\n- The text is still never executed.\n- `eval/` and the matrix classification are untouched.\n\n**Accepted** (the whole content, after trimming and removing think blocks and one optional code fence of any language tag):\n- A single `name(key=literal, ...)` to a tool offered in this request. Zero arguments and a trailing comma are fine.\n- A list `[name(...), name2(...)]`, with one or several calls and an optional trailing comma.\n- Literals: single- or double-quoted strings with escapes, numbers, `true`/`false`/`null`/`True`/`False`/`None`, lists, and dicts with string keys, nested up to 16 deep.\n\n**Rejected:**\n- Prose that mentions a call, and any text before or after the call or fence, including two fences.\n- An unknown tool, including one inside a list.\n- Unbalanced parentheses, brackets or quotes.\n- Positional arguments, variables such as `path=README`, expressions, calls as arguments, f-strings, tuples and duplicate keywords.\n- Dotted names, `;`-chained code, several calls without a list, unknown escapes, and raw newlines in strings.\n- JSON arrays.\n- A call whose text already appears in a non-assistant message in the request, which is the same echo rule JSON replies get.\n\n**Tests:** new file `cli/test/function_call_text.test.ts` with 7 tests, including three client tests on the mock gateway (feedback retry then native call, forced `required`, and a prose mention getting one request with no retry). Against origin/main's version of the source, 4 of the 7 fail, so the tests were red first.\n\n| Run | Node 22.22.2 | Node 24.21.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `function_call_text` + `content_tool_call` | 20 tests, 20 pass, 0 fail | 20 tests, 20 pass, 0 fail |\n| Broader set plus the new file | 221 tests, 197 pass, 24 fail | 221 tests, 197 pass, 24 fail |\n\nThe broader set is `client_robustness`, `client_tool_grammar`, `request_shape`, `repeated_calls`, `tool_grammar`, `tool_grammar_matrix`, `tool_grammar_wire` and `harness`.\n- On Node 22, origin/main's source runs 214 tests with 24 fail, and the failing set is identical to mine. They are Rust-core and worktree tests that fail here on host state; I did not check them against CI.\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` is clean.\n\n**XERJ:** queries are recorded in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Goose returned only model-catalog data and no llama.cpp pythonic parser is indexed. I borrowed only opencode's \"repair only when unambiguous\" principle, and no code was copied.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- No real gateway or inference was run, so the `engineering/lead-reasoning` behaviour is covered only by the mock.\n- The Node 24 failing set was not diffed against a Node 24 baseline; only the totals match Node 22.\n- CI on the PR has not been checked.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>93083</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>576751</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
