iling set is identical to mine. They are Rust-core and worktree tests that fail here on host state; I did not check them against CI.\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` is clean.\n\n**XERJ:** queries are recorded in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Goose returned only model-catalog data and no llama.cpp pythonic parser is indexed. I borrowed only opencode's \"repair only when unambiguous\" principle, and no code was copied.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- No real gateway or inference was run, so the `engineering/lead-reasoning` behaviour is covered only by the mock.\n- The Node 24 failing set was not diffed against a Node 24 baseline; only the totals match Node 22.\n- CI on the PR has not been checked.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>93083</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>576751</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
