{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"282ef0a4942dd18137e6f3823dd686c0af28096c883523978e99ec4080d3692d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`main` CI on the final commit `2382b534` completed with success. That commit contains all four merges: #543, #544, #545 and #546. So `main` is confirmed healthy after them, not assumed. The two intermediate runs I cancelled don't matter now, because the final run covers their content.\n\nNow the next merge. #549 should have finished its last check, so I'm verifying it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016RR6McJ9S51KQVEExzQCPN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin; echo \"main=$(git rev-parse --short=8 origin/main)\"; n=549; HEAD=$(gh pr view $n --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid); gh pr checks $n 2>&1 | grep -v -E '^Entire Gates|^package' | awk -F'\\t' '{print $1\": \"$2}' | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; J=$(gh pr checks $n 2>&1 | grep -E 'linux-x86_64' | grep -o 'job/[0-9]*' | cut -d/ -f2 | head -1); T=$(gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/jobs/$J/logs --allow-escape-sequences 2>&1 | sed 's/\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]//g' | awk '/origin \\+[0-9a-f]{40}/{n=match($0,/\\+[0-9a-f]{40}/); print substr($0,n+1,40); exit}'); git fetch -q origin $T 2>/dev/null; BASE=$(git rev-parse $T^1 2>/dev/null); PRF=$(gh pr diff $n --name-only | sort); MAINF=$(git diff --name-only $BASE origin/main 2>/dev/null | sort); OVER=$(comm -12 <(echo \"$PRF\") <(echo \"$MAINF\") | tr '\\n' ' '); echo \"#$n head=${HEAD:0:8} tested=${T:0:8} base=${BASE:0:8} overlap=[${OVER}] nonpass=$(gh pr checks $n 2>&1 | grep -v -E '^Entire Gates|^package' | grep -c -v -E '\\spass\\s|\\sskipping\\s')\"","description":"Verify #549 checks, head and overlap against main"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
