{"parentUuid":"61018ab4-7456-4e69-a452-096b63047841","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5DMhUsCZHaRWvhZrnFj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Z5zGtuDJn1Qb4PyFzapv2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hardening slice 4: legacy worktree merge git guard","prompt":"You are working on Slice 4 of a security-hardening task in the nexus-code repository (TypeScript CLI in `cli/`, Rust core in `core/`), in your own git worktree. This slice is REPRODUCE FIRST: a static review suspects a defect that may not be real, and an honest \"does not reproduce, here is the check that stops it\" is a valid outcome.\n\nGROUND RULES (from AGENTS.md; read it, docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 first):\n- Worktree: `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git fetch origin && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard4 -b v1/hardening-s4-worktree-merge origin/main && ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cli/node_modules /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard4/cli/node_modules`. Never edit ~/nexus-code itself. Claim the slice/hot files (cli/src/worktree.ts) under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` exactly as docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md describes (atomic mkdir + owner.json + a nexus-claims.log line) before editing; release the claim when done (\"released-<timestamp>\" naming, see `ls` of that directory). Check `git log` for foreign commits before each commit.\n- Isolate HOME for every test or probe: `HOME=$(mktemp -d)`. Never touch the real ~/.config/nexus. `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/claude-1000/cargo-hard4` if you build Rust. Stop processes by their own pid, never `pkill -f`. Chain shell commands with &&; never `git stash`.\n- Do NOT push, tag, merge, publish or open a PR. Commit locally and leave the branch ready (trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`).\n- Reference coding: query XERJ per docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md (`systemctl --user is-active xerj`; first query can take over a minute) for how mature agents (Codex CLI, Claude Code, OpenHands, Aider) guard git against planted config/hooks in agent-writable worktrees; record what you took/borrowed/rejected in your final report and the commit message; if unavailable write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" and use git grep.\n- Done means: a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after (or, if it does not reproduce, a regression test documenting the guard that stops it); affected test files pass on Node 22 AND 24 (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin` and `.../v24.21.0/bin` first on PATH); `npm --prefix cli run build` clean. Some tests fail on this host for host reasons (unbuilt cli/dist, stray /tmp/.git): compare against origin/main. Preserve existing comments. Report as measured.\n\nSLICE 4: guard the legacy worktree merge against planted git config and hooks (Medium; reproduce first).\nSuspected problem: `WorktreeManager.mergeWorktree` in `cli/src/worktree.ts` (around lines 410-425) runs plain `git status`, `git add -A` and `git commit` inside the agent-writable worktree. It uses no `trustedGitArgs`, no `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, no `core.fsmonitor=false`, and no `git_hook_guard`. It is called from `agent.ts:1922`. The newer paths (`cli/src/worktrunk/git.ts`, `cli/src/git.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_git.ts`) already guard against this.\nStep 1, reproduce: in a temp HOME and temp repository, create a linked worktree the way Nexus does. As the agent could with `run_command` in `auto` mode, replace the worktree's `.git` file with a directory containing a `config` with `core.fsmonitor` or `core.hooksPath` and a `pre-commit` hook that touches a sentinel file OUTSIDE the worktree. Then trigger `mergeWorktree`. Record whether the sentinel appears. If it does not, write down why (which existing check stops it), add that as a regression test anyway, and STOP this slice (report the result).\nStep 2, fix if it reproduces: run `verifyCheckout`/`trustedGitArgs` before any git call in `mergeWorktree`, and pin `--git-dir`/`--work-tree`; pass the same hardening `-c` flags and environment that `worktrunk/git.ts` uses, including `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, `core.fsmonitor=false`, the Git 2.54+ hook switches from `git_hook_guard.ts`, and `NON_INTERACTIVE`. Better, if feasible: send this path through the `worktrunk` merge implementation and delete the duplicate; if that is too big, say so and leave a tracked follow-up note in your report. Grep for every other plain `execFileSync(\"git\", ...)` / `spawnSync(\"git\"...)` in `cli/src` that runs inside agent-writable directories without the guard; list each in your report, and fix it or explain why it is safe.\n\nREPORT BACK (concise, one block): branch name and head SHA; the reproduction result (the exact observation, sentinel present or absent and why); what changed; tests added with before/after result and pass/fail TOTALS on Node 22 and 24; the list of other unguarded git call sites and your disposition for each; anything you could not verify; any user-visible behaviour change."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4728,"cache_read_input_tokens":737425,"output_tokens":7790,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1488},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4728,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":7790,"cache_read_input_tokens":737425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4728},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10386,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013Z5zGtuDJn1Qb4PyFzapv2":{"description":"Hardening slice 4: legacy worktr