{"parentUuid":"31831015-147e-45bc-b2ee-3a88b1cf641d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5DSBbevi8g9yEXrXDgG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three agents are working on the hardening slices, each in its own worktree with a local-only branch:\n- **Slice 1:** scrubbing credentials out of agent commands (`hard1`).\n- **Slice 4:** the legacy worktree merge guard (`hard4`), reproduce-first, so \"does not reproduce\" is an acceptable and honest result.\n- **Slices 6 and 7:** protected-path matching and `allowExternalSymlinks` (`hard6` and `hard7`).\n\nEach brief carries the slice text and your ground rules. That means a throwaway HOME, an isolated `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`, claims taken before editing, XERJ reference coding, tests that fail before and pass after on Node 22 and 24, and no push, tag, merge or PR.\n\nSlices 2, 3 and 5 wait, in the order you gave. Slice 2 and Slice 5 both touch `sandbox.ts` and `tools.ts`, so they start only after Slice 1 lands. I'll review each branch myself when its agent reports. That means I read the diff, re-run the tests, and independently check that the Slice 1 sentinel really stays out of `env` output. This is security code, so I won't rely on the agent's report alone.\n\nSeparately, #547 (VC-5) is still waiting on its last required job."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8976,"cache_read_input_tokens":742153,"output_tokens":436,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8976,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":742153,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens