{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-11-15T19:10:09.446Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4941041e38dd50bb</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_018BEdaMuECYMiSKmy2braGY</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a4941041e38dd50bb.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Hardening slice 1: scrub command environment\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Slice 1 is done and committed locally; nothing was pushed.** Branch `v1/hardening-s1-command-env`, head `954c601acdb3391cf3eb7a87beb09a0324cf55bf`, one commit on top of origin/main `897fd530`. Worktree: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/hard1`.\n\n**Reproduced on main.** With a sentinel `REDACTED in a temp HOME's `config.env`, `run_command \"env\"` printed it. This happened unsandboxed, under `--sandbox` with bwrap, and on the spawnSync fallback. The new test failed 3/3 before the fix with \"a credential reached the command environment: sk-sentinel-123\".\n\n**What changed**\n- `cli/src/command_env.ts` (new): one `buildCommandEnvironment()` plus `isCredentialName()`.\n  - It is a deny list. It drops every key from `config.env`, except PATH, HOME, USER, LOGNAME, SHELL, TERM, LANG, TMPDIR, PWD and `LC_*`, which stay.\n  - It also drops credential-looking names: `*_API_KEY`, `*_TOKEN`, `*_SECRET`, `*_PASSWORD`, `*_CREDENTIALS`, each with an optional `_FILE`, `_PATH` or `_ID`. Also `AWS_*`, `AZURE_*`, `NEXUS_GATEWAY_TOKEN*`, `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `NPM_TOKEN`, `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`, `KUBECONFIG`, `NETRC`, `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `DOCKER_CONFIG` and `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG`.\n  - It drops proxy variables that contain a user name or password.\n  - `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH` (comma-separated, trailing `*` for a prefix) is read via `operatorSetting`, so only the operator environment and `config.env` count. A value found in `process.env` is never trusted as the opt-in.\n- `cli/src/config.ts`: added `userConfigEnvKeys()`, which returns the key names from `config.env`.\n- `cli/src/tools.ts`: both the harness-core RPC spawn and the `executeViaSpawnSync` fallback now pass `env: buildCommandEnvironment()`.\n- `cli/src/sandbox.ts`: only the write-mode bwrap branch changed. It now adds `--clearenv`, then `--setenv` for each scrubbed variable.\n- `core/src/runner.rs`: second layer with the same name rules, `is_credential_name()`. `env_remove` is applied on both the normal and PTY spawn paths and honours the passthrough list. It strips by name pattern rather than clearing on an explicit RPC env.\n- `cli/test/command_env.test.ts` (new): four tests, with `leak_guard` imported and bridges shut down.\n  - Unsandboxed, bwrap and spawnSync each assert the sentinels never appear, the passthrough variable (including `GH_TOKEN`) does, and PATH/HOME/ordinary variables survive. A project-style `PROJECT_TOKEN` stays hidden.\n  - A fourth unit test covers `isCredentialName` and `buildCommandEnvironment`.\n\n**Test results (as measured)**\n\n| Check | Node 22.22.2 | Node 24.21.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `command_env.test.ts` (after fix) | 4/4 | 4/4 |\n| `sandbox_quoting` | 2/2 | 2/2 |\n| `readonly_home` | 5/5 | 5/5 |\n| `process_bounds_and_services` | 3/3 | 3/3 |\n| `lsp_honesty` | 13/13 | 13/13 |\n| `harness` | 90/90 | 90/90 |\n| `execution_tracking` | not run | 20/20 |\n| `fault_kill_mid_tool_call` | not run | 1/1 |\n\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` ran clean on Node 22 (I did not run it on 24).\n- `cargo test --release`: 53 + 386 + 1 + 4 + 1 passed, 0 failed. This includes the new `credential_names_match_the_typescript_rules` and `run_command_does_not_inherit_credentials`.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` was clean. All runs used the isolated CARGO_TARGET_DIR and a throwaway HOME.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I did not run the full `npm test` suite (needs the `SUITE` claim), only the related files above.\n- The Docker sandbox branch is unchanged. It does not forward the host env by default, but I did not test it.\n- The docs say to scrub \"keys from the credential authority in `client.ts`\". The authority holds the whole operator environment plus `config.env`, so I scrubbed `config.env` keys plus the credential name patterns instead.\n- Credential files under HOME (`.ssh`, `.aws`, `.npmrc`, `config.env` itself) are still readable by commands. Only inherited variables are scrubbed.\n\n**Reference coding.** XERJ was active, but its corpora (opencode, awesome-ai-system-prompts, serverless-workflow-spec) returned nothing relevant for env scrubbing, so I used no retrieved code.\n- **Took (from this repo):** the shape of `buildMcpEnvironment`, `buildVerifierEnvironment` and `buildLspEnvironment`. That means the operator-only passthrough via `operatorSetting`, trailing `*` prefixes, and dropping proxies that embed credentials.\n- **Borrowed (from memory, not verified against source):** Codex CLI's `shell_environment_policy` idea of pattern exclusion plus explicit include.\n- **Rejected:** an allow list like the verifier's, because agent commands need an ordinary toolchain environment; and shipping a full env over RPC.\n\n**User-visible change and proposed CHANGELOG.md entry** (I did not edit CHANGELOG.md, which is a hot file)\n- Fixed: Commands run through `run_command` no longer inherit credentials from the Nexus process. Variables from `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, plus anything named like a key, token, secret or password, `AWS_*`, `GH_TOKEN` and similar, are removed from the command environment, including inside the write-mode bwrap sandbox. To pass a variable through deliberately, list its name in `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH` (operator environment or `config.env` only). Commands that relied on `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `GH_TOKEN` and similar must now opt in.\n\nAll five claims I took (`SLICE_HARDENING_S1` and four `FILE_*`) are released, renamed with a `.released-&lt;timestamp&gt;` suffix, and logged in `nexus-claims.log`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>145143</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>55</tool_uses><duration_ms>1240006</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"ef4be5bb-7564-4c93-a7ad-02f03cfe2e86","deliveryId":"1d425f5d-3e92-4ad4-b8f7-cddc0b16ea96"}
