ironment, including inside the write-mode bwrap sandbox. To pass a variable through deliberately, list its name in `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH` (operator environment or `config.env` only). Commands that relied on `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `GH_TOKEN` and similar must now opt in.\n\nAll five claims I took (`SLICE_HARDENING_S1` and four `FILE_*`) are released, renamed with a `.released-&lt;timestamp&gt;` suffix, and logged in `nexus-claims.log`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>145143</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>55</tool_uses><duration_ms>1240006</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
