{"parentUuid":"4c2619ba-718c-45f6-a480-634190076a2e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5F3jbLsyWDnyV5wVLTh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Slice 1 passed 11 of 11 on both Node versions with bwrap present, so the sandbox tests actually ran. Slice 2 is next, building on Slice 1's branch, and I'm adding a PID namespace so the sandbox hides the parent's /proc entries.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":772310,"output_tokens":3857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":752},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3857,"cache_read_input_tokens":772310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch5F3jDXYCnRsQ5kiX7EX","requestRef":"4fcf44b3-902d-4f9a-a102-09119562c69f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"af73826e-d4a3-4685-a518-ef6ad64df2d9","timestamp":"2026-11-15T19:11:04.338Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"af73826e-d4a3-4685-a518-ef6ad64df2d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5F3jbLsyWDnyV5wVLTh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ARHwb54NwZ6sRh8tCZXngK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hardening slice 2: confine write-mode sandbox","prompt":"You are implementing Slice 2 of a security-hardening task in the nexus-code repository (TypeScript CLI in `cli/`, Rust core in `core/`), test-first, in your own git worktree. A static review of main found the defect below; VERIFY it on the base before fixing (reproduce it) and report honestly if something does not reproduce.\n\nBASE: this slice builds on Slice 1, which is a LOCAL branch not on origin: `v1/hardening-s1-command-env` (head 954c601a, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard1). Slice 1 added `cli/src/command_env.ts` (`buildCommandEnvironment`, `isCredentialName`), made `tools.ts` start harness-core and the spawnSync fallback with the scrubbed env, and made the write-mode bwrap branch in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` use `--clearenv` + `--setenv` for the scrubbed variables; `core/src/runner.rs` has `is_credential_name`. Read that commit (`git show 954c601a`) first and build on it; do not redo it.\n\nGROUND RULES (from AGENTS.md; read it, docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 first):\n- Worktree: `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2 -b v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine v1/hardening-s1-command-env && ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cli/node_modules /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2/cli/node_modules`. Never edit ~/nexus-code itself. Claim the slice and hot files (cli/src/sandbox.ts, cli/src/tools.ts) under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` exactly as docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md describes (atomic mkdir + owner.json + nexus-claims.log line) before editing; release the claims when done (\"released-<timestamp>\" naming, see `ls` of that directory). Check `git log` for foreign commits before each commit.\n- Isolate HOME for every test or probe: `HOME=$(mktemp -d)`. Never touch the real ~/.config/nexus, ~/.ssh or other real credential files: tests create SENTINEL files inside the temp HOME. `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2/core/target` (a worktree-local target) if you build Rust. Stop processes by their own pid, never `pkill -f`. Chain shell commands with &&; never `git stash`.\n- Do NOT push, tag, merge, publish or open a PR. Commit locally on your branch and leave it ready (trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`).\n- Reference coding: query XERJ per docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md (`systemctl --user is-active xerj`; first query can take over a minute) for how mature agents (Codex CLI's bubblewrap/seccomp sandbox, Claude Code, OpenHands, Aider, opencode, goose) build bwrap profiles (home masking, network off by default, die-with-parent, new-session, pid namespace); record what you took/borrowed/rejected in your final report and commit message; if unavailable write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" and use git grep.\n- Done means: regression tests that FAIL before the fix and pass after; affected test files pass on Node 22 AND 24 (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin` and `.../v24.21.0/bin` first on PATH); `npm --prefix cli run build` clean; `cargo test`/`cargo clippy` clean if Rust changed. bwrap is installed at /usr/bin/bwrap on this host; tests skip clearly if it is missing. Some tests fail on this host for host reasons (unbuilt Rust core: build it with `cd core && cargo build --release --offline` into the worktree-local target if a test needs core/target/release/harness-core; stray /tmp/.git): compare against the base before calling anything a defect. Preserve existing comments and unrelated code. Report as measured; say what you could not verify.\n\nSLICE 2: make write-mode `--sandbox` actually confine (High).\nProblem: in `cli/src/sandbox.ts`, the non-read-only bwrap branch (around lines 312-328) uses `--ro-bind / /`, so the whole host is readable, including `~/.ssh`, `~/.config/nexus`, `~/.aws` and `~/.gnupg`. The network is cut only when `network === false`, and `tools.ts:1594` passes `undefined` outside read-only mode. Egress approval covers only the fetch tool; shell `curl`/`wget` are never checked.\nFix:\n1. Mask `$HOME` in write mode the same way the read-only path does (`--tmpfs $HOME`). Then bind back read-only only the toolchain directories that real builds need. Detect them from `PATH` entries under `$HOME` and from a fixed list (`~/.cargo`, `~/.rustup`, `~/.nvm`, `~/.local/bin`, `~/.npm` caches, `~/.cache/pip`, `~/go/pkg`). Never bind `~/.ssh`, `~/.gnupg`, `~/.aws`, `~/.config/nexus`, `~/.config/gh`, `~/.netrc`, `~/.docker/config.json`, `~/.kube`, or browser profiles. Let the operator extend the allowlist (operator config only, read with `operatorSetting` like Slice 1's passthrough, never from a project .env), and show the effective mounts in `nexus doctor`.\n2. Turn the network off by default under `--sandbox` (`--unshare-net`). Add an explicit opt-in, such as `--sandbox-network` and/or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` (operator-only). In `review` mode, a command that needs the network asks for approval and the prompt says so. Under `--yes` the opt-in must still be explicit; do not turn the network on silently.\n3. Add `--die-with-parent` and `--new-session` to both bwrap branches. `ARCHITECTURE.md` already claims `--die-with-parent`; make that true. `--new-session` blocks TIOCSTI terminal injection. Check that PTY-mode commands still work with `--new-session`. If they do not, explain why and limit the change accordingly (report it).\n4. ADDITION from the owner's reviewer (confirmed by a probe): a scrubbed child process can still read its PARENT processes' environment through `/proc/<pid>/environ` (same uid; yama ptrace_scope=1 does not block that read), which holds the operator's credentials in the Nexus node process. Under `--sandbox`, add `--unshare-pid` and mount a fresh `--proc /proc` so host processes (and their environ) are not visible inside the sandbox; keep PTY mode working. Add a test: a sandboxed command cannot read the Nexus (parent) process's environ, using a fake variable in the test's own process environment (never a real credential).\n5. Keep the workspace bind writable, but see Slice 4/6 notes: do not weaken `.git` handling that exists today.\nTests (bwrap available; skip clearly if missing):\n- A sentinel file at `$HOME/.ssh/id_test` (inside a throwaway HOME) cannot be read from a sandboxed command; the same for `~/.config/nexus/config.env` sentinel.\n- `getent hosts example.com` or a connect to `1.1.1.1:53` fails by default and works with the opt-in (the opt-in test may be skipped if the host has no network; say so).\n- `cargo --version` and `node --version` still work when those toolchains live under `$HOME` (use PATH entries under the throwaway HOME pointing at symlinks or copies; do not rely on the real home).\n- A backgrounded child is gone after the parent is killed.\n- The /proc parent-environ test from item 4.\nRun `scripts/terminal-acceptance` and the evaluator tests as well (they use the sandbox and are the most likely to break); compare any failure against the base (Slice 1 branch) before calling it a regression.\n\nREPORT BACK (concise, one block): branch name and head SHA; what changed (files); whether each defect reproduced on the base (the exact observation); tests added with before/after result and pass/fail TOTALS on Node 22 and 24; results of scripts/terminal-acceptance and the evaluator tests; PTY and `--new-session` findings; anything you could not verify; every user-visible behaviour change (network off by default, masked HOME, pid namespace) with a proposed CHANGELOG.md entry (do not edit CHANGELOG.md, it is a hot file)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":772310,"output_tokens":3857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":752},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3857,"cache_read_input_tokens":772310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15305,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ARHwb54NwZ6sRh8tCZXngK":{"description":"Hardening slice 2: confine write-mode sandbox","prompt":"You are implementing Slice 2 of a security-hardening task in the nexus-code repository (TypeScript CLI in `cli/`, Rust core in `core/`), test-first, in your own git worktree. A static review of main found the defect below; VERIFY it on the base before fixing (reproduce it) and report honestly if something does not reproduce.\n\nBASE: this slice builds on Slice 1, which is a LOCAL branch not on origin: `v1/hardening-s1-command-env` (head 954c601a, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard1). Slice 1 added `cli/src/command_env.ts` (`buildCommandEnvironment`, `isCredentialName`), made `tools.ts` start harness-core and the spawnSync fallback with the scrubbed env, and made the write-mode bwrap branch in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` use `--clearenv` + `--setenv` for the scrubbed variables; `core/src/runner.rs` has `is_credential_name`. Read that commit (`git show 954c601a`) first and build on it; do not redo it.\n\nGROUND RULES (from AGENTS.md; read it, docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 first):\n- Worktree: `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2 -b v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine v1/hardening-s1-command-env && ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cl