{"parentUuid":"8b52c18b-06b9-46a0-a0da-9ddfd84910f2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01TCrhn1WDPL5Fj6zUhxZY7g","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"59ff1b03-161f-416c-9c7a-24e81cf0940f","timestamp":"2026-11-15T19:13:15.827Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"59ff1b03-161f-416c-9c7a-24e81cf0940f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5FDXDE9gm9g3z4mm5bD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three hardening slices are verified, and the fourth is in progress. All branches are local; nothing is pushed.\n\n**Slice 4: the worktree merge (head `ee0078a7`), the real vulnerability**\n- **Reproduced:** the legacy `mergeWorktree` ran Git inside the agent-writable worktree. A planted `.git` with `core.fsmonitor` or `core.hooksPath` ran code outside the worktree (hook and fsmonitor sentinels appeared).\n- **Fix:** it now refuses any worktree that isn't a verified linked worktree before running Git. Every later git call is pinned (hooks off, fsmonitor off, no prompts).\n- **Verified:** I ran the new tests against unfixed `main` myself, and all 4 fail there. After the fix, 118 of 118 pass on Node 22 and 24.\n- **Behaviour change:** your own git hooks no longer fire on Nexus's legacy worktree commit and merge, matching the newer path.\n- **Left as follow-up:** it didn't route this path through the `worktrunk` merge, and `evaluator.ts` still runs `git diff` in the evaluator workspace unguarded (low risk, unverified whether that workspace is agent-writable).\n\n**Slice 1: credentials in agent commands (head `954c601a`)**\n- **Reproduced:** `run_command \"env\"` printed the sentinel key unsandboxed, under bwrap and in the spawnSync fallback.\n- **Verified:** 11 of 11 pass on both Node versions with bwrap actually present.\n- **Gap I found and confirmed:** a scrubbed child can still read its parent processes' environment through `/proc/<pid>/environ` (same user, and `ptrace_scope=1` doesn't block it). Unsandboxed commands also still read `config.env`. Slice 1 removes what a command inherits, not what the user's own processes can read.\n- **Follow-ups:** I added a PID namespace to Slice 2, which the agent is now doing. The architecture doc (Slice 3) must say plainly that unsandboxed commands run as the same user.\n\n**Slices 6 and 7: `security.ts` (heads `7de595ed` and `4a09556f`)**\n- **Slice 6:** workspaces under `.env-tools/` or `id_rsa-backup/` were blocked wholesale, and that reproduced. Patterns now match workspace-relative paths.\n- **Verified:** with the Rust core built, 23 of 23 pass on both Node versions. The one test the agent saw failing was the unbuilt core, as it suspected.\n- **Slice 7:** `allowExternalSymlinks` was parsed and never read, and no doc promises it, so it is removed. No owner decision was needed.\n\n**Still to run, in your order:** Slice 2 (write-mode sandbox) is being built on Slice 1's branch. Then Slice 5 (Docker) and Slice 3 (docs). I'll write the CHANGELOG entries last, since the agents proposed them and didn't touch that file.\n\n`main` CI on `011bb6b3` is still in progress, so `main` isn't confirmed after the last merges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":782413,"output_tokens":1055,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1055,"cache_read_input_tokens":782413,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch5FDWtPxMdaLkWPaEoWo","requestRef":"1e18365c-e127-4cf2-959b-1a82859b9d32","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4e6958f-7f0d-4a5b-8138-5b6484f01926","timestamp":"2026-11-15T19:13:15.788Z","advisorModel":"clau