{"parentUuid":"76f8b7cc-ea26-4d76-a6ed-4f960c29e83a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5GV6obzaYQ15MvXK7nk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood: no pushes or PRs until every slice is built and validated. That means Slices 2, 5 and 3 as well, not only the four that are done. Then I open one PR per slice.\n\nWhere that stands:\n- **Validated, local only:** Slices 1, 4, 6 and 7 (branches `hard1`, `hard4`, `hard6`, `hard7`). I re-ran their tests myself on Node 22 and 24, and for Slice 4 I confirmed the fix by running its tests against unfixed `main`.\n- **Slice 2:** in progress, building the write-mode sandbox on Slice 1's branch. I'll review its bwrap profile and probe it myself.\n- **Slices 5 and 3:** queued behind Slice 2. Slice 5 and Slice 2 both edit `sandbox.ts`, and the docs have to describe Slice 2's final behaviour.\n\n**How I'll open the PRs once everything is validated:** the slices stack (Slice 2 builds on 1, and so on), so each PR targets the previous slice's branch to keep its diff to its own change. After each merges, the next is retargeted to `main`. Each PR gets the template sections, including the XERJ reference-coding record and the behaviour changes with the proposed CHANGELOG entry, and I'll merge in order, waiting for CI on `main` between merges.\n\nI'm waiting on the Slice 2 report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13,"cache_read_input_tokens":786580,"output_tokens":869,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":406},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":786580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5