{"parentUuid":"f9dfe696-f9fa-42da-b570-f4a82b172caf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5Ki3SADe7RVy8k44C3K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed: with the workspace set to $HOME, the sandbox leaks everything, since the writable bind re-exposes what the tmpfs mask hid. I'm sending the agent the exact reproduction and expected behaviour.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":800319,"output_tokens":1533,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":528},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1533,"cache_read_input_tokens":800319,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch5Ki39oPJYFjNnWio79r","requestRef":"565543c5-ea91-4043-af95-467d66fd587a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0f4370a-5e63-4928-894a-3973fb86d1bc","timestamp":"2026-11-15T20:12:08.385Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"a0f4370a-5e63-4928-894a-3973fb86d1bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5Ki3SADe7RVy8k44C3K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EoFXmQCrS7LFZjQjFficq7","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","summary":"Slice 2 gap: workspace=HOME re-exposes ~/.ssh","message":"Review of Slice 2 (a0a49daa): profile and tests look sound, and I re-read sandbox.ts. ONE required fix before this slice is done: a confinement hole when the WORKSPACE IS $HOME (or an ancestor of it / contains credential dirs). I reproduced it with your own wrapSandboxedCommand: throwaway HOME under /var/tmp with `.ssh/id_test` = SENTINEL-SSH and `proj/a.txt`. With workspace = $HOME/proj the sentinel is unreadable (good: \"No such file or directory\"), but with workspace = $HOME the command `cat $HOME/.ssh/id_test` prints SENTINEL-SSH: the writable workspace bind is applied on top of the `--tmpfs $HOME` mask and re-exposes everything under it (this is exactly what happens when an operator runs `nexus --sandbox` from their home directory). Probe script: /tmp/claude-1000/probe_home.mts (adjust paths; run with `HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx` from cli/).\nREQUIRED BEHAVIOUR: after the workspace bind, overlay every HOME_DENIED path (and HOME_MASKED_FILES, and the credential-bearing files/dirs your denied list covers) that lies INSIDE the bound workspace: a directory gets `--tmpfs <path>`, a file gets `--ro-bind /dev/null <path>`, only if it exists, so nothing from the denied list is readable even when the workspace is $HOME or contains it. The same applies when the workspace is an ancestor of $HOME (e.g. /home): the overlay set is the denied paths under HOME that fall within the workspace. Keep it a pure, testable function like sandboxHomeMounts and show the overlays in `nexus doctor` when relevant.\nTESTS (fail first on the current head): (a) workspace = throwaway $HOME: `.ssh/id_test` and a `.config/nexus/config.env` sentinel are unreadable; ordinary workspace files (e.g. `proj/a.txt`, a `.cargo` toolchain bind) still readable/writable as before; (b) workspace = $HOME/proj stays as today; (c) workspace = parent of the throwaway HOME (e.g. /var/tmp/<dir> containing home/): denied paths under it are masked. Re-run the sandbox and related test files on Node 22 AND 24, `npm --prefix cli run build`, and report the new head SHA with totals. Same rules as before (local only, no push/PR, claims, throwaway HOME, chain with &&).","type":"message","recipient":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Review of Slice 2 (a0a49daa): profile and tests l…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":800319,"output_tokens":1533,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":528},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1533,"cache_read_input_tokens":800319,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":5576,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EoFXmQCrS7LFZjQjFficq7":{"to":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","summary":"Slice 2 gap: workspace=HOME re-exposes ~/.ssh","message":"Review of Slice 2 (a0a49daa): profile and tests look sound, and I re-read sandbox.ts. ONE required fix before this slice is done: a confinement hole when the WORKSPACE IS $HOME (or an ancestor of it / contains credential dirs). I reproduced it with your own wrapSandboxedCommand: throwaway HOME under /var/tmp with `.ssh/id_test` = SENTINEL-SSH and `proj/a.txt`. With workspace = $HOME/proj the sentinel is unreadable (good: \"No such file or directory\"), but with workspace = $HOME the command `cat $HOME/.ssh/id_test` prints SENTINEL-SSH: the writable workspace bind is applied on top of the `--tmpfs $HOME` mask and re-exposes everything under it (this is exactly what happens when an operator runs `nexus --sandbox` from their home directory). Probe script: /tmp/claude-1000/probe_home.mts (adjust paths; run with `HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx` from cli/).\nREQUIRED BEHAVIOUR: after the workspace bind, overlay every HOME_DENIED path (and HOME_MASKED_FILES, and the credential-bearing files/dirs your denied list covers) that lies INSIDE the bound workspace: a directory gets `--tmpfs <path>`, a file gets `--ro-bind /dev/null <path>`, only if it exists, so nothing from the denied list is readable even when the workspace is $HOME or contains it. The same applies when the workspace is an ancestor of $HOME (e.g. /home): the overlay set is the denied paths under HOME that fall within the workspace. Keep it a pure, testable function like sandboxHomeMounts and show the overlays in `nexus doctor` when relevant.\nTESTS (fail first on the current head): (a) workspace = throwaway $HOME: `.ssh/id_test` and a `.config/nexus/config.env` sentinel are unreadable; ordinary workspace files (e.g. `proj/a.txt`, a `.cargo` toolchain bind) still readable/writable as before; (b) workspace = $HOME/proj stays as today; (c) workspace = parent of the throwaway HOME (e.g. /var/tmp/<dir> containing home/): denied paths under it are masked. Re-run the sandbox and related test files on Node 22 AND 24, `npm --prefix cli run build`, and report the new head SHA with totals. Same rules as before (local only, no push/PR, claims, throwaway HOME, chain with &&)."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch5Ki39oPJYFjNnWio79r","requestRef":"565543c5-ea91-4043-af95-467d66fd587a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","typ