{"parentUuid":"a44a506d-5745-430e-b61f-2315fb378fb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5KjKz7DS8iZA5m5AJ3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I sent Slice 2 back with the gap and the reproduction. The agent is resuming to fix it, with tests that fail first, and my probe's temporary directories are cleaned up.\n\nSlice 2 is not validated yet, so it blocks everything after it, including the PRs:\n- **Confirmed leak:** with the workspace at `$HOME` itself, a sentinel under `~/.ssh` is readable inside the sandbox. With the workspace at `$HOME/proj` it is correctly hidden. The fix overlays the credential paths that fall inside the workspace after the workspace is bound.\n- **Correction to what I said earlier:** the `/proc` parent-environment read does not reproduce through bwrap. The base already had `--unshare-pid` and a fresh `/proc`. My probe hit an unsandboxed child. That gap stands, but it belongs to unsandboxed commands, and Slice 3 will say so.\n- **Other review items:** the report also flags a few smaller notes. Commands lose `/dev/tty` under `--new-session`, so password prompts like `sudo` fail inside the sandbox. `~/.gitconfig` isn't bound, so commits lack the operator's identity. And the network opt-in can't be tested here because this host has no route.\n\nSlices 5 and 3 wait for the fixed Slice 2. I'm still not pushing or opening any PR until all seven slices are validated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":802442,"output_tokens":464,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":464,"cache_read_input_token