= an ancestor of `$HOME`, and a workspace that contains a credential directory.\n- `nexus doctor` (the `sandbox.confinement` check) lists the overlays when the workspace holds credential paths.\n- When the workspace is `$HOME`, the toolchain directories sit inside the writable bind, so they are writable there rather than read-only. That is inherent to binding `$HOME` writable.\n\n**Tests**\n- Four tests were added to `cli/test/sandbox_confine.test.ts`, for workspace = `$HOME`, `$HOME/proj`, an ancestor of `$HOME`, and the overlay function itself.\n- With the overlay function stubbed out (the old behaviour), three of the four failed: workspace = `$HOME`, ancestor, and the overlay function. Workspace = `$HOME/proj` passed, as intended.\n- With the fix all four pass, and `sandbox_confine.test.ts` is 13 of 13 on Node 22.\n- In the workspace = `$HOME` test, `.ssh` and `.config/nexus` are unreadable. `proj/a.txt` stays readable, a write to `proj/b.txt` lands on disk, and `cargo --version` still runs from a `.cargo/bin` on `PATH`.\n\n**Node 22 and 24 (47 related files; `npm --prefix cli run build` clean)**\n- **Node 22.22.2:** 200 of 200 pass, 0 fail.\n- **Node 24.21.0:** the aggregate run reports 710 pass, 21 fail, 9 skipped (740 total); it does not reach zero failures.\n- Those 21 fail identically on the S1 base `954c601a` on Node 24, so they are not caused by this slice. They are in `eval_dataset` (1), `eval_hardened` (4), `eval_harness` (6), `eval_integrity` (7), `eval_t3` (2) and `eval_version_probe_storage` (1).\n- At least one of them (`eval_version_probe_storage`) fails with \"requires the dedicated capped workspace fixture configured by CI\". I did not diagnose the other six files individually.\n- I did not re-run those files on Node 22 in isolation. They pass inside the 200 on Node 22, so the failures look specific to Node 24 on this host.\n- The totals differ between the two runs (200 vs 740) because of how the runner counts after failures, not because Node 24 ran different tests.\n\n**Other change in this commit**\n- My first commit had `config.ts` importing `sandbox.ts`, which created a cycle (`config` → `sandbox` → `command_env` → `config`). On Node 24 it made `readonly_home.test.ts` hang until the watchdog killed it.\n- It passed on Node 22 and on the earlier Node 24 run only by import-order luck.\n- I moved the `--sandbox-network` flag into a new import-free `cli/src/sandbox_network.ts`. After that, `readonly_home` (5 tests) passes on Node 24 alongside `sandbox_confine`.\n\n**Claims**\n- I re-took the slice, `FILE_cli_src_sandbox.ts`, `FILE_cli_src_doctor.ts` and `SUITE` for this fix and released them all, with log lines.\n- I removed the temporary base worktree.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>203850</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>104</tool_uses><duration_ms>8906609</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
