s-wt/hard2), which sits on Slice 1 `v1/hardening-s1-command-env` (954c601a). Slice 1 added `cli/src/command_env.ts` (`buildCommandEnvironment`, `isCredentialName`); Slice 2 reworked the bwrap branches in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` (HOME masking, `--unshare-net` by default with the operator opt-in `--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` via `sandboxNetworkEnabled()` in the import-free `cli/src/sandbox_network.ts`, `--die-with-parent`, `--new-session`, workspace overlays). Read `git show 954c601a a0a49daa cf3aff57 --stat` and the sandbox.ts diff first and build on them; reuse the SAME network opt-in for Docker; do not redo them, and do not create import cycles (config.ts must not import sandbox.ts; a cycle config -> sandbox -> command_env -> config already broke Node 24 once).\n\nGROUND RULES (from AGENTS.md; read it, docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 first):\n- Worktree: `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard5 -b v1/hardening-s5-docker v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine && ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cli/node_modules /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard5/cli/node_modules`. Never edit ~/nexus-code itself. Claim the slice and hot file (cli/src/sandbox.ts) under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` exactly as docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md describes (atomic mkdir + owner.json + nexus-claims.log line) before editing; release the claims when done (\"released-<timestamp>\" naming). Check `git log` for foreign commits before each commit.\n- Isolate HOME for every test or probe: `HOME=$(mktemp -d)`; never touch the real ~/.config/nexus or credential files. Stop processes by their own pid, never `pkill -f`. Chain shell commands with &&; never `git stash`.\n- Do NOT push, tag, merge, publish or open a PR. Commit locally and leave the branch ready (trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`).\n- Reference coding: query XERJ per docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md (`systemctl --user is-active xerj`; first query can take over a minute) for how mature agents (Codex CLI, OpenHands' Docker runtime, goose, opencode) harden `docker run` sandboxes (digest pins, cap-drop, no-new-privileges, read-only root, user mapping, network none); record what you took/borrowed/rejected in your final report and commit message; if unavailable write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" and use git grep.\n- Done means: regression tests that fail before the change and pass after; affected test files pass on Node 22 AND 24 (`~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin` and `.../v24.21.0/bin` first on PATH); `npm --prefix cli run build` clean. Some eval_* tests fail on Node 24 on this host for host reasons (a capped-workspace fixture that CI provides); compare against the base before calling anything a defect. If Docker is not usable on this host (`docker info`), unit-test the argv construction and say clearly that no container was run. Preserve existing comments and unrelated code. Report as measured.\n\nSLICE 5: harden the Docker sandbox (Low).\nIn `cli/src/sandbox.ts`, Docker branch (originally around lines 345-386):\n- Replace `alpine:latest` with a digest-pinned image. Make it operator-configurable (operator setting, read like the other operator-only settings, never from a project .env), and keep the pin in one place alongside the other pins. Find the real current digest of the chosen minimal image if you can reach the registry; if you cannot, say so and use a clearly marked placeholder that fails closed (no run) rather than an unpinned tag.\n- Add `--user $(id -u):$(id -g)`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default (same opt-in as Slice 2), `--pids-limit`, and `--read-only` with a writable tmpfs `/tmp`.\n- Pass the scrubbed environment from Slice 1 explicitly (`buildCommandEnvironment()`), with `--env` per variable and nothing inherited.\n- Remove the dead `mountMode` code; `readOnlyHost` returns before it is reached.\n- Update `dockerSandboxProbe` (around line 322 now) so it still passes with the new flags (the probe must use the same hardened flags and the pinned image, or be told why not).\nTests: argv-level tests that assert every flag above is present and that no unpinned `:latest` tag and no inherited environment remain; a test that the network opt-in changes `--network none`; if Docker is available, a real run proving a write outside the workspace/tmp fails and the sentinel env var does not appear.\n\nREPORT BACK (concise, one block): branch name and head SHA; what changed (files); the image pin and how you obtained it; tests added with before/after result and pass/fail TOTALS on Node 22 and 24; whether a container was actually run; anything you could not verify; user-visible behaviour change with a proposed CHANGELOG.md entry (do not edit CHANGELOG.md).","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/ae50b812197dda7b2.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4bda2f7e-bfe8-4cbc-892d-649f49a74a79","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"9ea01a53-d7ee-4fe2-b9fc-2aac534ea391","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5TCeZs7KS9bH3URvxLC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0179YHPbhXSfZo2NMbLRvUHq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hardening slice 3: docs match the code","prompt":"You are implementing Slice 3 (documentation) of a security-hardening task in the nexus-code repository, in your own git worktree. Everything you write must match the CODE; read the code, do not trust summaries.\n\nBASE: build on LOCAL branches that are not on origin: `v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine` (head cf3aff57, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2), which sits on Slice 1 `v1/hardening-s1-command-env` (954c601a). Read `git show 954c601a a0a49daa cf3aff57` (commit messages and diffs) first. Slice 5 (Docker hardening: digest-pinned image, `--user`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default with the same opt-in as the bwrap sandbox, `--pids-limit`, `--read-only` with a tmpfs `/tmp`, scrubbed env passed with `--env`) is being implemented in parallel on its own branch; describe Docker in the docs per that intended behaviour but mark the Docker details so they can be reconciled with the final Slice 5 code (list them in your report).\n\nGROUND RULES (from AGENTS.md; read it, docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 first):\n- Worktree: `cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git worktree add /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard3 -b v1/hardening-s3-docs v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine`. Never edit ~/nexus-code itself. Claim the slice and hot files (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/USER_MANUAL.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md) under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` exactly as docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md describes (atomic mkdir + owner.json + nexus-claims.log line) before editing; release them when done (\"released-<timestamp>\" naming). Check `git log` for foreign commits before each commit.\n- Isolate HOME for any probe: `HOME=$(mktemp -d)`; never touch the real ~/.config/nexus. Chain shell commands with &&; never `git stash`.\n- Do NOT push, tag, merge, publish or open a PR. Commit locally and leave the branch ready (trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`).\n- Reference coding: docs-only change; write \"Not applicable (documentation only)\" in your report.\n\nSLICE 3: make ARCHITECTURE.md match the code (Medium). Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §3, items 3 and 6:\n- State that egress approval covers network tools, not shell commands. The shell is confined only by the sandbox's network setting.\n- Describe exactly what write-mode `--sandbox` masks and binds (HOME as an empty tmpfs, the read-only toolchain bind-backs and the operator list `NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY`, the credential-location overlays when the workspace contains them, `/run/user/<uid>` and the docker socket hidden, cargo credential files masked), what the environment contains (the scrubbed command environment of Slice 1, the `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH` opt-in, operator-only), and the network default with its opt-in (`--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1`; `--yes` does not enable it; read-only mode is always offline).\n- Fix the `--die-with-parent` claim to match the code after Slice 2 (it is now on both bwrap branches; also `--new-session`, `--unshare-pid` with a fresh `/proc`). Note the user-visible consequence of `--new-session`: a command that opens `/dev/tty` directly (sudo, password prompts) fails inside the sandbox.\n- BE HONEST about limits, as confirmed by probes: (a) WITHOUT `--sandbox`, a command runs as the same user as Nexus; the scrubbed environment keeps credentials out of what it inherits (`env`, `printenv`), but such a command can still read the operator's files (for example `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, `~/.ssh`) and its parent processes' environment through `/proc/<pid>/environ` (same user; yama `ptrace_scope=1` does not block that read). Inside the bwrap sandbox host processes are invisible. (b) Under `--sandbox`, files outside `$HOME` are still readable (`--ro-bind / /`), e.g. other users' home directories or world-readable system files; only `$HOME` and the listed locations are masked. (c) The sandbox does not protect against a command that the operator approves with the network opt-in enabled. State these plainly; do not overclaim.\n- Also document the user-visible changes of the OTHER hardening slices where the docs describe the affected behaviour: Slice 4 (the legacy worktree merge runs Git pinned and no longer fires the repository's own hooks; a tampered worktree `.git` is refused), Slice 6 (protected paths match workspace-relative paths, so a workspace under a directory named like `.env-tools` is no longer blocked wholesale), Slice 7 (the unread `allowExternalSymlinks` policy key was removed; files that still set it load and the key is ignored).\nUpdate `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `README.md` (the \"Defense-in-Depth Sandboxing\" and \"auto mode\" bullets) and `CHANGELOG.md` to match. For CHANGELOG.md add entries under the Unreleased / next-version heading (see how the file is organised) using these proposals, adjusted to the code you read:\n * Security (Slice 1): Commands run through `run_command` no longer inherit credentials from the Nexus process. Variables from `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, plus anything named like a key, token, secret or password, `AWS_*`, `GH_TOKEN` and similar, are removed from the command environment, including inside the write-mode bwrap sandbox. To pass a variable through deliberately, list its name in `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH` (operator environment or `config.env` only). Commands that relied on `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `GH_TOKEN` and similar must now opt in.\n * Security (Slice 2): write-mode `--sandbox` now actually confines. `$HOME` is masked (`~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `~/.gnupg`, `~/.config/nexus` unreadable, also when the workspace is `$HOME`); only toolchain directories are mounted read-only (extend with `NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY`); the network is off by default (`--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` to opt in; `--yes` does not imply it); commands start in a new session (no `/dev/tty`) and die with the runner; `nexus doctor` lists the effective mounts.\n * Security (Slice 4): the legacy task-worktree merge refuses a worktree whose `.git` was replaced, and runs Git with hooks and fsmonitor disabled; a planted `core.fsmonitor` or hook in an agent-writable worktree no longer runs code outside it. The repository's own hooks no longer fire on that commit and merge.\n * Fixed (Slice 6): protected-path matching is relative to the workspace root, so projects under directories such as `~/.env-tools/` are no longer blocked wholesale; symlinks to protected targets are still refused.\n * Removed (Slice 7): the unread `allowExternalSymlinks` policy key (files that set it still load).\n * Security (Slice 5, Docker): list under Slice 5's intended behaviour above, marked for reconciliation.\nRun `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` (both must pass). Where a doc claims something about the code that you cannot confirm by reading the code, say so in your report instead of keeping or inventing the claim.\n\nREPORT BACK (concise, one block): branch name and head SHA; files changed; every statement you changed and which code line confirms it; the Docker details to reconcile with Slice 5; the results of both check scripts; anything you could not verify."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":932,"cache_read_input_tokens":813004,"output_tokens":6012,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":913},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":932,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"infer