{"parentUuid":"70e53b69-a2d1-461a-be07-e867dd336c6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5TFvNiUkgYoXXXB2o8R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Slices 5 and 3 are running in parallel on top of the probe-verified Slice 2 head `cf3aff57`, each in its own worktree and local-only.\n\n- **Slice 5 (Docker):** the image gets a digest pin, or a placeholder that fails closed (it never falls back to an unpinned tag). It also gets `--user`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default (same opt-in as the bwrap sandbox), `--pids-limit`, a read-only root with a tmpfs `/tmp`, and the scrubbed environment from Slice 1. It must not recreate the import cycle that hung Node 24 earlier.\n- **Slice 3 (docs):** it describes exactly what write-mode `--sandbox` masks and binds, the scrubbed environment, and the network default. It states the confirmed limits plainly: without `--sandbox`, a command can still read your files and its parent's `/proc` environment; files outside `$HOME` stay readable under the sandbox. It also carries the CHANGELOG entries for every slice, including the hook behaviour change from Slice 4. It will list the Docker details to reconcile with Slice 5's final code.\n\nMy own test run of the Slice 2 files on both Node versions is still going in the background. If it finds anything, I re-base these two. Nothing is pushed, and the PRs wait until all seven slices are validated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6799,"cache_read_input_tokens":813936,"output_tokens":467,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":467,"cache_re