{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-15T21:53:19.853Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a189534fbd1917a64</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0179YHPbhXSfZo2NMbLRvUHq</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a189534fbd1917a64.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Hardening slice 3: docs match the code\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Slice 3 is committed locally on `v1/hardening-s3-docs`, head `4a4f67c0c7ed945f4d2dc7e1980c4a4b6ffd8d9b`, on top of cf3aff57. Nothing was pushed. Both check scripts pass: `check_doc_versions.mjs` says \"consistent with latest stable v1.2.0\", and `check_requirements.mjs` reports 123 rows and exits 0. Reference coding: Not applicable (documentation only). I held the claims and released them as `released-&lt;timestamp&gt;`.\n\n**Files changed** (worktree `/home/mike/nexus-wt/hard3`): `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`. The CHANGELOG had no Unreleased heading, so I added `## [Unreleased]` above v1.2.0, with Security, Fixed and Removed sections.\n\n**Statements changed, and the code that confirms them**\n- **Egress covers network tools, not shell commands.** `run_command` has effect `exec` (`cli/src/core/capability_definitions/proc.ts`). The `egress` capabilities are `fetch_web`, `search_web` and `browser_*` (`net.ts`, `browser.ts`). The origin approval happens at `cli/src/agent.ts:5603` and `:5765`.\n- **Write-mode bwrap mounts.** HOME as an empty tmpfs, the toolchain bind-backs, `NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY`, the refused credential locations, the masked cargo credential files, `/run/user/&lt;uid&gt;` and the docker socket are all in `sandbox.ts` (`HOME_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULTS`, `HOME_DENIED`, `HOME_MASKED_FILES`, `sandboxHomeMounts`, and the write-mode bwrap branch).\n- **Credential overlays when the workspace holds them** come from `sandboxWorkspaceOverlays` in the same file, applied after the workspace bind.\n- **Environment.** The write-mode bwrap branch does `--clearenv` plus `--setenv` of `buildCommandEnvironment()`. The passthrough variable `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH` is read through `operatorSetting` in `cli/src/command_env.ts`. The second layer is in `core/src/runner.rs`, per the S1 commit message.\n- **Network.** Off unless `sandboxNetworkEnabled()` or `options.network === true` (`sandboxNetworkEnabled` in `sandbox.ts`, plus `networkAllowed` in the bwrap branch). The `--sandbox-network` flag is wired in `config.ts` and warns when used without `--sandbox`. `--yes` is not consulted anywhere on that path. Read-only mode passes `network: false` (`tools.ts:1570` and `:1599`).\n- **Process isolation.** The shared line `--unshare-pid --die-with-parent --new-session` applies to both bwrap branches, with a fresh `/proc` mounted on both. The `/dev/tty` consequence follows from `--new-session`.\n- **Item 7 `--die-with-parent` claim** now says it covers both branches and names `--new-session`.\n- **Slice 4, 6 and 7 behaviour** comes from the commit messages and diffs of `ee0078a7`, `7de595ed` and `4a09556f`, which I read.\n- **The three stated limits** (the sandbox masks only `$HOME` and the listed paths; unsandboxed commands run as your user; the network opt-in is unprotected) are written as plain limits, taken from your probe results and `--ro-bind / /`. I cannot re-verify the probe results from the code, including the `/proc/&lt;pid&gt;/environ` and Yama `ptrace_scope=1` point.\n\n**Docker details to reconcile with Slice 5**\n- Branch `v1/hardening-s5-docker` has no commits yet, and the Docker branch in `sandbox.ts` only has `--network none`. Everything else is the intended behaviour you gave me.\n- Where it appears: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §3 item 6 (a bullet marked \"reconcile with the final hardening Slice 5 code\"), the `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` sandbox entry, and the CHANGELOG Security entry.\n- The details to check are: digest-pinned image, `--user`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default with the same opt-in as bwrap, `--pids-limit`, `--read-only` with a tmpfs `/tmp`, and the scrubbed environment passed with `--env`.\n\n**Could not verify**\n- Slices 4, 6 and 7 are not on my branch. I described them from their commit messages and diffs, not from code on my branch.\n- I did not confirm whether the `nexus worktree merge` command uses the legacy `WorktreeManager.mergeWorktree` path. The manual therefore names `WorktreeManager.mergeWorktree` for `--worktree` task worktrees rather than the command.\n- I did not run the sandbox or any probe, because this slice is docs only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>114273</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>137857</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
