{"parentUuid":"1f334b61-8be5-4438-94bd-15c981efa9f0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Bs6BJ5CtDQPSkNsYTwxZPj","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":294},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0cc81cbd-0ee9-4b25-99fb-8b74473d8ec1","timestamp":"2026-11-15T21:53:29.943Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"1f334b61-8be5-4438-94bd-15c981efa9f0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"92865852-6440-4cfa-b230-3ed24fb21e28","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bs6BJ5CtDQPSkNsYTwxZPj","type":"tool_result","content":"4a4f67c0\n CHANGELOG.md         | 17 +++++++++++++++++\n README.md            |  7 ++++---\n docs/ARCHITECTURE.md | 14 +++++++++++---\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md  | 18 +++++++++++++-----\n 4 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n-3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress\n+3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress\n-6. **Container sandbox and argv isolation.** `--sandbox` confines execution using Linux Bubblewrap (`bwrap`) or Docker. The sandbox argv is constructed as a direct array without shell wrapping (REQ-SEC-109), preventing shell escaping flaws on complex workspace paths. In `--read-only` mode, `$HOME` is mounted as `--tmpfs $HOME`,\n-7. **Process group lifecycle and residual setsid escape risk.** The runner registers child process groups at spawn and terminates entire groups (`killpg`) on turn cancel, client crash, or process shutdown (REQ-AGT-109, REQ-SEC-106). Background services explicitly registered survive turn cancel but are cleaned on client exit. *L\n+6. **Container sandbox and argv isolation.** `--sandbox` confines execution using Linux Bubblewrap (`bwrap`) or Docker. The sandbox argv is constructed as a direct array without shell wrapping (REQ-SEC-109), preventing shell escaping flaws on complex workspace paths. The write-mode `bwrap` sandbox (`cli/src/sandbox.ts`) is buil\n+   - *Filesystem:* the host root is bound read-only (`--ro-bind / /`, remounted read-only) with a fresh `/dev`, `/proc` and an empty `/tmp`; the workspace is bound writable. `$HOME` is replaced by an empty tmpfs, so `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `~/.gnupg`, `~/.config/nexus` and browser profiles do not exist inside. Only toolchain direct\n+   - *Environment:* `--clearenv`, then only the scrubbed command environment (`cli/src/command_env.ts`) is set. Variables that came from `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, names that look like credentials (`*_API_KEY`, `*_TOKEN`, `*_SECRET`, `*_PASSWORD`, `AWS_*`, `GH_TOKEN`, `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, ...) and proxy URLs with embedded creden\n+   - *Network:* off by default (`--unshare-net`; Docker `--network none`). The operator opts in with `--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` in the operator environment. `--yes` does not enable it. `--sandbox-network` without `--sandbox` has no effect and warns. `--read-only` mode is always offline.\n+   - *Process isolation:* `--unshare-pid` with a fresh `/proc` (host processes and their `/proc/<pid>/environ` are invisible), `--die-with-parent` (every descendant dies with the runner) and `--new-session` (no controlling terminal, so the command cannot inject keystrokes into the operator's terminal). These flags are on both t\n+   - *Docker (reconcile with the final hardening Slice 5 code):* the intended behaviour is a digest-pinned image, a non-root `--user`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default with the same opt-in as `bwrap`, `--pids-limit`, `--read-only` with a tmpfs `/tmp`, and the scrubbed environment\n+   - In `--read-only` mode, `$HOME` is mounted as `--tmpfs $HOME` and the host root is not exposed (REQ-SEC-104); without bwrap, strict path confinement rejects paths outside the workspace.\n+\n+   *Limits, stated plainly:* (a) **Without `--sandbox`** a command runs as the same user as Nexus. The scrubbed environment keeps credentials out of what the command inherits (`env`, `printenv`), but the command can still read the operator's files (for example `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, `~/.ssh`) and the environment of its p\n+7. **Process group lifecycle and residual setsid escape risk.** The runner registers child process groups at spawn and terminates entire groups (`killpg`) on turn cancel, client crash, or process shutdown (REQ-AGT-109, REQ-SEC-106). Background services explicitly registered survive turn cancel but are cleaned on client exit. *L\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e654a059-58f9-470b-b851-34ba3a21a5a5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T21:53:30.208Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"4a4f67c0\n CHANGELOG.md         | 17 +++++++++++++++++\n README.md            |  7 ++++---\n docs/ARCHITECTURE.md | 14 +++++++++++---\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md  | 18 +++++++++++++-----\n 4 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n-3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress\n+3. **Approvals and posture defaults.** Per amended DEC-01, unset permission mode defaults to `review` regardless of folder trust. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands while retaining first-use egress approval per origin; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` enable full access and bypass approval prompts, including egress\n-6. **Container sandbox and argv isolation.** `--sandbox` confines execution using Linux Bubblewrap (`bwrap`) or Docker. The sandbox argv is constructed as a direct array without shell wrapping (REQ-SEC-109), preventing shell escaping flaws on complex workspace paths. In `--r