{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-15T21:55:14.631Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae50b812197dda7b2</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01MWsVCSNvR3uo92WCDWwQhP</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/ae50b812197dda7b2.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Hardening slice 5: Docker sandbox\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Slice 5 is committed locally; nothing was pushed.**\n\n**Branch and head:** `v1/hardening-s5-docker`, head `a674f152`, one commit on top of Slice 2 head `cf3aff57`. Worktree is `/home/mike/nexus-wt/hard5`. Both claims were taken and released.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `cli/src/sandbox.ts`\n- `cli/test/sandbox_docker.test.ts` (new)\n\nThe base state matched your description: `alpine:latest` and `mountMode` were present, and the network opt-in already applied to Docker. No import cycle was added.\n\n**What changed in the Docker branch:**\n- **Image:** `DOCKER_SANDBOX_IMAGE` is digest-pinned and lives in one place in `sandbox.ts`. The operator can override it with `NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE` (operator environment or `config.env`, read via `operatorSetting`, never a project `.env`). An override that is not `name@sha256:&lt;64 hex&gt;` is refused: it returns `sandboxed:false` with a warning and no container starts. `tools.ts` already treats that as a failure when a sandbox was requested.\n- **Flags:** `--user &lt;uid&gt;:&lt;gid&gt;`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--pids-limit 512`, `--read-only`, and `--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,size=256m`.\n- **Network:** `--network none` unless `--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is set. `network:false` always keeps it off.\n- **Environment:** one `--env NAME=value` per variable from `buildCommandEnvironment()`, nothing inherited. `HOME`, `PATH` and `TMPDIR` are replaced with container paths because the host values name paths that don't exist in the container.\n- **Cleanup:** the dead `mountMode` code is removed.\n- **Probe:** `probeDockerSandbox` goes through the same wrapper, so it uses the hardened flags and the pinned image. I raised its timeout from 15s to 60s so a first pull of the pinned image doesn't make it fail silently.\n\n**Image pin:** `alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea410b9215eaee7976ba6c0639039b444be8e5d638f7abbada189971eb2`. It is the multi-arch index digest, from `docker buildx imagetools inspect alpine:3.23` against the registry on 2026-11-15. I then pulled it by digest successfully.\n\n**Tests** (`cli/test/sandbox_docker.test.ts`, 7 tests):\n- Argv-level:\n  - Every flag is present.\n  - The image is pinned, with no `:latest` or bare `alpine`.\n  - Only scrubbed env vars appear, a sentinel `*_TOKEN` is absent, and there is no `-e` or `--env-file`.\n  - The network opt-in (flag and env var) removes `--network none`; the default and `network:false` keep it.\n  - An unpinned override fails closed.\n  - No `mountMode` remains.\n- Real container run:\n  - A write to `/` fails.\n  - `/tmp` and workspace writes succeed.\n  - The uid matches the host user.\n  - `CapEff` is zero.\n  - The sentinel is absent from both `env` and `/proc/self/environ`.\n  - The network is unreachable by default.\n- Before the change (Node 22, base `sandbox.ts` with the two new constants stubbed): 5 of 7 failed, 2 passed. The two passes are the network opt-in, which already worked on the base, and the default-no-network container test, which the base's `--network none` also satisfied.\n- After the change:\n\n| Run | Result |\n|---|---|\n| New file, Node 24 | 7/7 |\n| Four files together (`sandbox_docker`, `sandbox_confine`, `sandbox_quoting`, `command_env`), Node 22 | 26/26 |\n| Same four files, Node 24 | 26/26 |\n\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` is clean.\n- I did not run the full suite or the `eval_*` tests.\n\n**Host note:** `sandbox_quoting` first failed because `hard5` had no Rust core build. I symlinked the gitignored `core/target` to the one in `hard2`, and it passed after that.\n\n**Container run:** yes. Docker 29.9.3 is usable on this host, and the real-container tests ran against the pinned image.\n\n**XERJ:** reachable, but the goose and opencode corpora returned nothing relevant to `docker run` hardening, so I used no retrieved code.\n- **Took:** the standard hardening checklist (cap-drop ALL, no-new-privileges, read-only root plus tmpfs, non-root user, network none, pids limit, digest pin), from memory of OpenHands/Codex practice.\n- **Rejected:** custom seccomp/AppArmor profiles (Docker's default profile is kept) and `--memory`/`--cpus` limits (no operator setting yet).\n\n**Not verified:**\n- Only linux/amd64 was run.\n- Non-root user, `--read-only` and an unwritable `/tmp` for images that expect root are untested beyond the alpine shell.\n- Rootless Docker uid mapping is untested.\n- The 512-pid limit is a guess and has not been tuned against real builds.\n\n**Behaviour change and proposed CHANGELOG.md entry:**\n&gt; Security: the `--sandbox docker` engine now runs a digest-pinned image (alpine 3.23) as the invoking uid with all capabilities dropped, `no-new-privileges`, a read-only root plus a tmpfs `/tmp`, a 512-process limit, and no network unless `--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` is set. Only the scrubbed command environment reaches the container. `NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE` (operator setting) may substitute another image but it must be digest-pinned, otherwise no container is started. Commands that wrote outside the workspace and `/tmp`, relied on root, or used the network will now fail in Docker mode.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>93439</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>271220</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
