{"parentUuid":"4f985db7-2fc3-4ac1-ab6f-935baf3eeb01","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1f26fbd9-9f60-4d4c-a64c-0fc450d79361","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015iUKrTQgt1qsL4BTQ7kRvR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Resuming agent ae50b81\",\"resumedAgentId\":\"ae50b812197dda7b2\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"ae50b812197dda7b2\",\"name\":\"ae50b812197dda7b2\",\"ref\":\"618259\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"7c3b48fc-315f-41e2-9041-ef03e223ecac","timestamp":"2026-11-15T21:56:11.565Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Resuming agent ae50b81","resumedAgentId":"ae50b812197dda7b2","revivedAgentId":"ae50b812197dda7b2","pin":{"id":"ae50b812197dda7b2","name":"ae50b812197dda7b2","ref":"618259"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4f985db7-2fc3-4ac1-ab6f-935baf3eeb01","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"5b957abddea035dcdc75227293f50b973b33d9881357d60dc815861c852ee40e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Docker branch has the same gap as bwrap: with the workspace at $HOME or above, ~/.ssh and ~/.config/nexus are readable in the container, though they're hidden when the workspace is $HOME/proj. I'm passing this back to the Slice 5 agent.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015iUKrTQgt1qsL4BTQ7kRvR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ae50b812197dda7b2","summary":"Slice 5 gap: Docker leaks when workspace is HOME","message":"Review of Slice 5 (a674f152): the argv, the digest pin (I verified it against the registry and the local image) and the 7 container tests all check out on Node 22 and 24. ONE required fix before this slice is done: the Docker branch has the SAME confinement hole I found in the bwrap branch (fixed there in cf3aff57 by `sandboxWorkspaceOverlays`). The Docker branch mounts the workspace read-write (`-v ws:ws`) and applies no credential overlays, so when the workspace is $HOME or an ancestor of it, credential files are readable inside the container. I reproduced it with a real container using your `wrapSandboxedCommand(..., {mode:\"docker\"})` and a throwaway HOME under /var/tmp (probe: /tmp/claude-1000/probe_docker.mts, run from cli/ with `HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx`): workspace=HOME/proj -> `~/.ssh/id_test` and `~/.config/nexus/config.env` hidden (good); workspace=HOME -> leaked=YES (SENTINEL-SSH and SENTINEL-NEXUS printed); workspace=PARENT-of-HOME -> leaked=YES.\nREQUIRED: apply `sandboxWorkspaceOverlays(absWorkspace)` (already exported from sandbox.ts, pure) to the Docker run: for each overlay that is a directory add `--tmpfs <path>` (use options like `rw,nosuid,nodev,size=1m` or ro as appropriate), and for each file add `-v /dev/null:<path>:ro`, placed so they take effect over the workspace mount (Docker orders mounts by destination depth; verify with the real container, not by reading). Also mask the docker socket and `/run/user/<uid>` equivalents only if they could be inside a mounted workspace (they cannot under -v of the workspace alone: say so if you find it unnecessary). Keep symlink handling consistent with the bwrap overlays (overlay the target when it lies inside the workspace).\nTESTS (fail first on the current head, real container): workspace = throwaway HOME: `.ssh/id_test` and `.config/nexus/config.env` sentinels unreadable inside the container while `proj/a.txt` stays readable and a write to the workspace still works; workspace = parent of the throwaway HOME: same; workspace = HOME/proj unchanged. Use a throwaway HOME under /var/tmp with permissive modes (the container runs as your uid so modes matter little, but keep it deterministic). Re-run `sandbox_docker`, `sandbox_confine`, `sandbox_quoting`, `command_env` on Node 22 AND 24, `npm --prefix cli run build`, report the new head SHA and totals. Same rules as before (local only, no push/PR, claims, throwaway HOME, chain with &&). Also update your CHANGELOG proposal if the user-visible text changes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
