{"parentUuid":"345044c9-f9d6-4f01-ab47-a508d681adae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5V4hXEbvS6kBjRMkrmf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The orphans are gone: 17 killed and no test `cat` left. Two other `bwrap` processes remain that aren't from this test, and I'm leaving them. Now I'm sending Slice 2 the evidence and the decision."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":867484,"output_tokens":1527,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1527,"cache_read_input_tokens":867484,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch5V4h9utYTy2q7h7F4Xm","requestRef":"046f9896-b6fd-47e4-9aa7-17c3f9d708c8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d3e1980c-d9d9-4bee-a677-4d2c72464ae6","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:14:46.585Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"d3e1980c-d9d9-4bee-a677-4d2c72464ae6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5V4hXEbvS6kBjRMkrmf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wm8p4cX1qwYAxPd4tNKu5x","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","summary":"Slice 2: --new-session causes hang and orphans; remove it","message":"Review result for Slice 2 (cf3aff57): the workspace=HOME fix verified (my probe: all three layouts hidden, ordinary file readable). BUT I found a regression that blocks validation, and I have decided the fix (the owner authorised me to decide): REMOVE `--new-session` from BOTH bwrap branches. Keep `--die-with-parent` and `--unshare-pid` + fresh /proc.\nEVIDENCE (Node 22.22.2, load ~2): `test/readonly_home.test.ts` on Slice 1 (954c601a): 5 runs, 5/5 pass in ~5 s, no leaked processes. On your head cf3aff57: 3 runs, 2 of 3 HANG for the full timeout (rc=124, no output) and one passes in 5 s; each run leaks `bwrap ... -- cat pending-read.fifo` processes (I found 15+ orphans, some 2.7 h old, ppid=1, own session/pgid; I killed them by pid). In a scratch copy of cf3aff57 with `--new-session` removed: 5 runs, 5/5 pass in 5 s, zero leaked bwrap (count before=after). So `--new-session` is the cause: it makes the sandbox its own session (pgid=sid=pid), so the runner's process-group kill on cancel/deadline (killpg, REQ-AGT-109/REQ-SEC-106) no longer reaches the sandboxed command, which then survives cancellation and hangs the cancellation test. Your own test run on Node 22 reported 200/200; that run apparently did not hit it (it is intermittent) or predates the cycle fix.\n`--die-with-parent` itself is fine: I verified with a throwaway parent (spawn bwrap, parent exits or SIGKILLs itself) that the sandbox dies with the flag, with or without `--new-session`, and survives without the flag. TIOCSTI: this kernel has `dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti=0` (disabled for unprivileged since 6.2) and your own probe showed it failing with and without the flag, so dropping `--new-session` loses no verified protection; say so in a code comment (why it is NOT used: it defeats the runner's killpg; TIOCSTI is closed by kernel >= 6.2 default).\nDO: (1) remove `--new-session` from both branches and fix the comments; (2) update tests that assert it and add REGRESSION TESTS: (a) write-mode sandboxed command killed by cancel/deadline through the real RustCoreBridge leaves NO surviving process (mirror readonly_home's cancellation test for write mode; assert via pid, never `pgrep -f`), (b) loop readonly_home's cancellation scenario >= 5 times in a test or script to prove it is not intermittent; (3) re-run sandbox_confine, readonly_home (5x), command_env, sandbox_quoting, process_bounds_and_services and the wider related set on Node 22 AND 24, and report counts of leaked bwrap processes before/after (use `pgrep -x bwrap` and parent pid, never `pkill -f`/`pgrep -f` for decisions); `npm --prefix cli run build`. (4) Update your CHANGELOG proposal and any user-visible text: no `--new-session`, so `/dev/tty` works as before. Report the new head SHA and totals. Same rules (local only, no push/PR, claims, throwaway HOME, chain with &&). Also note for yourself: orphan processes from your earlier runs were my cleanup job this time; please clean up any you create by exact pid.","type":"message","recipient":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Review result for Slice 2 (cf3aff57): the workspa…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":867484,"output_tokens":1527,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1527,"cache_read_input_tokens":867484,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9598,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Wm8p4cX1qwYAxPd4tNKu5x":{"to":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","summary":"Slice 2: --new-session causes hang and orphans; remove it","message":"Review result for Slice 2 (cf3aff57): the workspace=HOME fix verified (my probe: all three layouts hidden, ordinary file readable). BUT I found a regression that blocks validation, and I have decided the fix (the owner authorised me to decide): REMOVE `--new-session` from BOTH bwrap branches. Keep `--die-with-parent` and `--unshare-pid` + fresh /proc.\nEVIDENCE (Node 22.22.2, load ~2): `test/readonly_home.test.ts` on Slice 1 (954c601a): 5 runs, 5/5 pass in ~5 s, no leaked processes. On your head cf3aff57: 3 runs, 2 of 3 HANG for the full timeout (rc=124, no output) and one passes in 5 s; each run leaks `bwrap ... -- cat pending-read.fifo` processes (I found 15+ orphans, some 2.7 h old, ppid=1, own session/pgid; I killed them by pid). In a scratch copy of cf3aff57 with `--new-session` removed: 5 runs, 5/5 pass in 5 s, zero leaked bwrap (count before=after). So `--new-session` is the cause: it makes the sandbox its own session (pgid=sid=pid), so the runner's process-group kill on cancel/deadline (killpg, REQ-AGT-109/REQ-SEC-106) no longer reaches the sandboxed command, which then survives cancellation and hangs the cancellation test. Your own test run on Node 22 reported 200/200; that run apparently did not hit it (it is intermittent) or predates the cycle fix.\n`--die-with-parent` itself is fine: I verified with a throwaway parent (spawn bwrap, parent exits or SIGKILLs itself) that the sandbox dies with the flag, with or without `--new-session`, and survives without the flag. TIOCSTI: this kernel has `dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti=0` (disabled for unprivileged since 6.2) and your own probe showed it failing with and without the flag, so dropping `--new-session` loses no verified protection; say so in a code comment (why it is NOT used: it defeats the runner's killpg; TIOCSTI is closed by kernel >= 6.2 default).\nDO: (1) remove `--new-session` from both branches and fix the comments; (2) update tests that assert it and add REGRESSION TESTS: (a) write-mode sandboxed command killed by cancel/deadline through the real RustCoreBridge leaves NO surviving process (mirror readonly_home's cancellation test for write mode; assert via pid, never `pgrep -f`), (b) loop readonly_home's cancellation scenario >= 5 times in a test or script to prove it is not intermittent; (3) re-run sandbox_confine, readonly_home (5x), command_env, sandbox_quoting, process_bounds_and_services and the wider related set on Node 22 AND 24, and report counts of leaked bwrap processes before/after (use `pgrep -x bwrap` and parent pid, never `pkill -f`/`pgrep -f` for decisions); `npm --prefix cli run build`. (4) Update your CHANGELOG proposal and any user-visible text: no `--new-session`, so `/dev/tty` works as before. Report the new head SHA and totals. Same rules (local only, no push/PR, claims, throwaway HOME, chain with &&). Also note for yourself: orphan processes from your earlier runs were my cleanup job this time; please clean up any you create by exact pid."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch5V4h9utYTy2q7h7F4Xm","requestRef":"046f9896-b6fd-47e4-9aa7-17c3f9d708c8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"73d5b9a2-0b25-47d5-9ca9-9c51eb4ceedd","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:14:56.195Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68