{"parentUuid":"73d5b9a2-0b25-47d5-9ca9-9c51eb4ceedd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1f26fbd9-9f60-4d4c-a64c-0fc450d79361","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wm8p4cX1qwYAxPd4tNKu5x","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Resuming agent a98715b\",\"resumedAgentId\":\"a98715b8bf34d44a7\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"a98715b8bf34d44a7\",\"name\":\"a98715b8bf34d44a7\",\"ref\":\"17ab35\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"9cc7754e-aeef-4a76-b9ee-3d2fc1555f15","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:14:56.558Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Resuming agent a98715b","resumedAgentId":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","revivedAgentId":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","pin":{"id":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","name":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","ref":"17ab35"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"73d5b9a2-0b25-47d5-9ca9-9c51eb4ceedd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"1699aecf0a1f002299657ad2115e5b22c9bc5f932bee8c46cfa3423fae6c0550","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The orphans are gone: 17 killed and no test `cat` left. Two other `bwrap` processes remain that aren't from this test, and I'm leaving them. Now I'm sending Slice 2 the evidence and the decision."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wm8p4cX1qwYAxPd4tNKu5x","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a98715b8bf34d44a7","summary":"Slice 2: --new-session causes hang and orphans; remove it","message":"Review result for Slice 2 (cf3aff57): the workspace=HOME fix verified (my probe: all three layouts hidden, ordinary file readable). BUT I found a regression that blocks validation, and I have decided the fix (the owner authorised me to decide): REMOVE `--new-session` from BOTH bwrap branches. Keep `--die-with-parent` and `--unshare-pid` + fresh /proc.\nEVIDENCE (Node 22.22.2, load ~2): `test/readonly_home.test.ts` on Slice 1 (954c601a): 5 runs, 5/5 pass in ~5 s, no leaked processes. On your head cf3aff57: 3 runs, 2 of 3 HANG for the full timeout (rc=124, no output) and one passes in 5 s; each run leaks `bwrap ... -- cat pending-read.fifo` processes (I found 15+ orphans, some 2.7 h old, ppid=1, own session/pgid; I killed them by pid). In a scratch copy of cf3aff57 with `--new-session` removed: 5 runs, 5/5 pass in 5 s, zero leaked bwrap (count before=after). So `--new-session` is the cause: it makes the sandbox its own session (pgid=sid=pid), so the runner's process-group kill on cancel/deadline (killpg, REQ-AGT-109/REQ-SEC-106) no longer reaches the sandboxed command, which then survives cancellation and hangs the cancellation test. Your own test run on Node 22 reported 200/200; that run apparently did not hit it (it is intermittent) or predates the cycle fix.\n`--die-with-parent` itself is fine: I verified with a throwaway parent (spawn bwrap, parent exits or SIGKILLs itself) that the sandbox dies with the flag, with or without `--new-session`, and survives without the flag. TIOCSTI: this kernel has `dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti=0` (disabled for unprivileged since 6.2) and your own probe showed it failing with and without the flag, so dropping `--new-session` loses no verified protection; say so in a code comment (why it is NOT used: it defeats the runner's killpg; TIOCSTI is closed by kernel >= 6.2 default).\nDO: (1) remove `--new-session` from both branches and fix the comments; (2) update tests that assert it and add REGRESSION TESTS: (a) write-mode sandboxed command killed by cancel/deadline through the real RustCoreBridge leaves NO surviving process (mirror readonly_home's cancellation test for write mode; assert via pid, never `pgrep -f`), (b) loop readonly_home's cancellation scenario >= 5 times in a test or script to prove it is not intermittent; (3) re-run sandbox_confine, readonly_home (5x), command_env, sandbox_quoting, process_bounds_and_services and the wider related set on Node 22 AND 24, and report counts of leaked bwrap processes before/after (use `pgrep -x bwrap` and parent pid, never `pkill -f`/`pgrep -f` for decisions); `npm --prefix cli run build`. (4) Update your CHANGELOG proposal and any user-visible text: no `--new-session`, so `/dev/tty` works as before. Report the new head SHA and totals. Same rules (local only, no push/PR, claims, throwaway HOME, chain with &&). Also note for yourself: orphan processes from your earlier runs were my cleanup job this time; please clean up any you create by exact pid."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
