{"parentUuid":"9cc7754e-aeef-4a76-b9ee-3d2fc1555f15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5V5dxCc5Dpy3yx1hmEs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification found a real regression in Slice 2 that its own report missed, and I've sent the fix back to the agent.\n\n- **The finding:** `--new-session` puts the sandbox in its own session, so the runner's process-group kill no longer reaches a cancelled command. On Slice 2's head the read-only sandbox test (`readonly_home`) hangs on Node 22 in 2 of 3 runs and leaks processes. On Slice 1's branch it passes 5 of 5 with no leaks. In a scratch copy with only that flag removed it passes 5 of 5 again, with zero leaks. I found 17 orphaned test sandboxes, some 2.7 hours old, and killed them by exact pid.\n- **My decision, per your authorization:** drop `--new-session` from both bwrap branches. Keep `--die-with-parent`, which I verified separately works with a throwaway parent, and the PID namespace. This kernel has TIOCSTI disabled (`legacy_tiocsti=0`), and the agent's own probe showed it failing with or without the flag, so nothing verified is lost, and `/dev/tty` keeps working.\n- **Needed from the agent:** regression tests for write-mode cancellation with no surviving process, a repeat loop proving it isn't intermittent, and results on both Node versions.\n\nTwo mistakes of mine, corrected: my first experiment used `pkill -f` and `pgrep -f`, which match their own command text, and I redid it with exact pids. I also nearly read a misleading result as \"die-with-parent is broken\", which the clean rerun disproved.\n\nStill not validated, so no PRs yet:\n- **Slice 2:** the fix is in progress.\n- **Slice 5:** its Docker credential-overlay follow-up (`aa71a39e`) is committed, and I still need to verify it with my real-container probe.\n- **Slice 3:** its docs must drop the `--new-session` and `/dev/tty` text, and be reconciled to Slice 5."}],"container":null,