{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:41:32.010Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>btlmxy6qj</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01SucwZKHf5E2seAxc8v5M3g</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/btlmxy6qj.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Background command \"git worktree add --detach /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2-base 954c601a &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1; B=/home/mike/nexus-wt/hard2-base; ln -s /home/mike/nexus-wt/pc2/cli/node_modules $B/cli/node_modules; cd $B/cli &amp;&amp; export PATH=/home/mike/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin:$PATH; HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 900 node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_dataset.test.ts test/eval_hardened.test.ts test/eval_harness.test.ts test/eval_integrity.test.ts test/eval_t3.test.ts test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts 2&gt;&amp;1 | grep -aE '^ℹ (tests|pass|fail)' | tr '\\n' ' '; cd /home/mike/nexus-code &amp;&amp; git worktree remove --force $B; echo; pgrep -x bwrap | wc -l\" completed (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>","reason":"delivered_to_agent"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:41:50.572Z","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a98715b8bf34d44a7</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/tasks/a98715b8bf34d44a7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Hardening slice 2: confine write-mode sandbox\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>`--new-session` is removed from both bwrap branches. The new head is `7fe32b4d` on `v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine`, local only, on top of `cf3aff57` and `a0a49daa`. `--die-with-parent`, `--unshare-pid` and the fresh `/proc` stay.\n\n- **Code:** `cli/src/sandbox.ts` now carries a comment explaining why `--new-session` is not used. It puts bwrap in its own session, so the runner's `killpg` on cancel or deadline no longer reaches the sandbox. TIOCSTI is already closed by the kernel default (`dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti=0` since 6.2). `/dev/tty` works as before.\n- **Tests that assert the flag:** `sandbox_confine.test.ts` now asserts `--die-with-parent` and `--unshare-pid` are present and `--new-session` is absent.\n- **New regression test:** `cli/test/sandbox_cancel.test.ts`. It uses the real `RustCoreBridge`, and a write-mode `--sandbox` bridge for the first test. Each test runs 5 rounds of cancel and 5 rounds of deadline, with a backgrounded `sleep` in write mode. Survivors are bwrap pids that exist after the run and did not before.\n- **Test results:** `readonly_home` ran 5 times on each of Node 22.22.2 and 24.21.0, 5/5 on all ten runs, with no bwrap leaked afterwards. `sandbox_cancel` passes on the fixed code (7.7 s for write mode, 12 s for read-only).\n- **Fail-before:** with `--new-session` put back, the read-only cancel test hangs to the 170 s watchdog and leaves one bwrap, which I killed by pid. The write-mode test passed in that variant (7.9 s), so it does not catch the flag; the read-only test is the discriminating one.\n- **Wider run:** 49 related files, including `sandbox_confine`, `sandbox_quoting`, `command_env`, `process_bounds_and_services` and the new test, give 715 pass, 21 fail, 9 skipped on both Node versions.\n- **The 21 failures** are all in six eval files: `eval_dataset` (1), `eval_hardened` (4), `eval_harness` (6), `eval_integrity` (7), `eval_t3` (2) and `eval_version_probe_storage` (1). On the S1 base (`954c601a`) those same six files fail the same 21: 55 pass and 21 fail of 76 on Node 22, and the same split on Node 24. They need the CI capped-workspace fixture and similar, so they are not a regression.\n- **Earlier numbers:** my previous \"Node 22: 200 of 200\" report counted differently; I did not resolve why those eval files passed in that run, and I did not re-run them to find out.\n- **Build:** `npm --prefix cli run build` is clean on both Node versions.\n- **Leaks:** `pgrep -x bwrap` counts 0 before and 0 after the wider run. Two orphaned bwrap processes from my earlier hung `readonly_home` runs had been left behind. I killed them by exact pid (they ignored SIGTERM, so `kill -9`) and confirmed none were left. I stopped the throwaway base worktree and removed it by path.\n\n**Proposed CHANGELOG entry, updated:**\n\n&gt; **Security: `--sandbox` now actually confines.** Write-mode sandboxed commands run with `$HOME` masked, so `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `~/.gnupg` and `~/.config/nexus` are unreadable. This holds even when the workspace is, contains, or sits above `$HOME`. Only toolchain directories (`~/.cargo`, `~/.rustup`, `~/.nvm`, `~/.local/bin`, `~/.npm`, `~/.cache/pip`, `~/go/pkg`, `PATH` entries under HOME) are mounted read-only; extend them with `NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY`. **The network is off by default**; opt in with `--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` (not implied by `--yes`). Sandboxed commands die with the runner and cannot see host processes. `nexus doctor` lists the effective mounts and overlays.\n\nThere is no `--new-session` entry now, and the earlier note about `/dev/tty` is dropped. Claims for the slice, `sandbox.ts` and `SUITE` are released.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>227838</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>124</tool_uses><duration_ms>12626719</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
