{"parentUuid":"f9e14287-a731-4858-a9a9-2bc51b2af7c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5XPGkEPhsbrZp8U8YJP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tz7af1xdB2btfyeBLZnJC3","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a189534fbd1917a64","summary":"Slice 3: re-stack on S5, drop new-session, reconcile Docker","message":"Slice 3 review: the first pass (4a4f67c0) reads honestly. The code underneath has since changed, so please update the docs to the FINAL code. (1) Re-stack: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard3 && git rebase --onto 077abf83 cf3aff57 v1/hardening-s3-docs` (077abf83 is the final Slice 5 head on `v1/hardening-s5-docker`, which sits on the final Slice 2 head 7fe32b4d); resolve any conflicts; re-take the doc claims (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/USER_MANUAL.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md) under nexus-claims as before and release when done. (2) `--new-session` was REMOVED from both bwrap branches in 7fe32b4d (it puts the sandbox in its own session so the runner's killpg on cancel/deadline no longer reached it: measured hang + leaked sandboxes; TIOCSTI is already closed by kernel default `legacy_tiocsti=0`, >=6.2). Remove every statement that the sandbox runs in a new session / has no controlling terminal / that /dev/tty fails; the process-isolation line is now `--unshare-pid` + fresh `/proc` + `--die-with-parent`. (3) Replace the provisional Docker text with what the code at 077abf83 actually does: digest-pinned image `alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea4...` in one constant `DOCKER_SANDBOX_IMAGE`, operator override `NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE` (operator environment or config.env; must be `name@sha256:<64 hex>` or no container starts), `--user <uid>:<gid>`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default with the same opt-in (`--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1`; `network:false` always off), `--pids-limit 512`, `--read-only` with `--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,size=256m`, the scrubbed environment passed per variable with `--env` (HOME/PATH/TMPDIR replaced with container paths), and workspace credential overlays (`sandboxWorkspaceOverlays`: tmpfs for credential directories, /dev/null for files) when the workspace is, contains, or is above $HOME. Remove the \"reconcile with Slice 5\" markers. (4) Update the CHANGELOG entries to these finals: S2: \"Security: `--sandbox` now actually confines. Write-mode sandboxed commands run with `$HOME` masked, so `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `~/.gnupg` and `~/.config/nexus` are unreadable, even when the workspace is, contains, or sits above `$HOME`. Only toolchain directories (`~/.cargo`, `~/.rustup`, `~/.nvm`, `~/.local/bin`, `~/.npm`, `~/.cache/pip`, `~/go/pkg`, `PATH` entries under HOME) are mounted read-only; extend them with `NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY`. The network is off by default; opt in with `--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` (not implied by `--yes`). Sandboxed commands die with the runner and cannot see host processes. `nexus doctor` lists the effective mounts and overlays.\" S5: \"Security: the `--sandbox docker` engine runs a digest-pinned image (alpine 3.23) as the invoking uid with all capabilities dropped, `no-new-privileges`, a read-only root plus a tmpfs `/tmp`, a 512-process limit, and no network unless `--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` is set. Only the scrubbed command environment reaches the container, and credential locations under a workspace that is or contains `$HOME` are masked. `NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE` (operator setting) may substitute another image but it must be digest-pinned, otherwise no container is started. Commands that wrote outside the workspace and `/tmp`, relied on root, or used the network now fail in Docker mode.\" Keep the S1, S4, S6, S7 entries. Verify every changed statement against the code at the new base (cite file:line in your report), run `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs`, commit locally (no push/PR), and report the new head SHA.","type":"message","recipient":"a189534fbd1917a64","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Slice 3 review: the first pass (4a4f67c0) reads h…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":882852,"output_tokens":2187,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":490},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2187,"cache_read_input_tokens":882852,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":8710,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Tz7af1xdB2btfyeBLZnJC3":{"to":"a189534fbd1917a64","summary":"Slice 3: re-stack on S5, drop new-session, reconcile Docker","message":"Slice 3 review: the first pass (4a4f67c0) reads honestly. The code underneath has since changed, so please update the docs to the FINAL code. (1) Re-stack: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/hard3 && git rebase --onto 077abf83 cf3aff57 v1/hardening-s3-docs` (077abf83 is the final Slice 5 head on `v1/hardening-s5-docker`, which sits on the final Slice 2 head 7fe32b4d); resolve any conflicts; re-take the doc claims (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/USER_MANUAL.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md) under nexus-claims as before and release when done. (2) `--new-session` was REMOVED from both bwrap branches in 7fe32b4d (it puts the sandbox in its own session so the runner's killpg on cancel/deadline no longer reached it: measured hang + leaked sandboxes; TIOCSTI is already closed by kernel default `legacy_tiocsti=0`, >=6.2). Remove every statement that the sandbox runs in a new session / has no controlling terminal / that /dev/tty fails; the process-isolation line is now `--unshare-pid` + fresh `/proc` + `--die-with-parent`. (3) Replace the provisional Docker text with what the code at 077abf83 actually does: digest-pinned image `alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea4...` in one constant `DOCKER_SANDBOX_IMAGE`, operator override `NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE` (operator environment or config.env; must be `name@sha256:<64 hex>` or no container starts), `--user <uid>:<gid>`, `--cap-drop ALL`, `--security-opt no-new-privileges`, `--network none` by default with the same opt-in (`--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1`; `network:false` always off), `--pids-limit 512`, `--read-only` with `--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,size=256m`, the scrubbed environment passed per variable with `--env` (HOME/PATH/TMPDIR replaced with container paths), and workspace credential overlays (`sandboxWorkspaceOverlays`: tmpfs for credential directories, /dev/null for files) when the workspace is, contains, or is above $HOME. Remove the \"reconcile with Slice 5\" markers. (4) Update the CHANGELOG entries to these finals: S2: \"Security: `--sandbox` now actually confines. Write-mode sandboxed commands run with `$HOME` masked, so `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `~/.gnupg` and `~/.config/nexus` are unreadable, even when the workspace is, contains, or sits above `$HOME`. Only toolchain directories (`~/.cargo`, `~/.rustup`, `~/.nvm`, `~/.local/bin`, `~/.npm`, `~/.cache/pip`, `~/go/pkg`, `PATH` entries under HOME) are mounted read-only; extend them with `NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY`. The network is off by default; opt in with `--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` (not implied by `--yes`). Sandboxed commands die with the runner and cannot see host processes. `nexus doctor` lists the effective mounts and overlays.\" S5: \"Security: the `--sandbox docker` engine runs a digest-pinned image (alpine 3.23) as the invoking uid with all capabilitie