not verify that kernel default against any code. Item 7 now says `--die-with-parent` and a PID namespace.\n- **Docker text rewritten**, with the \"reconcile with Slice 5\" markers gone. It now covers these points:\n  - **Image:** the image is the constant `DOCKER_SANDBOX_IMAGE` (line 57), which is `alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea4...`.\n  - **Override:** `NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE` (line 58) must match `name@sha256:&lt;64 hex&gt;` (line 59), otherwise no container starts (lines 64-66 and 583-591).\n  - **Run flags:** `--user uid:gid` (line 601), `--cap-drop ALL` (602), `--security-opt no-new-privileges` (603) and `--network none` unless opted in (604). `--pids-limit` is 512 (605 and line 60), and the root is `--read-only` with `--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,size=256m` (607).\n  - **Environment:** the scrubbed environment goes in with one `--env` per variable, and `HOME`, `PATH` and `TMPDIR` are replaced with container paths (610-612).\n  - **Workspace overlays:** credential paths in a workspace that is, contains or is above `$HOME` are overlaid via `sandboxWorkspaceOverlays` (618-620).\n- **Docker network opt-in.** The Docker branch uses the same `options.network !== false &amp;&amp; (options.network === true || sandboxNetworkEnabled())` switch as bwrap, so `--sandbox-network` or `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` applies and `network:false` is always off.\n- **README:** its sandbox bullet now says Docker runs a digest-pinned image as your uid with capabilities dropped and no network by default, and that commands are killed with the runner.\n- **CHANGELOG:** the Slice 2 entry now uses your final wording, plus one sentence that files outside `$HOME` stay readable inside the sandbox. I rewrote the Slice 5 entry as the \"`--sandbox docker` engine runs a digest-pinned image...\" text you gave, and kept the Slice 1, 4, 6 and 7 entries.\n- **USER_MANUAL:** it carries the same `--new-session` removal and Docker rewrite.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- I did not re-read the Slice 4, 6 and 7 code, since they are unchanged from my first pass.\n- I did not run the sandbox or any probe.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>125896</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>4</tool_uses><duration_ms>44241</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
