{"parentUuid":"628e8a40-a228-42b5-a0c5-63b18c505a31","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"044f9db8-b393-47df-8818-3d8d0407f89a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BSTgCMZJBaQVXch9mB9ZDa","type":"tool_result","content":"S7 -> #553\nS2 -> #554\nS6 body now references: Slice 7 (#553)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2ccd27c6-ef79-4490-89b7-1add1a7f28f2","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:48:36.760Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"S7 -> #553\nS2 -> #554\nS6 body now references: Slice 7 (#553)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"628e8a40-a228-42b5-a0c5-63b18c505a31","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"655fb1c7768b543b29f4740524f77eba0a9cb4742b89dc6567e5b591f77d69d8","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PRs #550, #551 and #552 are open, and I'm now working on the dependent Slice 7 and Slice 2 while fixing a placeholder in #552's body.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BSTgCMZJBaQVXch9mB9ZDa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && FOOT='🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)'; mk() { gh pr create --base main --head \"$1\" --title \"$2\" --body \"$3\" >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr list --head \"$1\" --json number -q '.[0].number'; }\nB7=\"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\n\\`allowExternalSymlinks\\` was parsed in \\`security.ts\\` and set to false but never read. No doc promises it (README, manual and CHANGELOG do not mention it; the manual's symlink-confinement text refers to the Rust core), so it is removed from the policy type and both parser sites. A workspace-sourced policy can still only tighten rules, never loosen them; a test pins that (it feeds \\`allowExternalSymlinks: true\\` and \\`allowedPaths: [\\\".git\\\"]\\`, which have no effect).\n\n**Depends on #552** (slice 6; this branch carries its commit, so this PR's CI tests the combination). Merge after #552.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test: the policy no longer has an \\`allowExternalSymlinks\\` key (fails before, passes after). \\`security.test.ts\\` + \\`security_gates.test.ts\\`: 24 of 24 on Node 22 and 24 with the Rust core built. \\`npm --prefix cli run build\\` clean.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable beyond slice 6's notes (removal of dead code).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\n\\`.nexus-security.json\\` files that set the key still load; the key is ignored. Changelog entry is in the docs PR.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Covered by the docs PR (hardening 3/7).\n\n$FOOT\"\nP7=$(mk v1/hardening-s7-external-symlinks \"fix(security): remove the unread allowExternalSymlinks policy key (hardening 7/7)\" \"$B7\"); echo \"S7 -> #$P7\"\nB2=\"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nWrite-mode \\`--sandbox\\` used \\`--ro-bind / /\\`, so the whole host including \\`~/.ssh\\`, \\`~/.config/nexus\\`, \\`~/.aws\\` and \\`~/.gnupg\\` was readable, the network was open, and the claimed \\`--die-with-parent\\` was absent. **Reproduced on the base** (sentinel readable, network unshare absent, background child outlived the killed bwrap).\n\n**Depends on #550** (slice 1; this branch carries its commit, so CI tests the combination). Merge after #550.\n\n- \\`\\$HOME\\` is an empty tmpfs; only toolchain directories (\\`~/.cargo\\`, \\`~/.rustup\\`, \\`~/.nvm\\`, \\`~/.local/bin\\`, \\`~/.npm\\`, \\`~/.cache/pip\\`, \\`~/go/pkg\\`, \\`PATH\\` entries under HOME, plus the operator list \\`NEXUS_SANDBOX_HOME_READONLY\\`) are bound back read-only. Credential locations are refused as binds, also through symlinks; cargo credential files are masked; \\`/run/user/<uid>\\` and the Docker socket are hidden.\n- **Found in review, fixed here:** when the workspace is \\`\\$HOME\\`, contains it, or is above it, the writable workspace bind re-exposed \\`~/.ssh\\` (reproduced with a sentinel: workspace=\\$HOME leaked, workspace=\\$HOME/proj did not). \\`sandboxWorkspaceOverlays\\` now overlays credential paths inside the workspace (tmpfs for directories, \\`/dev/null\\` for files).\n- Network off by default (\\`--unshare-net\\`); opt in with \\`--sandbox-network\\` or \\`NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1\\` (operator-only; \\`--yes\\` does not imply it; read-only mode always offline). In review mode the approval prompt says whether a command will have network or looks like it needs it.\n- \\`--die-with-parent\\` on both bwrap branches. **\\`--new-session\\` is deliberately NOT used**: it makes the sandbox its own session, so the runner's \\`killpg\\` on cancel/deadline no longer reaches it. Measured: with it, \\`readonly_home\\` hung in 2 of 3 runs and leaked sandboxes (15+ orphans, some 2.7 h old); without it 5 of 5 pass with zero leaks. TIOCSTI is already closed by this kernel's default (\\`legacy_tiocsti=0\\`, Linux 6.2+).\n- \\`--unshare-pid\\` plus a fresh \\`/proc\\` were already present: a sandboxed command cannot read its parents' \\`/proc/<pid>/environ\\`. (Unsandboxed commands still can; see the docs PR.)\n- \\`nexus doctor\\` lists the effective mounts and overlays. The \\`--sandbox-network\\` flag lives in an import-free module (\\`sandbox_network.ts\\`) because a first version created a config/sandbox/command_env import cycle that hung Node 24.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`sandbox_confine.test.ts\\` (13) and \\`sandbox_cancel.test.ts\\` (new, real \\`RustCoreBridge\\`, 5 cancel and 5 deadline rounds in write and read-only mode): 15 of 15 with \\`sandbox_confine\\` on Node 22 and 24; \\`readonly_home\\` 5 runs each on both versions, all pass, **bwrap count 0 before and after**; independent probe of all three workspace layouts: sentinels hidden, ordinary file readable. Type-check clean. 21 \\`eval_*\\` tests fail on Node 24 on this host with a capped-workspace fixture that CI provides; they fail identically on slice 1's branch, so CI is the arbiter.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ (goose, opencode prefixes) returned only unrelated hits for bwrap; nothing borrowed. Followed the repo's own read-only bwrap branch; rejected binding all of HOME read-only. Network reachability with the opt-in could not be shown (no route on the host); the opt-in is tested through the absence of \\`--unshare-net\\`.\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\n**Behaviour changes:** \\`--sandbox\\` commands lose the network by default; \\`\\$HOME\\` inside the sandbox is an empty tmpfs (writes there are lost; \\`~/.gitconfig\\`, \\`~/.npmrc\\`, \\`~/.ssh\\` invisible, so commits inside the sandbox lack the operator's identity). Files outside \\`\\$HOME\\` remain readable (\\`--ro-bind / /\\`); the docs PR says so. Changelog entry is in the docs PR.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Covered by the docs PR (hardening 3/7).\n\n$FOOT\"\nP2=$(mk v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine \"fix(security): write-mode --sandbox masks HOME and cuts the network by default (hardening 2/7)\" \"$B2\"); echo \"S2 -> #$P2\"\nread -r P1 P4 P6 < /tmp/claude-1000/pr_nums_a.txt; gh pr view $P6 --json body -q .body | sed \"s/#PLACEHOLDER7/#$P7/\" > /tmp/claude-1000/b6new.md && gh pr edit $P6 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/b6new.md >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"S6 body now references: $(gh pr view $P6 --json body -q .body | grep -o 'Slice 7 (#[0-9]*)')\"; echo \"$P2 $P7\" > /tmp/claude-1000/pr_nums_b.txt","description":"Open slices 7 and 2 and fix the placeholder reference in the slice 6 PR body"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","id":"aef924c4-28c3-4cc7-807c-e8208b949215","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:48:37.201Z","version":"2.1.323","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"02245c82d4cb86350db44b7c9960d5f359fa3c3746ce766c103fc6f328b1a703","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"bda0d973-cbad-4ee1-9c99-4e9452d8384f","keep":1484,"tail":["655fb1c7768b543b29f4740524f77eba0a9cb4742b89dc6567e5b591f77d69d8","03f15b4699ebfe813bd7f116fff94e5094b7395d435226d4cc9b87eeda545796","3bad71dc3ffc775ae082591b64158248819f867b7d394ad69feea31c98514778"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1486,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"98e7ec4efe06eba6dc3d90a6cc676286b92f6552525d8200ff9b3398653d1c88"}
