{"parentUuid":"bdee01e6-8ad7-4cf2-9630-70e6879a7be9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5XeYxxSZkTx1Sg6sPsV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#553 (Slice 7) and #554 (Slice 2) are open, and #552's body now points at #553. The last two are Slice 5 (on #554) and the docs slice (on Slice 5)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3115,"cache_read_input_tokens":899353,"output_tokens":2325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3115,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2325,"cache_read_input_tokens":899353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3115},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch5XeYf7bPAd3HV2kYn8v","requestRef":"aef924c4-28c3-4cc7-807c-e8208b949215","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"57c9cf00-975e-4452-bd38-aa1351627a0f","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:48:38.839Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"57c9cf00-975e-4452-bd38-aa1351627a0f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5XeYxxSZkTx1Sg6sPsV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cxs6JrQdNCBdvgi35zF5te","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"FOOT='🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)'; mk() { gh pr create --base main --head \"$1\" --title \"$2\" --body \"$3\" >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr list --head \"$1\" --json number -q '.[0].number'; }\nB5=\"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nThe Docker sandbox ran the floating tag \\`alpine:latest\\` with no privilege or network restrictions and a workspace bind that, like bwrap before slice 2, re-exposed credentials when the workspace was \\`\\$HOME\\` or above it.\n\n**Depends on #554** (slice 2; this branch carries its commits, so CI tests the combination). Merge after #554.\n\n- Image: \\`alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea410b9215eaee7976ba6c0639039b444be8e5d638f7abbada189971eb2\\` in one constant (\\`DOCKER_SANDBOX_IMAGE\\`); operator override \\`NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE\\` must be \\`name@sha256:<64 hex>\\` or no container starts (fail closed). I verified the digest against the registry (\\`docker buildx imagetools inspect alpine:3.23\\`) and the locally pulled image.\n- \\`--user <uid>:<gid>\\`, \\`--cap-drop ALL\\`, \\`--security-opt no-new-privileges\\`, \\`--network none\\` unless the slice-2 opt-in is set, \\`--pids-limit 512\\`, \\`--read-only\\` with \\`--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,size=256m\\`; the scrubbed environment from slice 1 is passed per variable with \\`--env\\` (HOME, PATH, TMPDIR replaced with container paths). Dead \\`mountMode\\` code removed; the probe uses the same hardened flags (timeout raised so a first pull does not fail it silently).\n- **Found in review, fixed here:** the same credential re-exposure as bwrap when the workspace is, contains or is above \\`\\$HOME\\` (reproduced with a real container and a sentinel: HOME and PARENT layouts leaked); now overlaid with \\`sandboxWorkspaceOverlays\\` (tmpfs for directories, \\`/dev/null\\` for files), mount order verified in real containers.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`sandbox_docker.test.ts\\`: 12 of 12 on Node 22 and 24 with real containers on the pinned image (a write to \\`/\\` fails, \\`CapEff\\` is zero, uid matches, the sentinel env var is absent from \\`env\\` and \\`/proc/self/environ\\`, network unreachable by default, credential overlays hold in all three layouts). Before the change 5 of 7 original tests failed. With the sandbox, cancellation, environment and quoting files: 33 of 33 on both versions, no leaked bwrap or containers. Independent real-container probe: no leak in any layout. Linux/amd64 only; rootless Docker and images that expect root are untested; 512 pids is a guess, not tuned.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ corpora returned nothing relevant to \\`docker run\\` hardening; the checklist (cap-drop ALL, no-new-privileges, read-only root plus tmpfs, non-root user, network none, pids limit, digest pin) is from memory of OpenHands/Codex practice. Rejected custom seccomp/AppArmor profiles (Docker's default kept) and memory/CPU limits (no operator setting yet).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nCommands that wrote outside the workspace and \\`/tmp\\`, relied on root, or used the network now fail in Docker mode. Changelog entry is in the docs PR.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Covered by the docs PR (hardening 3/7).\n\n$FOOT\"\nP5=$(mk v1/hardening-s5-docker \"fix(security): harden the Docker sandbox (hardening 5/7)\" \"$B5\"); echo \"S5 -> #$P5\"\nB3=\"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nDocs only. Makes \\`ARCHITECTURE.md\\` §3 (items 3, 6, 7), the manual, the README bullets and the CHANGELOG match what the hardening slices actually do, and states the limits plainly: egress approval covers network tools, not shell commands (the shell is confined only by the sandbox's network setting); write-mode \\`--sandbox\\` masks \\`\\$HOME\\` and the listed locations but files outside \\`\\$HOME\\` stay readable; **without \\`--sandbox\\` a command runs as the same user** and can still read the operator's files and its parents' \\`/proc/<pid>/environ\\` (the scrubbed environment only removes what it inherits); the network opt-in is unprotected. Records why \\`--new-session\\` is not used. Documents the slice 4, 6 and 7 behaviour changes and adds an \\`[Unreleased]\\` changelog section.\n\n**Depends on #554 and #$P5 (slices 2 and 5; this branch carries their commits) and describes #550, #551, #552, #553.** Merge last.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` and \\`node scripts/check_requirements.mjs\\` pass. I spot-checked the cited code: the Docker constants and flags each exist once in \\`sandbox.ts\\`, \\`--new-session\\` appears in the docs only in the sentence explaining why it is not used.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (documentation only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable (documentation only).\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation of slices 1 to 7.\n\n$FOOT\"\nP3=$(mk v1/hardening-s3-docs \"docs: sandbox and command-environment behaviour match the code (hardening 3/7)\" \"$B3\"); echo \"S3 -> #$P3\"; echo \"$P5 $P3\" > /tmp/claude-1000/pr_nums_c.txt; gh pr list --state open --search \"hardening\" --json number,title,headRefName -q '.[]|\"#\\(.number) \\(.headRefName)\"' | sort","description":"Open the Docker and docs PRs and list all seven hardening PRs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3115,"cache_read_input_tokens":899353,"output_tokens":2325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3115,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2325,"cache_read_input_tokens":899353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3115},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13162,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Cxs6JrQdNCBdvgi35zF5te":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && FOOT='🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)'; mk() { gh pr create --base main --head \"$1\" --title \"$2\" --body \"$3\" >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr list --head \"$1\" --json number -q '.[0].number'; }\nB5=\"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nThe Docker sandbox ran the floating tag \\`alpine:latest\\` with no privilege or network restrictions and a workspace bind that, like bwrap before slice 2, re-exposed credentials when the workspace was \\`\\$HOME\\` or above it.\n\n**Depends on #554** (slice 2; this branch carries its commits, so CI tests the combination). Merge after #554.\n\n- Image: \\`alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea410b9215eaee7976ba6c0639039b444be8e5d638f7abbada189971eb2\\` in one constant (\\`DOCKER_SANDBOX_IMAGE\\`); operator override \\`NEXUS_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE\\` must be \\`name@sha256:<64 hex>\\` or no container starts (fail closed). I verified the digest against the registry (\\`docker buildx imagetools inspect alpine:3.23\\`) and the locally pulled image.\n- \\`--user <uid>:<gid>\\`, \\`--cap-drop ALL\\`, \\`--security-opt no-new-privileges\\`, \\`--network none\\` unless the slice-2 opt-in is set, \\`--pids-limit 512\\`, \\`--read-only\\` with \\`--tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,size=256m\\`; the scrubbed environment from slice 1 is passed per variable with \\`--env\\` (HOME, PATH, TMPDIR replaced with container paths). Dead \\`mountMode\\` code removed; the probe uses the same hardened flags (timeout raised so a first pull does not fail it silently).\n- **Found in review, fixed here:** the same credential re-exposure as bwrap when the workspace is, contains or is above \\`\\$HOME\\` (reproduced with a real container and a sentinel: HOME and PARENT layouts leaked); now overlaid with \\`sandboxWorkspaceOverlays\\` (tmpfs for directories, \\`/dev/null\\` for files), mount order verified in real containers.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`sandbox_docker.test.ts\\`: 12 of 12 on Node 22 and 24 with real containers on the pinned image (a write to \\`/\\` fails, \\`CapEff\\` is zero, uid matches, the sentinel env var is absent from \\`env\\` and \\`/proc/self/environ\\`, network unreachable by default, credential overlays hold in all three layouts). Before the change 5 of 7 original tests failed. With the sandbox, cancellation, environment and quoting files: 33 of 33 on both versions, no leaked bwrap or containers. Independent real-container probe: no leak in any layout. Linux/amd64 only; rootless Docker and images that expect root are untested; 512 pids is a guess, not tuned.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ corpora returned nothing relevant to \\`docker run\\` hardening; the checklist (cap-drop ALL, no-new-privileges, read-only root plus tmpfs, non-root user, network none, pids limit, digest pin) is from memory of OpenHands/Codex practice. Rejected custom seccomp/AppArmor profiles (Docker's default kept) and memory/CPU limits (no operator setting yet).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nCommands that wrote outside the workspace and \\`/tmp\\`, relied on root, or used the network now fail in Docker mode. Changelog entry is in the docs PR.\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Covered by the docs PR (hardening 3/7).\n\n$FOOT\"\nP5=$(mk v1/hardening-s5-docker \"fix(security): harden the Docker sandbox (hardening 5/7)\" \"$B5\"); echo \"S5 -> #$P5\"\nB3=\"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nDocs only. Makes \\`ARCHITECTURE.md\\` §3 (items 3, 6, 7), the manual, the README bullets and the CHANGELOG match what the hardening slices actually do, and states the limits plainly: egress approval covers network tools, not shell commands (the shell is confined only by the sandbox's network setting); write-mode \\`--sandbox\\` masks \\`\\$HOME\\` and the listed locations but files outside \\`\\$HOME\\` stay readable; **without \\`--sandbox\\` a command runs as the same user** and can still read the operator's files and its parents' \\`/proc/<pid>/environ\\` (the scrubbed environment only removes what it inherits); the network opt-in is unprotected. Records why \\`--new-session\\` is not used. Documents the slice 4, 6 and 7 behaviour changes and adds an \\`[Unreleased]\\` changelog section.\n\n**Depends on #554 and #$P5 (slices 2 and 5; this branch carries their commits) and describes #550, #551, #552, #553.** Merge last.\n\n## Validation\n\n\\`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs\\` and \\`node scripts/check_requirements.mjs\\` pass. I spot-checked the cited code: the Docker constants and flags each exist once in \\`sandbox.ts\\`, \\`--new-session\\` appears in the docs only in the sentence explaining why it is not used.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nNot applicable (documentation only).\n\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\n\nNot applicable (documentation only).\n\n## Documentation and coordination\n\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation of slices 1 to 7.\n\n$FOOT\"\nP3=$(mk v1/hardening-s3-docs \"docs: sandbox and command-environment behaviour match the code (hardening 3/7)\" \"$B3\"); echo \"S3 -> #$P3\"; echo \"$P5 $P3\" > /tmp/claude-1000/pr_nums_c.txt; gh pr list --state open --search \"hardening\" --json number,title,headRefName -q '.[]|\"#\\(.number) \\(.headRefName)\"' | sort","description":"Open the Docker and docs PRs and list all seven hardening PRs"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Cxs6JrQdNCBdvgi35zF5te":{"cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch5XeYf7bPAd3HV2kYn8v","requestRef":"aef9