{"parentUuid":"7a56518d-4401-474c-9687-2578c8548fb1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01B2GMGSWY2yWpVjtUf33j5Y","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0ac006d4-78fd-488b-8179-a2dbc56b05c4","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:49:13.630Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"0ac006d4-78fd-488b-8179-a2dbc56b05c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5Xgqatgps6CbsNmoQtS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All seven hardening slices are validated and open as PRs, on the validated heads and unmerged, with one watch on their CI.\n\n| Slice | PR | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1: scrub the command environment | #550 | none |\n| 2: confine the write-mode sandbox | #554 | #550 |\n| 3: docs match the code | #556 | #554 and #555 |\n| 4: legacy worktree merge guard | #551 | none |\n| 5: Docker sandbox | #555 | #554 |\n| 6: protected paths are workspace-relative | #552 | none |\n| 7: remove `allowExternalSymlinks` | #553 | #552 |\n\n**How I did it**\n- **Base:** every PR targets `main` and carries its dependency's commits, so its CI tests exactly the combination that will exist after the dependency merges. Each body names its dependency.\n- **PR bodies:** they carry the template sections, the reproduction evidence, the XERJ notes, the behaviour changes and the known limits.\n- **Merge order:**\n  - #550, #554, #555, #556 in that order.\n  - #551 independently.\n  - #552 then #553.\n  - I verify each head, its tested merge commit and file overlap first, and I wait for `main` between interacting merges.\n\n**What validation caught, beyond what the agents reported**\n- **Slice 4:** real code execution outside the worktree. Its new tests fail on unfixed `main`, 4 of 4.\n- **Slices 2 and 5:** a credential leak when the workspace is `$HOME` or above it, in both the bwrap and Docker sandboxes. Both are fixed and probe-verified.\n- **Slice 2:** `--new-session` hung tests and leaked sandboxes. I removed it and verified 5 of 5 with zero leaks.\n\n**Known limit, stated in the docs PR:** without `--sandbox`, a command still runs as your user. It can read your files and its parents' `/proc/<pid>/environ`. These PRs remove what a command inherits, not what your own account can read.\n\nCI on seven PRs will be slow, since the runners are shared. The watch reports each PR's required checks as they finish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1503,"cache_read_input_tokens":905026,"output_tokens":720,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1503,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":905026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1503},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch5XgqHHRdHjpVLVTwR3i","requestRef":"023d9f0e-7a1c-473e-8301-82997327170d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d2f42939-a033-4496-8eb6-fb9aed0e1a93","timestamp":"2026-11-15T22:49:13.619Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
