{"parentUuid":"66713ee2-f9f2-4864-afca-57f32975d397","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5aGdfEZ2TdUMVeLr7j7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI on the pull requests already found two real problems in the Slice 2 chain, and I fixed both:\n- **Leak-guard ratchet:** `sandbox_cancel.test.ts` builds a real bridge without importing the leak guard from #519, so the ratchet failed the Slice 2 chain (#554, #555, #556). I added the import and confirmed with the ratchet test that the test releases everything it starts.\n- **CodeQL, `js/incomplete-sanitization` (high):** `sandbox_confine.test.ts:69` built a regex from an escaped version string. I replaced it with a plain substring check, so the pattern is gone.\n\nI verified both fixes on Node 22 and 24 (21 of 21 across the cancel, confine and ratchet tests, no leaked `bwrap`). They went in as a normal commit on #554, merged into #555 and #556 without rewriting any history.\n\nThe other four PRs (#550, #551, #552, #553) show no failures so far. CI is re-running on the three updated heads, and one watch covers all seven. I'll verify each head, its tested merge commit and file overlap before merging, and wait for `main` between interacting merges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":918641,"output_tokens":385,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":918641,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transfo