{"parentUuid":"4ae56649-800d-4096-97b2-dc41f0870fd0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5axQoRodkoAVjcvwEL5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four of the seven hardening slices are merged, each at its exact head after verification:\n\n| Slice | PR | Merge commit |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4: worktree merge guard | #551 | `b42ae2d6` |\n| 1: environment scrub | #550 | `2639213d` |\n| 6: workspace-relative protected paths | #552 | `21487c97` |\n| 7: remove `allowExternalSymlinks` | #553 | `57d10ccb` |\n\nFor #553 my automatic overlap rule would have wrongly flagged it, because #552's own commit is in both. So I checked by hand that its real delta is two files that nothing else on `main` touched.\n\n**Still open:** the sandbox chain is on its corrected heads, with CI re-running.\n- **#554 (Slice 2):** merges first.\n- **#555 (Slice 5, Docker):** after #554.\n- **#556 (the docs):** last.\n\n**`main` health:** I haven't confirmed it after these four merges. Its CI run on the final commit `57d10ccb` is still in progress. I cancelled the two oldest intermediate runs to free the runners and logged it, since the final run covers all four merges. One watch covers #554–#556 and that run. When #554 passes at its exact head, I merge it, then #555 and #556 in order, and report when `main` is confirmed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1687,"cache_read_input_tokens":927623,"output_tokens":445,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1687,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":927623,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemer