{"parentUuid":"d89f6b62-bb4b-45ff-b6f3-6dc46b5686b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5dfVnCi9LRBDgwBvtrH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Six of the seven hardening slices are on `main`, with one watch covering the last PR and the `main` run:\n\n| Slice | PR | Merge commit |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4 | #551 | `b42ae2d6` |\n| 1 | #550 | `2639213d` |\n| 6 | #552 | `21487c97` |\n| 7 | #553 | `57d10ccb` |\n| 2 | #554 | `b9a89f2b` |\n| 5 | #555 | `bbde9319` |\n\nFor #555 I confirmed beforehand that its true remaining change was two files, that nothing else on `main` touches them, and that a trial merge was clean.\n\n**Still open:**\n- **#556 (the docs):** it has one job pending. When that finishes, I merge it, and then every statement in the architecture text and changelog describes code that is actually on `main`.\n- **`main` health:** not confirmed yet. The runs on `21487c97` and the final commit `bbde9319` are still going. As before, the run on the last commit covers all six merges, and I'll read its conclusion before calling `main` healthy.\n\nI cancelled four intermediate `main` runs across this stretch, each logged, to keep the shared runners free. Each is re-runnable if the final run fails and I need to isolate which slice caused it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1614,"cache_read_input_tokens":938417,"output_tokens":427,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1614,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":938417,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1614},"type":"message"}],"sp