{"parentUuid":"0fc2744e-2cce-44b3-b510-625730613de3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0dea262a-4abe-4bbc-93e2-8a304046b63c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, ListAgents, Monitor, Read, ReadMcpResourceTool, ScheduleWakeup, SendMessage, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Workflow, Write, bash, mcp__plugin_claude-mem_mcp-search__work_state_read, mcp__rea__inspect_binary_hardening, mcp__rea__inspect_go_binary, mcp__rea__inspect_rust_binary</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n## What this work is for:\nThis section records facts without weighing them; whoever continues from this summary weighs them, holding back only a step that plainly serves serious, wrongful harm, not work that is merely sensitive, unusual or borderline.\n\n*From the earlier summary (its recorded facts, marked as such; the step it left pending has since been carried out):*\n- The original request, from the user's first message, was \"I need you to fully audit the entire codebase. Ensure all functionality is complete, working, and frontier coding client ready. Once everything is verified and complete, land and release v1.1.4\". (from that summary)\n- The user pasted an external \"Nexus Code v1.1.x readiness audit\", Entire review findings and an evidence-integrity audit; the pasted audit says \"Leave push, merge, tags, publishing and production routing changes to the owner\" and \"Do not silently change release version or claim 1.1.4 qualification\". (from that summary)\n- Repo mikeholownych/nexus-code (local `/home/mike/nexus-code`, stale checkout; owner Mike Holownych): TypeScript CLI `cli/`, Rust core `core/`, eval harness `eval/`. Work touches the repo, GitHub PRs/CI, the owner's installed clients and config, the claims log `.git/nexus-claims.log`, memory files under `/home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/memory/`. (from that summary)\n- Owner constraints (verbatim, from that summary): \"Entire Gate is no longer a valid gate.. for any PR\"; \"we should still be running the review prompts that the Entire agents were running locally.\"; \"You are to ensure that all gates reach desired end state.\"; \"I also told you that you are authorized to do whatever it takes to get to release... So, you have the authority to take over eval\"; \"for live provider.. this environment uses the homelab-ai setup.. there are no individual ollama, vllm, or llama.cpp setups. Everything goes through the custom gateway (10.0.8.5)\"; \"I already mentioned the key is already setup in the nexus config. use that.\"; \"the gateway is not something that is, or should be, controlled by this product. This product should work no matter what it connects to and is presented with.\"; \"going forward, do the research.. how do other client harnesses solve for the same issue. Iplement that as a bare minimum.. improved if at all possible.\"; \"you are the only agent working in the repo.. everything is yours.\" Never delete/re-cut tags; Dependabot PRs exempt; never work around the rm-safety hook. Self-rules: chain commands with `&&`; never `git stash`; Rust builds only with isolated `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`; merge with merge commits (`gh pr merge --merge --match-head-commit <full sha>`); read pass/fail totals; verify CI status+conclusion before claiming; run suites with throwaway HOME; never `pkill -f`/`pgrep -f` for decisions (stop by exact pid). (from that summary)\n- Earlier-summary facts: v1.1.4 stable published; v1.2.0 plan/semantic-integrity workstream landed as PRs #493–#509; the pasted specs' guardrails say not to discard unrelated work, rewrite Git history, weaken tests, fabricate evidence, merge/publish without authorization, or send private repository data to unapproved services; a boundary was stated for REA study (file-level metadata only for proprietary clients; no decompiling or credential files). (from that summary)\n\n*From this conversation:* The work is a release and hardening program for Nexus Code, an open-source coding-agent CLI owned by the user, who describes positioning in AI governance. It touches the owner's repo, GitHub PRs/CI, a shared inference gateway (`https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`) used under a `GATEWAY` claim with the key read from `~/.config/nexus/config.env` into the environment only, a TypeSafe API key the user said \"is in ~/.zshrc\" (one variable read, never printed or written), and the owner's installed clients/memory files. A pasted task (from the user, no words of their own) asked for seven security-hardening slices for run_command/sandbox code (\"A static review of main at 03bf579 found the defects below\"); its ground rules say \"Do not push, tag, merge or publish unless the owner tells you to. Open PRs only when asked\", and the user later said \"open PRs once it has all been validated\". The user also said: \"You are authorized to use the resources available to you to continue on until all work is complete. If a decision is required, evaluate all options and choose the option best suited and in-line with the work we've been doing.\" The pending step is merging the seven hardening PRs as their CI passes.\n\n## State and work done\n\n**v1.2.0 release (done).** rc.1 matrix G1.1-4 failed (lead-reasoning 195/200, deep 200/200; recorded unaltered, `docs/evidence/v1.2.0/G1.1-4-rc.1.md`). Owner chose \"Accept and record\". Promotion commit `f1ad33b9` (version-only on rc.1 `cc82b5ee`) landed on main via merge-commit PR #524 (`e781bf29`) after the release workflow first failed its \"tag must be ancestor of main\" guard (my ordering slip; tag never moved; failed job re-run). Release v1.2.0 published (latest), tag `v1.2.0` = `d6075b8d`, assets/checksums/attestations/install verified; owner approved publishing. Published-archive G1.1-4 measurement (16:56–17:47Z): deep 200/200, lead-reasoning 155/200 (45 plain read_file prompts returned the call as function-call text `read_file(path=\"README.md\")`, 10/10 in a probe), recorded in PR #548 (`docs/evidence/v1.2.0/G1.1-4-v1.2.0.md`); release body updated with both measurements. The Stop hook for goal \"frontier quality release at v1.2.0\" repeatedly said not satisfied; I agreed and never claimed frontier quality. User later set `/goal resume`.\n\n**Merged to main this stretch (each at exact head after checks verified; main CI green on final commit `011bb6b3`):** #511/#512 plans, #513 PC-1, #514 DH-1/2, #515 PR-3, #516 MQ-6, #517 CS-4, #518 MQ-5, #519 PC-2 (incl. Node 22 watchdog fix), #520 CS-3, #521 PR-1, #522, #525 (fix MQ-5×MQ-6 red main), #526 (post-stable docs: LATEST v1.2.0), #541 (AGENTS.md rewrite + CLAUDE.md `@AGENTS.md` + `docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md`; NOTE earlier I wrongly called it #527 — #527 is Dependabot), #543 (steering-judgment research record `docs/research/steering-judgment/`), #544 (plans: VC-10 gated steering judge, PC-7 flaky eval_integrity test, CX-5 wording), #545 WM-2 (Rust edit_file failure feedback), #546 CX-5 (compaction invariant; compaction-03 active), #547 VC-5 (verified re-check on resume), #548 (stable evidence + WM-4/GA-43 plan), #549 WM-4 (function-call-text recognition, recognition only). Merge rule adopted: batch only PRs whose files are disjoint from main changes since their tested base (computed via git); serialize overlapping ones; verify PR head and that passing run belongs to current head (stale monitor events happened). Lessons added to `tasks/lessons.md`. Memory file `owner-authorizes-autonomous-decisions.md` saved/indexed.\n\n**Other research/outputs:** reviewed agent-rules-books, OpenHands docs, Anthropic context-management post and 2026 Agentic Coding Trends Report (read in full via PDF); lessons folded into v1.2.1/v1.3 plans. Steering-conflict evaluation (regex `steeringNegations` vs TypeSafe `jev-1.14.0` and gateway `engineering/deep` judges on 26 synthetic messages): regex caught 3/12 withdrawals; TypeSafe 12/12, 0/66 FP; gateway 11/11, 0/64 (row 26 missing: gateway ECONNREFUSED); only synthetic text sent; plan unit VC-10 is gated (not built).\n\n**Hardening task (7 slices, all validated by me, branches pushed, PRs opened; none merged):**\n| Slice | PR | Branch | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 scrub command env (`cli/src/command_env.ts`, runner.rs second layer, `NEXUS_COMMAND_ENV_PASSTHROUGH`) | #550 | v1/hardening-s1-command-env (954c601a) | none |\n| 2 write-mode sandbox confine (HOME tmpfs, workspace credential overlays, network off by default `--sandbox-network`/`NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK`, `--die-with-parent`, doctor; `--new-session` deliberately NOT used) | #554 | v1/hardening-s2-sandbox-confine (head ae52792c) | #550 |\n| 3 docs (ARCHITECTURE §3, manual, README, CHANGELOG [Unreleased]) | #556 | v1/hardening-s3-docs (17e76911) | #554, #555; describes all |\n| 4 legacy worktree merge guard (reproduced code execution via planted .git; new tests fail 4/4 on unfixed main) | #551 | v1/hardening-s4-worktree-merge (ee0078a7) | none |\n| 5 Docker sandbox hardening (digest-pinned `alpine:3.23@sha256:469c9ea4…` verified vs registry, cap-drop, no-new-privileges, network none, pids 512, read-only+tmpfs, credential overlays) | #555 | v1/hardening-s5-docker (2c6673b6) | #554 |\n| 6 protected paths workspace-relative | #552 | v1/hardening-s6-protected-paths (7de595ed) | none |\n| 7 remove `allowExternalSymlinks` | #553 | v1/hardening-s7-external-symlinks (4a09556f) | #552 |\nAll PRs target main; dependents carry their base's commits. Findings from my independent review: workspace=`$HOME`/ancestor re-exposed `~/.ssh` in both bwrap and Docker (fixed, probe-verified); `--new-session` defeated the runner's killpg (readonly_home hung 2/3, orphan bwrap; removed; 5/5 pass, 0 leaks); scrubbed child can still read parent `/proc/<pid>/environ` and operator files when unsandboxed (documented in #556). CI then found: leak-guard ratchet failure (`sandbox_cancel.test.ts` lacked `./helpers/leak_guard.js`) and CodeQL `js/incomplete-sanitization` at `sandbox_confine.test.ts:69` — both fixed in S2 commit ae52792c and merged (no history rewrite) into S5/S3 branches; CI re-running on heads #554 ae52792c, #555 2c6673b6, #556 17e76911.\n\n**Latest event:** monitor `b2c0hc8dn` reported \"#551 required checks finished: fail=0\" (not yet verified/merged by me). Other monitors/agents are idle; helper worktrees under `/home/mike/nexus-wt/` (hard1–hard7, etc.).\n\n## Open items / next steps\n1. Verify #551's head (`ee0078a7`), that its passing run tested the current merge commit, and file overlap with main since its tested base; then merge with `gh pr merge 551 --merge --match-head-commit <full sha>`.\n2. Merge order: #550 → #554 → #555 → #556 (docs last); #551 independent; #552 → #553. Before each: all required checks (`test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, `linux-x86_64`) pass at exact current head, tested merge commit matches, no overlap with main changes; wait for `main` CI between interacting merges. Re-check CodeQL on all.\n3. The 21 Node-24 `eval_*` failures on this host fail identically on slice 1's base (CI capped-workspace fixture); CI is arbiter.\n4. Remaining v1.2.1 plan work (Phase 1/2 units not yet started: CX-1, WM-1, DH-5, MQ-1/2/3, PR-2, PR-9, PR-11, etc.), VC-10 gated; follow-ups noted: `evaluator.ts:210-236` unguarded `git diff`, routing legacy worktree merge through worktrunk, `@file` import expansion CX-7.\n5. Standing constraints: no frontier-grade claim; failed runs recorded unaltered; tags immutable; never `pkill -f`; throwaway HOME; credentials only via environment, never printed; don't touch the owner's other Docker services; leave Dependabot PRs alone.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"3554142e-6234-437b-9a5c-29cc7cdea9f2","timestamp":"2026-11-15T23:30:22.771Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":97,"turnIndex":583},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
