{"parentUuid":"ca0f90f6-4f55-4ecf-be98-b7bcc2f2f71b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5n4sxWaZeuTN1JiDFHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wave 1 is under way: I've asked Dependabot to rebase #533 (`dotenv` patch) and #530 (`commander` 12→15) onto the current `main`.\n\n- **Why rebase first:** all 14 PRs are 57 commits behind `main`, and their failures are scattered across unrelated jobs. #532 changes one experiments `package.json` yet failed `linux-x86_64`. These runs date from the red-`main` window I fixed in #525, so the failures are most likely stale-base noise. A rebased run is the quickest way to confirm that.\n- **#530 needs more than a green run:** commander 15 requires Node ≥22.12.0 but `cli/package.json` says `>=22`, so a user on Node 22.0–22.11 would hit a broken install. The CLI is plain-`tsc` ESM with no bundler, so ESM-only commander is fine. The only negative option, `--no-resume`, is unaffected. Commander 13 also made excess arguments an error by default, which the tests should show. If CI is green, I'll fix the engines range in our own branch, supersede #530 and note it in the changelog.\n- **Next:** once wave 1 is checked, I rebase the 12 experiments bumps in small groups to keep CI load down. Many of them are the same bump across directories, so I'll check each one's real diff and merge only those that pass at their exact head.\n\nTwo watches are running, one on the two rebased PRs and one 25-minute fallback. Nothing has been merged or closed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":141859,"output_tokens":498,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_