{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"b6ab6db5d50f03a20619ae801bf793bc7b41c7bc08c515b128f55bde016a8438","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XWEekXwZLATd6nYBvWqdLC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr create --base main --head v1/deps-commander-15 --title \"chore(deps): commander 12 → 15, engines node >=22.12.0 (supersedes #530)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSupersedes the Dependabot bump #530, which could not be rebased and would have left `engines.node` at `>=22` while commander 15 requires Node 22.12.0 or newer.\n\n## What changes\n- `commander` 12.1.0 → 15.1.0 (ESM-only; fine here: `cli` is `\"type\": \"module\"`, plain `tsc`, no bundler).\n- `engines.node` `>=22` → `>=22.12.0` in `cli/package.json` and the lockfile root, so an install on Node 22.0–22.11 is refused up front instead of failing at runtime.\n- `allowExcessArguments(true)` on the `nexus` and `nexus-sidecar` programs. Commander 13 made extra positional arguments an error; before this change `nexus doctor extra` ran doctor and `nexus trust a b` acted on `a`. Verified on both builds. A dependency bump should not change that contract, so it is kept. Tightening it would be a separate, deliberate change.\n- New `cli_excess_arguments.test.ts`: fails 2/2 without the setting, passes 2/2 with it.\n\n## Other commander changes checked\n- v14 help groups, v15 `--no-*` default: the only negative option is `--no-resume` with no positive twin, so unaffected.\n- Node 20 drop: already `>=22`.\n\n## Evidence\n- `tsc` clean, build runs, CLI reports its version through commander 15.\n- Option-handling set (precedence, scope, provider_cli, run_json_output, operator_config_startup, doctor, config, upgrade, experimental_and_readonly): 126 pass / 4 fail locally. The same 4 fail by name on a clean `main` build with commander 12 (they need the Rust core, absent on this host); CI is the arbiter for those.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Open the PR for the commander 15 upgrade"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
