{"parentUuid":"dbfcadb4-96a1-41e2-9a10-950ed6cdbb8c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5vtaZ2n7b9ajegtCVuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PR title and body still say commander 15, so I'm rewriting them to match what the branch now does and why."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":204174,"output_tokens":1486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":711,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1486,"cache_read_input_tokens":204174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":711},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch5vtaEvy7giM8tkJzYFH","requestRef":"4c0d3154-c0bd-4dba-acc3-d67cbc15f74c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"c355eaf0-ffa4-40ad-88d6-b8c2d954deb5","timestamp":"2026-11-16T03:53:25.544Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"c355eaf0-ffa4-40ad-88d6-b8c2d954deb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5vtaZ2n7b9ajegtCVuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YH2sBkdk3zKxHvTBsm8fyP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 557 --title \"chore(deps): commander 12 → 14, keep the Node.js 22 floor (supersedes #530)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSupersedes the Dependabot bump #530 (commander 12 → 15). It targets commander 14 instead, so the supported Node.js floor stays 22.\n\n## Why not 15\nCommander 15 requires Node ≥22.12.0, and CI on the first version of this PR proved what that costs: `node_floor.test.ts` enforces that `package.json` engines, `doctor`, the upgrade preflight and `install.sh` state the same **major-only** floor (22), and the frozen v1.0.0 spec text asserts `\">=22\"`. Raising it to a minor means reworking the installer's version parsing, two source files, several tests and spec wording, in release-critical code, for no functional gain: Nexus only `import`s commander, so the `require(esm)` support behind that engines figure is not used.\n\nCommander 14 supports Node ≥20 and is the maintainer-supported line until May 2027. Node 22 itself reaches end of life around April 2027, which is the natural point to raise the floor deliberately and take 15.\n\n## What changes\n- `commander` 12.1.0 → 14.0.3 (`engines.node` stays `>=22` in `cli/package.json` and the lockfile root).\n- `allowExcessArguments(true)` on the `nexus` and `nexus-sidecar` programs. Commander 13 made extra positional arguments an error; before this change `nexus doctor extra` ran doctor and `nexus trust a b` acted on `a`, verified on both builds. A dependency bump should not change that contract, so it is kept. Tightening it would be a separate, deliberate change.\n- New `cli_excess_arguments.test.ts`: fails 2/2 without the setting, passes 2/2 with it (re-verified on commander 14).\n\n## Other commander changes checked\n- v14 help groups and v15 `--no-*` default: the only negative option is `--no-resume` with no positive twin, so unaffected.\n\n## Evidence\n- `tsc` clean, build runs. Local: `node_floor`, `cli_excess_arguments` and the option-handling files give 42 pass / 1 fail; the one failure (`--read-only given before the subcommand…`) also fails on a clean `main` build because it needs the Rust core, absent on this host. The earlier CI run on the commander 15 version had exactly one failing test across 3,892 on Node 22, `node_floor`, which is what this revision resolves.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr view 557 --json title,headRefOid -q '.title+\" @ \"+.headRefOid[0:8]'","description":"Rewrite the PR title and body to describe the commander 14 change"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":204174,"output_tokens":1486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":711,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1486,"cache_read_input_tokens":204174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":711},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":6040,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YH2sBkdk3zKxHvTBsm8fyP":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr edit 557 --title \"chore(deps): commander 12 → 14, keep the Node.js 22 floor (supersedes #530)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSupersedes the Dependabot bump #530 (commander 12 → 15). It targets commander 14 instead, so the supported Node.js floor stays 22.\n\n## Why not 15\nCommander 15 requires Node ≥22.12.0, and CI on the first version of this PR proved what that costs: `node_floor.test.ts` enforces that `package.json` engines, `doctor`, the upgrade preflight and `install.sh` state the same **major-only** floor (22), and the frozen v1.0.0 spec text asserts `\">=22\"`. Raising it to a minor means reworking the installer's version parsing, two source files, several tests and spec wording, in release-critical code, for no functional gain: Nexus only `import`s commander, so the `require(esm)` support behind that engines figure is not used.\n\nCommander 14 supports Node ≥20 and is the maintainer-supported line until May 2027. Node 22 itself reaches end of life around April 2027, which is the natural point to raise the floor deliberately and take 15.\n\n## What changes\n- `commander` 12.1.0 → 14.0.3 (`engines.node` stays `>=22` in `cli/package.json` and the lockfile root).\n- `allowExcessArguments(true)` on the `nexus` and `nexus-sidecar` programs. Commander 13 made extra positional arguments an error; before this change `nexus doctor extra` ran doctor and `nexus trust a b` acted on `a`, verified on both builds. A dependency bump should not change that contract, so it is kept. Tightening it would be a separate, deliberate change.\n- New `cli_excess_arguments.test.ts`: fails 2/2 without the setting, passes 2/2 with it (re-verified on commander 14).\n\n## Other commander changes checked\n- v14 help groups and v15 `--no-*` default: the only negative option is `--no-resume` with no positive twin, so unaffected.\n\n## Evidence\n- `tsc` clean, build runs. Local: `node_floor`, `cli_excess_arguments` and the option-handling files give 42 pass / 1 fail; the one failure (`--read-only given before the subcommand…`) also fails on a clean `main` build because it needs the Rust core, absent on this host. The earlier CI run on the commander 15 version had exactly one failing test across 3,892 on Node 22, `node_floor`, which is what this