{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","hash":"6a9d9e44035e2a9f891242ab9588ced51bd7169269e984e4426cd02a55bd7bc4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PR title and body still say commander 15, so I'm rewriting them to match what the branch now does and why."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YH2sBkdk3zKxHvTBsm8fyP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr edit 557 --title \"chore(deps): commander 12 → 14, keep the Node.js 22 floor (supersedes #530)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSupersedes the Dependabot bump #530 (commander 12 → 15). It targets commander 14 instead, so the supported Node.js floor stays 22.\n\n## Why not 15\nCommander 15 requires Node ≥22.12.0, and CI on the first version of this PR proved what that costs: `node_floor.test.ts` enforces that `package.json` engines, `doctor`, the upgrade preflight and `install.sh` state the same **major-only** floor (22), and the frozen v1.0.0 spec text asserts `\">=22\"`. Raising it to a minor means reworking the installer's version parsing, two source files, several tests and spec wording, in release-critical code, for no functional gain: Nexus only `import`s commander, so the `require(esm)` support behind that engines figure is not used.\n\nCommander 14 supports Node ≥20 and is the maintainer-supported line until May 2027. Node 22 itself reaches end of life around April 2027, which is the natural point to raise the floor deliberately and take 15.\n\n## What changes\n- `commander` 12.1.0 → 14.0.3 (`engines.node` stays `>=22` in `cli/package.json` and the lockfile root).\n- `allowExcessArguments(true)` on the `nexus` and `nexus-sidecar` programs. Commander 13 made extra positional arguments an error; before this change `nexus doctor extra` ran doctor and `nexus trust a b` acted on `a`, verified on both builds. A dependency bump should not change that contract, so it is kept. Tightening it would be a separate, deliberate change.\n- New `cli_excess_arguments.test.ts`: fails 2/2 without the setting, passes 2/2 with it (re-verified on commander 14).\n\n## Other commander changes checked\n- v14 help groups and v15 `--no-*` default: the only negative option is `--no-resume` with no positive twin, so unaffected.\n\n## Evidence\n- `tsc` clean, build runs. Local: `node_floor`, `cli_excess_arguments` and the option-handling files give 42 pass / 1 fail; the one failure (`--read-only given before the subcommand…`) also fails on a clean `main` build because it needs the Rust core, absent on this host. The earlier CI run on the commander 15 version had exactly one failing test across 3,892 on Node 22, `node_floor`, which is what this revision resolves.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr view 557 --json title,headRefOid -q '.title+\" @ \"+.headRefOid[0:8]'","description":"Rewrite the PR title and body to describe the commander 14 change"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DfCPtAZR4mzC6bzwY68oBp","name":"Monitor","input":{"command":"declare -A d; while true; do all=1; for n in 557 535 536; do [ -n \"${d[$n]}\" ] && continue; all=0; out=$(gh pr checks $n 2>&1 | grep -v -E '^Entire Gates|^package'); p=$(echo \"$out\" | grep -c -E '\\spending\\s'); f=$(echo \"$out\" | grep -c -E '\\sfail\\s'); h=$(gh pr view $n --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid | cut -c1-8); if [ \"$n\" = 557 ] && [ \"$h\" != e85e8e39 ]; then continue; fi; [ \"$p\" = 0 ] && [ -n \"$out\" ] && { echo \"#$n head=$h checks finished: fail=$f\"; d[$n]=1; }; done; [ \"$all\" = 1 ] && break; sleep 120; done","description":"PRs 557 (new head e85e8e39), 535 and 536 checks finishing","timeout_ms":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","id":"3926dd7e-ed37-4799-ae63-9b78db7276bd","timestamp":"2026-11-16T03:53:36.621Z","version":"2.1.323","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"02245c82d4cb86350db44b7c9960d5f359fa3c3746ce766c103fc6f328b1a703","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"4c0d3154-c0bd-4dba-acc3-d67cbc15f74c","keep":292,"tail":["6a9d9e44035e2a9f891242ab9588ced51bd7169269e984e4426cd02a55bd7bc4","4f850b3d9e8587eca67a0e0e9652c43432b22352354f59833b65a9c1ea963d0f","d04cc38be9eb2fb2deb58e608aa9f1ac52d1a7c059ebdd18120aff527224bfa1"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",294,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"a5f0c97712fcfc2b9c6ae4ff6b5ad8435b531de5c9c3f63ca72a0c2b17e8cf75"}
{"parentUuid":"7b3a6497-940b-4eb7-97cb-92c0e4cc7f55","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01YH2sBkdk3zKxHvTBsm8fyP","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7e52b6d5-c9e1-457c-9ad7-647a276a3110","timestamp":"2026-11-16T03:53:41.741Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"7e52b6d5-c9e1-457c-9ad7-647a276a3110","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch5vuV1SUqVB2dFGG9dhS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI on #557 failed on its first version, and I've changed the PR as a result.\n\n**What CI caught:** one test out of 3,892 on Node 22, `node_floor.test.ts`. The repo enforces that `package.json` engines, `doctor`, the upgrade preflight and `install.sh` all state the same major-only Node floor of 22. My engines bump to `>=22.12.0` broke that. My local run couldn't have shown it, because the timed-out full run never reached that test.\n\n**The change:** #557 now takes commander **14.0.3** (`engines` stays `>=22`) in place of 15.\n- Commander 15 would mean reworking the installer's version parsing, two source files, several tests and frozen spec text, in release-critical code, for no functional gain.\n- Commander 14 is maintainer-supported until May 2027, and its own Node requirement is `>=20`.\n- Node 22 reaches end of life around April 2027, which is the natural moment to raise the floor deliberately and take 15.\n- The `allowExcessArguments(true)` line and its test are unchanged. The test fails 2 of 2 without the line and passes 2 of 2 with it on commander 14.\n\n**A correction to what I said earlier:** I claimed Node 22.0–22.11 users would hit a broken install. I hadn't verified that, and it is probably wrong for an ESM import like ours. The `22.12` figure exists for `require(esm)`, which we don't use. The floor invariant is the real reason for the switch.\n\n**Next:**\n- The watch (`ba0qb7qfl`) covers #557 at its new head `e85e8e39` and the two `cf` PRs, #535 and #536.\n- I merge #557 only after its checks pass at that head. Then I close #530 with a link and `@dependabot ignore this major version`, so Dependabot doesn't reopen commander 15. That ignore is a Dependabot setting I can reverse, and I'll say so in the comment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1803,"cache_read_input_tokens":204885,"output_tokens":644,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1803,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":644,"cache_read_input_tokens":204885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1803},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch5vuUbdHyq1eRNWUo13y","requestRef":"3926dd7e-ed37-4799-ae63-9b78db7276bd","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"7bf196d7-0dd5-4551-8c00-3f3a7b8ca0b6","timestamp":"2026-11-16T03:53:41.738Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
