{"parentUuid":"ab272e2a-7860-4d83-9fb8-eee1215f7e20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6D6agBCuSmnSFbWehqL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 37 tests pass on Node 24, including the 13 layout tests, and CI covers Node 22. I'm committing this test-only change and opening the PR.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":279025,"output_tokens":1291,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":246},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1291,"cache_read_input_tokens":279025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch6D6aN4bHwRLbHS3Yj6o","requestRef":"bab722ee-f028-48cb-8e67-45f9db46108d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9ba828d7-63c8-4a80-b326-6ddc03f8b4e3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:26:00.060Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"9ba828d7-63c8-4a80-b326-6ddc03f8b4e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6D6agBCuSmnSFbWehqL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JqgmQAdGvHhp8vkwTnNJfK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/codeql-fix && git add cli/test/code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest: pass path lists to the overlay build script as argv, not spliced into code\n\nCodeQL js/bad-code-sanitization (alerts 56, 57) flags code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts:228, where two\nJSON.stringify results were interpolated into a `node -e` script. The values were fixed literals in\nthe test, so nothing attacker-controlled reached it, but string-built code is the fragile pattern.\nThe script is now static and reads both lists from process.argv. Behaviour verified for the pass\ncase and both fail cases; the 37 tests in the file pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q -u origin v1/codeql-code-sanitization 2>&1 | tail -1; cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr create --base main --head v1/codeql-code-sanitization --title \"test: pass overlay build script paths as argv (CodeQL js/bad-code-sanitization)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nResolves the two open code-scanning alerts, #56 and #57 (`js/bad-code-sanitization`, medium), both at `cli/test/code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts:228`.\n\n## What it was\nTwo `JSON.stringify(...)` results were interpolated into a JavaScript string passed to `node -e`. The values (`pinned`, `carried`) are fixed literals in the test, so no attacker-controlled data reached it: a false positive in practice. Building code by string splicing is still the fragile pattern CodeQL is right to dislike, so this fixes it instead of dismissing the alerts.\n\n## Change\nThe script is now static. It reads both lists from `process.argv` (`node -e <script> <pinned> <carried>`) and `JSON.parse`s them. Test-only, no behaviour change.\n\n## Evidence\n- The script was checked directly in its three cases: exit 0 when the pinned files are unchanged and the carried ones changed; exit 1 when a pinned file is changed; exit 1 when a carried file is not changed.\n- `code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts`: 37 of 37 pass locally on Node 24 with the isolated-HOME runner, including the 13 workspace-layout tests that use this script.\n- Left alone: three sibling tests in the same file build their scripts the same way (lines 122, 197, 250). CodeQL does not flag them, so I kept this change to what the alerts name.\n\nThe alerts close when CodeQL re-analyses `main` after the merge; I will confirm that.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit the fix, push the branch and open the PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":279025,"output_tokens":1291,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":246},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1291,"cache_read_input_tokens":279025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":5163,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JqgmQAdGvHhp8vkwTnNJfK":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/codeql-fix && git add cli/test/code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest: pass path lists to the overlay build script as argv, not spliced into code\n\nCodeQL js/bad-code-sanitization (alerts 56, 57) flags code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts:228, where two\nJSON.stringify results were interpolated into a `node -e` script. The values were fixed literals in\nthe test, so nothing attacker-controlled reached it, but string-built code is the fragile pattern.\nThe script is now static and reads both lists from process.argv. Behaviour verified for the pass\ncase and both fail cases; the 37 tests in the file pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q -u origin v1/codeql-code-sanitization 2>&1 | tail -1; cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr create --base main --head v1/codeql-code-sanitization --title \"test: pass overlay build script paths as argv (CodeQL js/bad-code-sanitization)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nResolves the two open code-scanning alerts, #56 and #57 (`js/bad-code-sanitization`, medium), both at `cli/test/code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts:228`.\n\n## What it was\nTwo `JSON.stringify(...)` results were interpolated into a JavaScript string passed to `node -e`. The values (`pinned`, `carried`) are fixed literals in the test, so no attacker-controlled data reached it: a false positive in practice. Building code by string splicing is still the fragile pattern CodeQL is right to dislike, so this fixes it instead of dismissing the alerts.\n\n## Change\nThe script is now static. It reads both lists from `process.argv` (`node -e <script> <pinned> <carried>`) and `JSON.parse`s them. Test-only, no behaviour change.\n\n## Evidence\n- The script was checked directly in its three cases: exit 0 when the pinned files are unchanged and the carried ones changed; exit 1 when a pinned file is changed; exit 1 when a carried file is not changed.\n- `code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts`: 37 of 37 pass locally on Node 24 with the isolated-HOME runner, including the 13 workspace-layout tests that use this script.\n- Left alone: three sibling tests in the same file build their scripts the same way (lines 122, 197, 250). CodeQL does not flag them, so I kept this change to what the alerts name.\n\nThe alerts close when CodeQL re-analyses `main` after the merge; I will confirm that.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit the fix, push the branch and open the PR"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch6D6aN4bHwRLbHS3Yj6o","requestRef":"bab722ee-f028-48cb-8e67-45f9db46108d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd1bdfbf-8475-44de-8f8d-8dce98b950e6","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:26:05.242Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
